Samdech Techo Hun Sen Tells the Vice President of the European Commission that Cambodia cannot trade its national sovereignty for any aid or favor
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to stand firm in defending Cambodia's sovereignty, emphasizing that he does not trade national sovereignty for any aid or favor.
The reaffirmation of the firm stance of defending national sovereignty was made during the Prime Minister's meeting with Mr. Joseph Borrell Fontaine, Senior Representative for Foreign Affairs and Political Security and Vice President of the European Commission. On August 4, 2022.
Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, said that during the meeting, the Vice President of the European Commission reminded about the removal of the EBA from Cambodia, highlighting a number of reasons for the EU to withdraw.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, in response to what the Vice President of the European Commission said, Samdech Techo Prime Minister did not have much response, he just briefly stated that Cambodia can not trade its national sovereignty for any aid or favor. One from abroad.
In 2020, the European Union decided to remove about 20 percent of Cambodia's preferential tariffs. The removal of the preferential tariff means that about 40 items of Cambodian goods are required to pay tax on imports to European countries. Most of the goods are clothing, footwear and travel products exported to Europe worth 1 billion euros every year.
However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the European Subcommittee continue to demonstrate the continued strengthening of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and the European Union. The Prime Minister praised the fruitful results of the 11th Joint Commission Meeting of Cambodia and the European Union held in March 2022. The meeting contributed to strengthening relations and cooperation between the two sides.
Samdech Techo also thanked the European Union for providing cooperative assistance to Cambodia since 1992, which has contributed significantly to the development of Cambodia, and highly appreciated the European Union for providing vaccine assistance through the CAVAC mechanism and financing. In the past, which has contributed to the success of Cambodia in the campaign to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and the socio-economic recovery of Cambodia.
In addition to the above issues, in this meeting, Mr. Joseph Borrell Funteles informed the Prime Minister about the trip to Siem Reap and walked 16 hours to see the magnificent temples of Cambodia, which highlight not only the artistic but Even the architecture. He added that the temples in Cambodia are the great wealth of mankind.
He also thanked the European Union for its support to Cambodia during its chairmanship of the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting, which ended successfully in November 2021, and thanked the European Union for its support. To Cambodia as the chair of ASEAN in 2022 and the role of special envoy of the ASEAN chair in 2022 on Myanmar.
