Taiwan Defense Ministry website hit by cyber-attack amid tensions with China
Taiwan's Defense Ministry on Thursday said its website had been hit by a cyber-attack and was temporarily shut down amid tensions with China over the visit of US House of Representatives Speaker Nancy Pelosi in Taipei. Taiwan. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, August 4, 2022.
Earlier this week, several official websites of the Taiwanese administration, including the website of the Office of the Taiwanese Leader, Tsai Yingwen, were hacked, with some Taiwanese officials claiming to be the work of China and Russia.
Taiwan's Defense Ministry has been closely monitoring and working with experts to strengthen the IT security system as China launches large-scale military exercises.
