TOP NEWS: Cambodia issues statement on concerns over tensions in Taiwan Strait and urges stakeholders to abide by China-US agreement
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Cooperation of Cambodia on the night of August 3, 2022 issued a statement expressing deep concern over the recent escalation of tensions in the Taiwan Strait and urging all The parties concerned respect the agreements signed between the People's Republic of China and the United States, as stated in previous joint statements between the two sides.
In a statement obtained by Fresh News, the Royal Government of Cambodia affirmed that it has been closely monitoring the recent developments in the Taiwan Straits and would like to make the following statement:
The Royal Government of Cambodia expresses its deep concern over the recent escalation of tensions in the Taiwan Straits and urges all parties to respect the agreements signed between the People's Republic of China and the United States, as existing. As stated in previous joint statements between the two parties.
* The Royal Government of Cambodia has always adhered to the "one-China policy" and considered issues related to Hong Kong, Taiwan, Tibet and Xinjiang as China's internal affairs and the sovereignty of the People's Republic of China.
The Royal Government of Cambodia calls on all parties concerned to seek peaceful solutions, maintain the status quo and avoid provocation for the cause of peace, stability, progress and prosperity in the region and the world.
