This announcement was made by Mr. Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of China, during a working meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen on Wednesday afternoon, August 3, 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Wang Yi expressed their strong commitment to continue to strengthen relations and cooperation between the two countries. Wang Yi reiterated the Chinese government's position to continue to strongly support Cambodia's domestic and foreign policy and foreign policy and to strongly support Cambodia's long-term vision under the leadership of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. In particular, the protection of Cambodia's sovereignty and independence.
Mr. Wang Yi also highlighted that due to Cambodia's comprehensive strategic partnership and common destiny policy, Cambodia-China relations and cooperation have remained strong despite the uncertainties and sharp developments. Regional and global situation.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed China's support for Cambodia's policies, both domestic and foreign. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia is ready to ensure that the relations between Cambodia and China continue to be strong with the leadership of the successor without change.
Regarding the Cambodian successor leader, Mr. Wang Yi announced that China will continue to strongly support the successor leader from the Cambodian People's Party, which is an important key for Cambodia and for Cambodia-China friendship.
According to Kao Kim Hourn, Wang Yi not only announced his continued support for Cambodia's successor, but also expressed his appreciation for Dr. Hun Manet's leadership.
It should be noted that Dr. HUN Manet, a permanent member of the Cambodian People's Party, was voted by the Central Committee members as a candidate for the future Prime Minister on December 24, 2021.
Mr. Hun Manet is the eldest son of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. Manet was born during the Democratic Kampuchea regime, a brutal killing field regime ruled by Pol Pot and his cronies. When he was about five months pregnant, his father, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, fled to Vietnam in search of national liberation from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot on June 20, 1977. .
After reuniting with his family, Mr. Hun Manet received the most care and attention from his father and mother. He was also highly regarded by his father for his education until he became an outstanding student. Mr. Hun Manet became the No. 1 outstanding student in mathematics in the country in the 1992-1993 academic year from Phnom Daun Penh High School.
After graduating from Phnom Penh in the early 1990s, Hun Manet was sent by his father, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to study in the United States at the age of 16.
Living in the United States was a time when Hun Manet disciplined himself and took control of his life away from his parents, no longer having the same strict responsibilities as when living in the country. Despite living without the direct supervision of his parents, Mr. Hun Manet is a Cambodian with a high level of character and a love for education and has worked hard to study until he graduated from prestigious American schools such as the military academy. West Point and so on.
Not only is he a graduate of an internationally renowned school, Mr. Hun Manet is also an intellectual who has been involved in practical work for many years in both the Party, the military and the humanitarian framework. In particular, Mr. Hun Manet is an intellectual trained and experienced by another strong professor, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, his father.
Through his father's work experience and personal training, Hun Manet is seen as a worthy and strong successor in Cambodia who can ensure peace and stability. Bring continuous progress and prestige for Cambodia.
Speaking to the media after the meeting on the afternoon of August 3, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, emphasized that in the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Mr. Wang Yi discussed a lot on bilateral relations and cooperation. Parties as well as regional and global issues.
On the issue of bilateral relations and cooperation between Cambodia and China, the Prime Minister expressed his pleasure to meet with Mr. Wang Yi again after missing a meeting for a while due to the outbreak of Kovid 19. Samdech Techo highlighted that the relationship between Cambodia and China has laid a solid foundation and deepened cooperation in many fields.
Mr. Wang Yi addressed the Prime Minister, who allowed him and the delegation to meet to discuss work. Wang Yi also conveyed greetings from the President, Prime Minister and Chinese leaders to Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Mr. Wang Yi also wished Samdech Techo Hun Sen for his 70th birthday on August 5.
Mr. Wang Yi said that the Prime Minister used his life to help build Cambodia, restore the country from the war and build a better life for the people. In particular, that has enhanced Cambodia's role in the region and the world.
During the meeting, Wang Yi also highlighted the Chinese government's position on Cambodia. In that, China continues to strongly support Cambodia's domestic policy and foreign policy line. Chinese State Councilor Wang Yi congratulated the CPP on the results of the commune council elections, which reflected the correct leadership of Samdech Techo.
China will continue to strongly support Cambodia's long-term vision under the leadership of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. In particular, the protection of Cambodia's sovereignty and independence. China will continue to strongly support the successor leaders from the Cambodian People's Party, which is the key for Cambodia and for Cambodia-China friendship.
Wang Yi pointed out that due to Cambodia's comprehensive strategic partnership and common destiny policy, Cambodia-China relations and cooperation have remained strong despite the uncertainties and sharp developments in the regional situation. And the world as well.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Mr. Wang Yi for bringing greetings and greetings to Samdech from the Chinese leadership, as well as direct wishes from Mr. Wang Yi.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed China's support for Cambodia's policies, both domestic and foreign. Samdech Techo further stated that Cambodia has already made arrangements to ensure that the Cambodian-Chinese relations continue to be strong with the leadership of the successor without any change.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that Cambodia and China continue to cooperate in all areas that the country already has, including politics, economy and other areas.
Samdech Techo also congratulated the outcome of the recent Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Meeting held as a contribution to boosting cooperation between the two countries.
The Prime Minister also thanked China for its contribution to demining in Cambodia, which Cambodia has set to become a landmine-free and unexploded ordnance country by 2030. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked China to continue to support the policy of clearing mines and unexploded ordnance.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also requested the Chinese government to continue to support Cambodia's sustainable development goals to make Cambodia successful.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted the many benefits of Chinese investment in Cambodia, as well as Chinese assistance for development such as infrastructure construction.
The Prime Minister also thanked China for helping Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19, making Cambodia successful in the fight against Kovid 19. In particular, the massive supply of vaccines from China, which is a strong reference. This success has put Cambodia at the top of the assessment list of the country after the 19 Kovid crisis by the Japanese company Nike.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also emphasized that despite Cambodia's success, the fight against Kovid 19 is still a priority for Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that cooperation on public health care is still important, especially to make Cambodia able to produce vaccines.
Samdech Techo emphasized that due to the vaccination, Cambodia has fully reopened its economy. The reopening of full economic activity has made Cambodia more able to export and also increased its revenue.
Samdech Techo stressed that vaccines are the lifeblood of Cambodia's economy. Samdech Techo highlighted that as a strategy going forward, in 2024 and 2025, Cambodia is ready to buy an additional 100 million doses of vaccine to ensure that Cambodia avoids the outbreak of Kovid 19.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his desire to see the growth of trade between Cambodia and China even higher, although now achieved high. Samdech wants the trade volume between the two countries to reach 15 billion US dollars, while last year reached about 11 billion US dollars.
Samdech Techo saw that this trade volume could be achieved because Cambodia and China have a free trade agreement, the ASEAN-China Free Trade Agreement and the RCEP Comprehensive Partnership Agreement.
In relation to this comprehensive RCEP partnership, Samdech Techo Hun Sen recalled his request at the opening of the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting to establish the RCEP Secretariat in Phnom Penh. In this regard, Samdech Techo asked China to support this proposal because China is a member of this agreement as well.
Through Wang Yi, Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the Chinese government to continue to help Cambodia, especially to open bigger markets for Cambodian agricultural products. Samdech Techo also asked China to continue to increase investment in Cambodia and increase flights between the two countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked China to continue to help develop the energy sector in Cambodia, which is an important sector to support the economy in the aftermath of the Russia-Ukraine war.
During the meeting, Wang Yi also highlighted Cambodia's important role in chairing ASEAN this year.
Wang Yi stated that China will continue to strongly support Cambodia's economic recovery and development. Wang Yi also thanked Samdech Techo for his continued strong support for the one-China policy.
Wang Yi also promised to encourage investment in Cambodia and encourage the business community to continue investing in Cambodia. As for the vaccine, Wang Yi promised to provide it to Cambodia whenever needed.
Regarding agriculture, Wang Yi also promised to import more from Cambodia because China has a large market. Involved in the energy sector, the Chinese side will look into this case and will study together to promote in the energy sector as well.
The talks between Samdech Techo and HE Wang Yi are in-depth to expand bilateral relations, especially in the areas of economy, investment, tourism and development.
Finally, Mr. Wang Yi said that as the President of ASEAN this year, there are many challenges, as he said that this is not a hot pot, but a hot stone that is added little by little. However, Samdech turned the hot stone into gold due to the talent and experience of Samdech Techo Prime Minister. Wang Yi believes that Cambodia has a great position in the world through its chairmanship of ASEAN.
He wished His Excellency President Xi Jinping and Prime Minister Li Keqiang a warm welcome and wished the 20th General Assembly of the Communist Party of China success. Russian Foreign Minister arrives in Cambodia for ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting
