UAE expresses desire to increase investment in Cambodia, especially in agriculture
(Phnom Penh): On August 3, 2022, Dr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Mission, met with Mr. Abdulnasser Al Shaali, Deputy Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of the United Arab Emirates on the occasion of his visit. Participated in the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings in Phnom Penh.
The meeting was held to strengthen cooperation between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates, which was held at the office of Senior Minister Osman Hassan in Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Dr. Osman Hassan thanked the United Arab Emirates for its good cooperation with Cambodia, as well as for providing humanitarian assistance, building schools, hospitals, mosques and providing scholarships to Cambodian students. The great enthusiasm of the United Arab Emirates to participate in the development of Cambodia.
He also thanked the United Arab Emirates for supporting Cambodia to become a member of the Organization of Islamic Cooperation (OIC). As the Special Envoy of the Organization of the Islamic Conference (OIC) in Cambodia, he also requested the United Arab Emirates to continue to facilitate Cambodia to become a member of this organization as soon as possible.
In addition, Dr. Osman Hassan also requested the United Arab Emirates to invest in Cambodia, especially in the field of agriculture, because Cambodia is a country rich in raw materials, and especially the Royal Government of Cambodia always welcomes foreign investment in Cambodia. Moreover, Cambodia is a fast developing country, these are great opportunities to invest and get high returns.
In response, Abdulnasser Al Shaali also expressed his pleasure at the good cooperation between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates, especially Cambodia has played an important role in resolving the food security crisis in the United Arab Emirates. He said the UAE intends to increase investment with Cambodia in exporting Cambodian rice and agricultural crops to his country's markets as well as international markets.
Please be reminded that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has emphasized that Cambodia wants to have relations with OIC member countries that will be able to contribute to the socio-economic development of Cambodia, and Cambodia wants all those countries to contribute to Cambodia. Training human resources through the provision of scholarships for the training of Muslim students.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, has been appointed as the Secretary-General of ASEAN from 2023. This was confirmed by Mr. Kong Phok, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and the official spokesperson for the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings.
Speaking at a press conference on the evening of August 3, 2022, the official spokesman of the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings said: "Announcing the appointment of His Excellency Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, as Secretary-General of ASEAN, which will begin in 2023."
He confirmed that Cambodia's current appointment was also welcomed by the ASEAN Foreign Ministers.
According to Article 11 of the ASEAN Charter, the ASEAN Secretary-General will be formally appointed by the ASEAN Summit for a five-year term, which can no longer be extended, and shall be selected from among the nationals of the ASEAN Member States. Based on the alphabetical rotation of the names of member states, careful consideration of integrity, competence, professional experience and gender equality.
