Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, told reporters after the meeting that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Qatari Foreign Minister had discussed issues focusing on relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Qatar.
According to Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, both Samdech Techo and the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Qatar have seen the improvement of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and Qatar. However, there are still many potential sectors that Cambodia and Qatar should pay more attention to, especially in the economic field.
In terms of the economy, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted the high potential for investment in Cambodia, especially food production. In this regard, Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants Qatar to look for investment opportunities in Cambodia, focusing on the processing of agricultural products. Especially processing rice for export because Cambodia has a lot of rice left.
Regarding investment and business, the Qatari Foreign Minister confirmed that he would urge business delegations to come to Cambodia to discuss with Cambodian business to expand this business sector. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also encouraged the private sector of the two countries to work together.
The Qatari Foreign Minister saw that Cambodia still has a lot of potential for investment and he believed in growth opportunities for investment in Cambodia.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Qatar also discussed tourism. Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants Qatar to launch direct flights to Cambodia. The request was made by the Qatari Foreign Minister, who indicated that he would submit the proposal to the airline for review.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also expressed his congratulations and wished Qatar success for the organization of the World Cup at the end of this year. Qatar Foreign Minister invites Samdech Techo Hun Sen to visit and watch football match in Qatar
The Qatari Foreign Minister also informed Samdech Techo Hun Sen that during the tournament, the weather in Qatar was hot but not a problem due to the air conditioning in the stadium.
