Nearly 10,000 duty-free right-hand drive vehicles in the country have registered to pay taxes by the end of July.
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia said that as of the deadline of July 31, 2022, more than 9,800 existing duty-free right-hand drive vehicles in Cambodia have been registered. And pay taxes after the head of government allows those right-hand drive vehicles to pay taxes without having to adjust the steering wheel.
Mr. Pha Eng Veng, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, said that in the past, the Royal Government has instructed the owners of existing duty-free right-hand drive vehicles in Cambodia to register and declare their right to occupy. July 31, 2022 for the General Department of Customs to identify existing duty-free right-hand drive vehicles in Cambodia, otherwise the vehicles that have not been declared will be considered as new imported vehicles.
He said that by July 31, 2022, the deadline for the deadline, nearly 10,000 vehicles had come to declare and register, of which more than 3,000 had already completed their tax obligations and more than 6,000 remained. Units that have not yet been taxed.
He stated that for more than 6,000 steering vehicles that have not been able to pay this tax, the General Department of Customs and Excise will leave time until October 8, 2022.
Please be reminded that on July 6, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, allowed the existing duty-free right-hand drive vehicles in the country to enter the tax without having to change the steering wheel from right to left, but Right-hand drive imports to Cambodia will no longer be allowed from July 6, 2022.
Following the announcement, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia called on all right-hand drive car owners to register and declare ownership rights as existing vehicles in the country, even though no tax results have yet been paid. Have the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia record the exact number, otherwise, when the Customs and Excise authorities start cracking down, it will be considered as a new car imported after July 6, 2022.
At the same time, the General Department of Customs and the Government of Cambodia have announced that they will take strict measures at the border checkpoints, especially at the Cambodian-Thai border, to prevent the fraudulent import of new right-hand drive vehicles from Thailand to Cambodia. . Samdech Techo Hun Sen Meets Qatar Foreign Minister
