WASHINGTON, Aug. 2 (Xinhua) - Nancy Pelosi arrived safely in Taiwan on Tuesday. Through the visit, it made the 82-year-old Pelosi the first speaker of the US House of Representatives to visit Taiwan in more than 25 years.
As tensions are rising to unprecedented levels in decades, here are the key developments in the development of US-China-Taiwan relations:
1950 - Taiwan becomes an ally of the United States, which is at war with China in the Korean War. The United States deployed a navy to the Taiwan Strait to protect Taipei from any Chinese attacks at the time.
From 1954 to 1955: The first Taiwan Strait crisis erupted. Beijing has fired artillery on some Taiwan-controlled islands southeast of the Chinese coast. In the crisis, Taiwan lost control of some islands and sent the remaining troops and people to Taiwan.
1979 - The United States agrees to a "one-size-fits-all" policy, severing diplomatic ties with Taiwan and turning to ties with China. Under the leadership of Chinese leader Teng Xiaoping, China launched a "one country, two systems" political system and peaceful reunification with Taiwan.
1996 - Third Taiwan Strait Crisis: At that time, Taiwan held its first direct presidential election. Beijing has fired missiles into waters near Taiwan, and the United States has sent aircraft carriers to the area. In this election, Mr. Ly Teng Huy won a landslide victory in March 1996.
2005 - China enacts anti-secession law in March, declaring any Taiwan declaration of independence or secession illegal. In April of the same year, opposition leaders Kuomintang and the Chinese Communist Party met for the first time since 1949.
December 2016 - US President-elect Donald Trump holds a live telephone conversation with Tsai Ing-win.
2017 - The Donald Trump administration approves $ 1.4 billion arms sales to Taiwan.
March 2018 - Donald Trump signs a law encouraging the United States to send senior officials to visit Taiwan.
September 2018: US State Department approves $ 330 million sale of spare parts for F-16 fighter jets to Taiwan and other military aircraft.
July 2022: Zhou Biden and Xi Jinping hold a telephone conversation for more than two hours. Biden stressed that the United States has not changed its policy toward China, but strongly opposes any attempt to change the status quo in the Taiwan Straits unilaterally and by force.
August 3: Ms. Pelosi pays an official visit to Taiwan, meeting with key Taiwanese leaders, including Taiwanese leader Tsai Ying-wen. China has called Ms. Pelosi's visit to Taiwan "provocative" and has declared a military siege of Taiwan from August 4 to 7.
Taiwan will relentlessly defend its security and retaliate against any actions that violate the island's sovereignty, and tighten alert levels under the principle of non-aggression, the Defense Ministry said. Explosion.
Taiwan's Defense Ministry also added that China is waging a psychological war against Taiwan and has urged people not to believe rumors and report false information to the authorities.
On Tuesday night, US House Speaker Nancy Pelosi arrived in Taiwan without fear of a Chinese warning. Her actions angered Beijing and called for military exercises near and around Taiwan this week.
