He said that WCS Cambodia, in collaboration with the Ministry of Environment and local communities, is committed to strengthening strategic methods and resources to combat illegal animal trapping in the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary in Mondulkiri Province.
According to the first quarterly report of the National Bank of Cambodia, in line with the growing demand and advancement of financial technology, electronic payment systems continue to be developed and modernized, which strengthens payments more efficiently, securely and cost-effectively. Appropriate.
At the same time, the national clearing system, the fast payment system and the Cambodian Swiss system are being updated to add some essential functions, and the Bakong system is being developed to facilitate interbank payments, especially in Financial markets.
The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) confirmed that electronic payment transactions continued to increase, such as the transfer of funds in riel through the retaliatory system, which almost doubled, and payments through the Bakong system increased to 18.5 trillion riel, or about 4 $ 5 billion with a total of 8.1 million transactions.
He also said that ACLI Bank may be selected by the National Bank of Cambodia as a payment agent with the two countries as it has successfully settled with Thailand.
"We already have the system, we have the experience, we are ready and waiting for our National Bank and the central banks of other ASEAN countries to work together and choose which bank we will follow, but the payment is comprehensive," he added. Of course, not just one bank, because the National Bank of Cambodia has a system that allows a wide range of payments to all banks.
As for the payment from Cambodia to Thailand, Mr. In Channy confirmed that it is working well, while the payment from Thailand to Cambodia, the central banks of the two countries are working together to make the payment from Thailand to Cambodia by the end of 2022, which will Make payments between the two countries more comprehensive.
Please be informed that currently, 37 banking and financial institutions as members of Bakong have participated in the development of KHQR function, of which 29 banking and financial institutions have successfully operated with KHOR and launched and settled goods with business partners throughout Country.
According to the report of the National Bank of Cambodia in the first half of 2022, the banking sector continues to maintain resilience and contribute to the recovery of economic activity. Assets of banking and financial institutions increased by 17.2%, loans to major sectors increased by 23.4% and customer deposits increased by 16%, indicating public trust in the banking system. Currently, the number of customer deposit accounts has increased to 13.2 million and credit accounts to 3.5 million.
