ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights (ICHA) issues a press release on the outcome of the first special meeting
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Human Rights Committee, in its capacity as Chairman of the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights (ICHA) 2022, has issued a press release on the outcome of the first special meeting of the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights. Icha). This is according to the press release received by Fresh News on August 3, 2022.
The first special meeting of Icha from July 30 to August 2, 2022 in Phnom Penh, chaired by Mr. Keo Remy, Cambodian Representative to Aicha and attended by Deputy Representative of Aicha of ASEAN All as well as the ASEAN Secretariat. The special meeting discussed the finalization and approval of the ICHA 2022 Annual Report and the ICHA President's Statement to the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting.
The meeting also agreed to refer the recommendations of the Regional Dialogue: Self-Assessment of Aisha's 10-Year Progress to the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting. AISA 2023 Agenda / Priorities is also finalized for submission to the ASEAN Standing Committee (CPR) and submitted to the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting for approval.
Progress of Aisha's programs and priority activities were also discussed, including children's rights, human rights and the environment, human trafficking, business and human rights, access to clean water and sanitation, and access to education.
The meeting also discussed preparations for the 10th Anniversary of the ASEAN Human Rights Declaration (AHRD) and the Phnom Penh Statement on the adoption of the AHRD, the ASEAN Human Rights Dialogue and the 4th ASEAN-EU Human Rights Policy Dialogue. Planned this year.
On August 2, 2022, the AISA representative had a meeting with the ASEAN Foreign Ministers during the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings. The meeting provided a forum for a frank exchange of views between the ASEAN Foreign Ministers and all AIC representatives on the human rights situation in the region.
Recognizing the important role of ICHA and its essential contribution to building the ASEAN Community, the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting reaffirmed its support for ICHA in its efforts to promote and protect its rights. People. Aicha also made a statement and submitted Aicha's 2022 Annual Report to the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting at the meeting.
The 82-year-old Pelosi is the second most important person after the outgoing US vice president to arrive safely in Taiwan on Tuesday night. Became the first Speaker of the US House of Representatives to visit Taiwan in more than 25 years.
But China considers her visit a serious provocation, and North Korea, an ally of China, has also come forward to condemn it. Pyongyang strongly condemns the intervention in Taiwan, which is China's internal affair, and fully supports China, North Korea's foreign ministry spokesman was quoted as saying by North Korean state media KCNA.
"It is only right that a sovereign state take action against external forces that intrude on its internal affairs and are destroying its territorial integrity," the spokesman added. In addition to North Korea, Russia has also announced its support for China and condemned the visit.
However, the White House and Pelosi personally confirmed that her visit to Taiwan was not a change in US "one-China policy" and that the United States remained opposed to Taiwan's declaration of independence.
Prior to the opening of the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers 'Meeting and related meetings, Dr. Kong Phok, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia and the Official Spokesperson of the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting, held a conference on Agenda for today's meeting.
The 82-year-old Pelosi is the second most important person after the Vice President to succeed the presidency, and the current visit makes her the first Speaker of the US House of Representatives to visit. Taiwan for more than 25 years.
China has called Ms. Pelosi's visit to Taiwan "provocative" and has declared a military siege of Taiwan from August 4 to 7. Pelosi is expected to meet with top Taiwanese leaders, including Taiwanese leader Tsai Ying-wen.
This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Opens the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and Related Meetings
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of August 3, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of ASEAN, presided over the opening ceremony of the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings held at Sokha Hotel.
Prior to the opening ceremony of the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings, the Prime Minister welcomed the Foreign Ministers of ASEAN Member States and ASEAN dialogue partners, and Samdech Techo will also meet with the Foreign Ministers of the Member States. ASEAN as well.
In 2022, as the chair of ASEAN, Cambodia has set out the common theme of the "ASEAN Working Together: Addressing All Challenges" with high commitment to addressing the ASEAN, regional and global issues. Hot today.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings are an important forum for ASEAN as well as dialogue partners to review and discuss issues and make decisions for the ASEAN Leaders and Dialogue Partners. ASEAN Summit and related meetings at the end of the year.
On the occasion of the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting, there will be three separate tripartite meetings between Cambodia and the ASEAN Secretariat, with three ASEAN dialogue partners: Norway, Turkey and Switzerland.
According to the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, up to 38 ASEAN foreign ministers, foreign ministers and representatives of ASEAN partner countries will attend the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings in Cambodia. The foreign ministers of the world powers, including the United States, China, Russia, Japan and Australia, have already confirmed their participation in the meeting in Cambodia.
The forum for such a solemn and face-to-face meeting has been missed for two years (2020-2021) due to the Kovid 19 outbreak. The ASEAN and related meetings two years ago were held only online.
The officials in charge of the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings are each very busy and highly responsible.
Cambodia is a country that used to be eaten by the flames of war. The flames of war have left Cambodia without any capacity, not to mention the ability to hold important meetings, even to participate in forums.
On the contrary, for now, Mlup Sok Santepheap has given Cambodia the opportunity to build its full capacity, economy, human resources and its role. In fact, as of now, Cambodia has the capacity to host the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings, and Cambodia also has the ability to chair meetings to address issues and set out a vision for regional and global prosperity.
These are great honors and a source of great pride for the entire Cambodian nation. Let all Cambodians rejoice and applaud the chairmanship of ASEAN and the leadership of this important regional and global meeting and to contribute to creating a better environment to enhance the image and honor of the Cambodian nation.
