(Tbong Khmum): 752 target farmers in Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province, who lost 542 hectares of rice fields due to floods in 2022, were given more than one seed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. 56 tons to facilitate farmers to restore their livelihoods.
The handover ceremony was held at Prey Nokor Krao pagoda in Dauntey commune, Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province this morning, August 3, 2022, under the chairmanship of Mr. Vong Sandab, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Mr. Dr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province.
Please be informed that in the rainy season this year, there has been a series of heavy rains since the beginning of May, combined with the flow of water from the upper part, which has caused the paddy of some farmers who have just planted to be completely damaged by flooding. Many times, along with the effects of the Kovid 19 crisis, farmers have been severely short of rice varieties to grow when the water recedes.
