(Cambodian Natural Resource Protected Areas): Finding mushrooms in the forest increases the additional income of the communities in the protected areas. Through this, until August, the community in the Sang Ruk Vorn Wildlife Sanctuary in Oddar Meanchey province can still remove mushrooms from the forest to increase additional income for the family. Wild mushrooms are a seasonal non-timber forest product that is usually only available during the rainy season from July to August.
During the rainy season, wild mushrooms have become an important source of additional food, where local people in the natural bar area enjoy the business of removing peacock mushrooms, rattan mushrooms in the rainforest for food and the rest can be traded. .
The community in Andong Teuk village, Samrong commune, Oddar Meanchey province, who came to find mushrooms, said that the peacock mushrooms that grow in the forest are very delicious when they are used for cooking, such as frying and boiling. People can find more mushrooms, including peacock mushrooms to eat and can sell to the market per kilogram for 10,000 to 14,000 riels. A villager can harvest 3 to 5 kg of mushrooms in just 2 to 3 hours a day.
Mr. Phuong Lina, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Environment, said that during the rainy season, especially between the rainy season and the rainy season, the protected area provides beauty and growth of various wild vegetables in That has this peacock mushroom, too. Many families have come to collect peacock mushrooms in the rainforest in the Sang Ruk Vorn Wildlife Sanctuary based on the rainfall.
