(Phnom Penh): In the afternoon of August 2, 2022, the first meeting of the Advisory Council for the Development of Automotive and Electronics was held at the office of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (DAC). Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary General of the ECCC
The objectives of the meeting are: (1) to discuss and collect input related to the roles, responsibilities and functions of the Advisory Council, (2) to determine the priority measures for cooperation, and (3) to implement the implementation of development measures. Programs to improve the skills of the workforce.
The meeting was attended by representatives of relevant ministries, institutions, investors in both sectors, developers of special economic zones, technical and vocational training establishments, national and international business associations, and the Secretariat to lead and coordinate the implementation of Cambodia's industrial development policy. 2015-2025 (IDP) of the CEC A total of about 70 people.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea reminded the meeting about the background of the establishment of the Advisory Council as one of the 20 measures set out in the draft roadmap for the development of the automotive and electronics sector in Cambodia through the high note of the Samdech. Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on May 3, 2022.
The meeting vigorously discussed the long-term vision and specific orientation mechanisms, along with the specific needs and challenges of investors, in order to make the Cambodian economy more cost-effective in the operation of these sectors.
In this regard, the meeting also heard and discussed the presentation on human resource development, with the development of program development measures to improve the skills of the workforce to meet the needs in the field of automotive and electronics.
The Council agrees to hold a meeting every six months to monitor and evaluate the progress of the implementation of the proposed measures and the challenges that may be encountered during implementation.
