Minister Vong Soth Recommends 4 Points to Promote and Develop Human Resources in Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, made four important recommendations to promote and develop human resources in the field of social affairs, veterans and youth rehabilitation. This recommendation was made during the celebration of awarding professional certificates and bachelor's degrees to students of the National Institute of Social Affairs on August 2, 2022.
The four main recommendations include:
1: Continue to promote the training of human resources on a regular basis to promote quality knowledge and skills in line with the situation of the education sector and the labor market.
2: Continue to develop digital education for the training of human resources in the digital economy through the integration of digital technology to all curriculum levels.
3: Continue to strengthen and improve the quality of education and governance of the National Institute of Social Affairs through the modernization of new teaching programs, curriculum and management system.
4: Continue to improve the study environment, study resources and physical infrastructure even better.
In addition, Mr. Vong Soth also congratulated the 196 winning students, including 96 females, 10 foreign students who successfully graduated in accordance with the degree program, professional certificate and bachelor's degree. National Institute of Social Affairs.
He said that this is the third time since 2017 that he has awarded diplomas to winning students for the National Institute of Social Affairs, which considers this to be a contribution to the development of human resources in the field of social work, despite the challenges. Of the 19 outbreaks of Kovid for the past two years in order to ensure the sustainability of education and to ensure the safety of education and training in accordance with the program.
