(Phnom Penh): Meas Sok Sen San, secretary-general and spokesman for the Ministry of Economy and Finance, said that Cambodia's debt situation was "manageable" and that there was no risk or concern about the current debt. Cambodia is in the baseline ratio of only 33 to 35%.
Speaking at a press conference on "Five Years Achievement of the Ministry of Economy and Finance" at the Office of the Council of Ministers on August 2, 2022, Mr. Meas Sok Sen San outlined the current state of Cambodia's debt as of now. $ 9.81 billion, while the government has been working to repay both bilateral and multilateral creditors, with the government repaying $ 183 million in the first quarter of 2022.
He also pointed out that the Royal Government of Cambodia manages this debt very carefully and the borrowing is also done with a clear purpose, that is, this loan is used for various investments such as construction of infrastructure, etc. with transparency. And efficiency.
He added, "However, the Royal Government has conditions for borrowing, not just borrowing, and what is important is the victory of Cambodia is that we borrow, not to pay salaries, we borrow to invest. . It is important that we have five conditions for borrowing, and that the five conditions we submit to the National Assembly for approval are not arbitrary. "We have a debate in parliament to borrow this."
In the first quarter of 2012, the Royal Government paid a total of $ 183.03 million in debt service to development partners. Compared with the same period last year, debt repayments in the first quarter of 2022 increased by about 33%.
