Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, on behalf of the Prime Minister's Chief of Staff Difficulties for the affected people.
On the morning of Tuesday, August 2, 2022, Senior Minister Kun Kim continued to inspect the floodwaters that are flooding rice fields in Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province.
During the visit to understand the difficulties and impacts of farmers, there was also the participation of the Secretariat of the Disaster Management Secretariat of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, HE Governor of Kampong Thom Province, Provincial Military Operations Area Commander, District Governor and relevant officials. Ngong province.
According to the preliminary report of the Provincial Disaster Management Secretariat, Kampong Svay district was affected by floods in eight communes, equivalent to 4,425 hectares, of which 2,707 hectares were damaged, equivalent to 2,171 families.
In front of the farmers affected by the floods, Senior Minister Kun Kim brought the memories of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen to all farmers, as well as to mourn the impact of the disaster. The flood of rain.
The Senior Minister also informed the farmers about Samdech Techo's instructions to pay attention to solving the difficulties and impacts of the people from the floods.
The Senior Minister also instructed the Provincial Disaster Management Secretariat to continuously monitor and update the impact and subsequent damage in order to facilitate the provision of rice seeds for post-flood recovery. Has faded.
Although Senior Minister Kun Kim also praised the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, the competent authorities, the joint forces, implemented the plan to prevent and solve the problems caused by the floods.
The Senior Minister also made some recommendations to the Provincial Disaster Management Committee to be prepared and have timely and effective response measures to reduce the impact to a minimum.
It should be noted that on August 1, Senior Minister Kun Kim also visited to inspect the impact of floods in Baray and Taing Kork districts, Kampong Thom province.
On the afternoon of August 2, 2022, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, paid a courtesy call on Ms. Nguyen Thi Thanh, Member of the National Assembly Standing Committee and President of the Vietnam-Cambodia Friendship Association. She and the delegation paid an official visit to Cambodia.
The President of the Senate believes that the visit of the delegation to Cambodia on this occasion will contribute to deepening and enhancing the good relations between the two countries and the existing peoples of the two countries, for the greater benefit of the time. Present and future for both country and people.
On behalf of the delegation, Ms. Nguyen Thi Thanh expressed her deep gratitude to the President of the Senate for taking the time to meet with the delegation. She said that this is the first time she has visited Cambodia on behalf of the President of the Vietnam-Cambodia Friendship Association.
She praised Cambodia's rapid progress in all areas under the proper leadership of the Senate, the National Assembly and the Royal Government, and also praised Cambodia for leading the way in the management of Kovid-19 and its restoration and development. The economy is recovering rapidly.
At the same time, Ms. Nguyen Thi Thanh expressed her congratulations on the achievements that Cambodia has achieved under the leadership of the Senate, National Assembly and the Royal Government, such as the success of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Council Election and the acceptance of As the rotating chair of ASEAN and AIPA, as well as hosting the 2023 SEA Games.
Ms. Nguyen Thi Thanh emphasized that in the past 55 years since the establishment of diplomatic ties between the two countries, the two countries' governments and peoples have enjoyed good relations, friendship, solidarity and cooperation. Good neighbors, traditional friendship, cooperation in all fields and lasting "and Cambodia's success and happiness are Vietnam's success and happiness.
On behalf of the Vietnamese people, Ms. Nguyen Thi Thanh thanked the King, the Senate, the National Assembly, the Royal Government and the Cambodian people for always supporting and nurturing the traditional good relations between the two countries. Taking that opportunity, she also brought greetings from the General Secretary of the Party, the President, the Prime Minister and the President of the National Assembly to the President of the Senate.
Over the past 55 years, the two countries have gone through many difficult disciplines and united to fight the common enemy for the cause of independence, sovereignty, integrity and development. Therefore, the current leadership must continue to work hard to maintain the tradition of solidarity and friendship to be a legacy for the next generation of leaders of the two countries.
The people of the two countries are very happy to see the governments of the two countries build the border line into a border line of peace, friendship, cooperation and development. The President of the Senate encouraged the Friendship Association of the two countries to continue their efforts to deepen the relationship and cooperation between the two countries so that no one can break it.
On behalf of the Senate, the President of the Senate expressed his sincere congratulations on the great achievements of the Vietnamese government and people in their socio-economic development. He is confident that under the proper leadership of the Vietnamese government and parliament, Vietnam will continue to achieve greater socio-economic achievements in implementing the decisions of the 13th General Assembly of the Communist Party of Vietnam.
The President of the Senate thanked the top leaders of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam for sending greetings to Samdech. Through the delegation, Samdech extended his greetings to all senior leaders and governments of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam. Samdech wished the delegation good health and a successful visit to Cambodia.
