Senior Minister Ly Thuch: Five provinces will be declared mine-free by the end of 2022
(Phnom Penh): On behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Chairman of the Mine Action Authority, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Action Authority, confirmed that five provinces will be declared mine-free by the end of 2022. 3 more to be declared as mine-free provinces under the Samdech Techo project for mine action "Provide safe land, create a smile".
After the civil war in the 1970s, Cambodia became the world's most heavily mined country with about 4 to 6 million mines and other ammunition throughout its region. Landmines and other unexploded ordnance killed 19,816 people and injured 36,100 others.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch made the remarks while presiding over a contract signing ceremony between the Mine Authority and the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) to clear mines in Takeo, Kampong Cham, Kampot, Kampong Chhnang and Svay Rieng provinces. Declared a demining province under the Samdech Techo project for mine action "Provide safe land, create a smile" at the Mine Authority this morning, August 2, 2022.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch stated: "Today, the Mine Authority has brought good news: five provinces, including Takeo, Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Kampot and Svay Rieng, will be declared mines under the Samdech Techo project. "Provide safe land, create a smile," which is good news for people in these five provinces and across the country as well.
Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that for the main operators performing this task, the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) will work to clear mines to provide safe land to people living in the five provinces.
In addition, Senior Minister Ly Thuch confirmed that the Army will start demining operations in the mined water in Kampong Speu province in Phnom Sruoch district, a former hot battlefield with a minefield of up to 655 hectares, while the Blue Hat Army (NPMIC) has been clearing minefields in Tbong Khmum province so far, 25 percent of which has been cleared, which is scheduled to be completed by November.
For the signing of an agreement between the Mine Authority and the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC), which will begin demining operations from August 2022, which includes:
Senior Minister Ly Thuch expressed his deepest gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for providing special gifts to the people of Cambodia in the five provinces to ensure the safety and harmony of life and livelihood. Cambodian-Singaporean diplomats officially inaugurate Cambodia-Singapore Cooperation Center
(Oddar Meanchey): The Ministry of Environment provides landscape viewing towers to protected areas to be used for the purpose of protecting and conserving more natural resources and encouraging protected areas to become places that can attract tourists from near and far.
Mr. Phuong Lina, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Department of Environment, in the recent campaign to promote the potential of natural resources and birds in Cambodia in Samrong City, Oddar Meanchey Province, expressed his pleasure at the project of the Ministry of Environment to provide two more towers. Boeung Snor area, Samrong city and at Sangkha Ruk Voan wildlife sanctuary in Oddar Meanchey province. So far, the province has 4 landscape towers (2 wood and 2 metal).
Mr. Phuong Lina stated that the viewing towers not only provide a means to strengthen the inspection and monitoring, as well as take measures to better respond to criminal activities, these towers provide tourists with a view of the forest and wildlife. Contribute to the development of tourism, connect land to support more income to the community and help the national economy.
The director of the department considers that there are 3 protected areas in Oddar Meanchey province, like the bride hidden in the field of ecotourism, especially the scenery in the 3 protected areas and the Oddar Biodiversity Conservation Corridor with beautiful forests and wildlife. As well as rare and endangered birds are living.
Mr. Phuong Lina hopes that tourists come and visit and the community is ready to provide services such as: selling various products, providing cooking services and setting up tents is also an important part for earning extra income.
According to Chuob Paris, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Environment, the project of the Ministry of Environment is to enhance the landscape in protected areas and promote the benefits of tourism in this natural area.
Please note that the Ministry of Environment in the first phase plans to build 10 landscape towers in 2022. By August 2022, the Ministry has provided four landscape towers, including two in Banteay Meanchey and two in Oddar Meanchey.
