(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Management and Development Commission (TCDC), made 11 key recommendations for the implementation of the Master Development Plan. Siem Reap tourism to be more efficient.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth's key recommendations were made at a ceremony to disseminate the composition and implementation mechanism of the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Development and Management Committee, accompanied by the announcement of the 2022-2023 Action Plan at Sokha Hotel, Siem Reap, Siem Reap Province on the first day. August 2022.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth strongly believes that the launch of the Commission's implementation mechanism will promote the successful, efficient and effective implementation of the "Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035" with the participation of the spirit. Ownership, proactiveness and high responsibility from ministries-institutions, sub-national administrations, local authorities, the private sector, local communities and stakeholders.
On behalf of the Chairman of the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Management and Development Commission, the Deputy Prime Minister made the following key recommendations:
First, the relevant ministries and institutions under the mechanism of the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Management and Development Commission must participate in implementing with high responsibility in accordance with the recommendations of the Prime Minister Samdech Techo on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the conference Restoring and promoting Cambodian tourism in and after the Kovid-19 crisis
Second: Continue to develop Chong Khneas Port in accordance with tourism port standards and study the design and development plan of Chong Khneas Port for short, medium and long term.
Third: The Ministry of Tourism must study, determine the location, and develop the new Siem Reap tourist area.
Fourth, the Executive Committee must prepare a budget to implement the work for 2022-2023 for the Ministry of Economy and Finance to review and decide
Fifth, the five newly formed sub-committees shall prepare their work programs and cooperate with the Secretariat to implement the action plan of the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Management and Development Commission.
Sixth: The Secretariat shall organize a training course on "Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035" for stakeholders, especially tourism target management units, local authorities, private sector, and relevant communities.
Seventh, the Sub-Committee on Tourism Promotion and Attraction of the Executive Committee shall discuss and cooperate with the provincial administration and the private sector in Siem Reap to urgently prepare a promotion strategy for a separate Siem Reap tourism destination in accordance with the guidelines. Defined in the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035.
8th: Continue to strengthen the properties of Siem Reap in attracting and receiving national and international tourists through:
Ninth: Continue to strengthen the quality and scope of mobile and internet services in Siem Reap, especially in priority areas and remote tourist destinations to promote national tourism and attract more international tourists.
10th: Angkor Institute must continue to study and launch a ticket policy for Angkor resort that is attractive for international tourists
