Minister Thong Khon said that in order to attract tourists to Siem Reap during the Kovid-19 crisis in 2021 and 2022, the Prime Minister decided to allow domestic and foreign tourists to work and stay. Cambodia from 2 years onwards can visit the Angkor resort free of charge, which will encourage more domestic tourists to Siem Reap.
He added that the Royal Government has also provided an incentive policy for the purchase of tickets to Angkor by increasing the number of days to visit, including:
Siem Reap will receive more than 100,000 international tourists in 2022 and will increase to about 500,000 in 2023, absorbing a quarter of international tourists visiting Cambodia. More than 2 million locals will visit Siem Reap in 2022 and about 4 million in 2023.
