Kampot Provincial Governor Leads Officials to Pay Tribute to Tremeng Commune Chief in Chhouk District
(Kampot): Dr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot Province, led government officials, the Armed Forces and relevant authorities to pay their respects to the late Mr. Oung Treng, Chief of Trameng Commune, Chhouk District, who passed away at 7:45 am today. On August 1, 2022, at the age of 77, he fell ill at the commune chief's house in Trameng village, Trameng commune, Chhuk district, Kampot province.
On that occasion, Mr. Mao Thunin and all the leaders expressed their condolences to the family of the deceased and expressed their condolences for the loss of Mr. Oung Treng, Chief of Trameng Commune, who is the husband, grandfather, father-in-law.
He considers that this loss is a great loss of a good colleague who has struggled to sacrifice his physical and mental strength in the cause of the motherland. On the other hand, it is the loss of a loving husband and father who have nurtured, cared for, and provided for the family, as well as educated, instructed, and given good advice to make their children good citizens in society.
The provincial governor also donated 100 kilograms of rice, 10 cases of orange juice, 10 cases of noodles, 10 cases of pure water and 2 million riels to participate in the funeral.
India reports first Asian foot-and-mouth disease death
New Delhi: Indian authorities have reported the first case of chickenpox in Asia after the death of a man who had just returned from the United Arab Emirates for a positive test. This is according to the release by AFP on Monday, August 1, 2022.
The Indian man died in Kerala on July 30, about a week after returning from the United Arab Emirates, and was taken to a hospital.
So far, three chickenpox-related deaths have been reported outside of Africa in an outbreak declared by the World Health Organization.
