Come to know the truth! Senior Minister Kun Kim inspects flood situation in Baray and Taing Kork districts (Video inside) (Kampong Thom): This afternoon, August 1, 2022, Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, visited Monitor the flood situation, rainfall and rice crop impacts of the people in Tnaot Chum commune, Baray district and Sralao commune, Taing Kork district, Kampong Thom province.
The visit was also attended by officials from the National Committee for Disaster Management, the Secretariat of the Disaster Management Secretariat of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Deputy Governors, District Governors and relevant officials around the province.
According to the report of the Provincial Disaster Management Secretariat, Tang Kork district, with continuous rains, affected and damaged 7 rice fields in 7 communes, equal to 966 hectares. Of that, 499 hectares were damaged, equivalent to 583 families.
Separately, Baray district affected the rice cultivation of 841 hectares of farmers. In that, light rice increased the season by 486 hectares and heavy rice by 355 hectares. If there is no more rain, the impact and damage may be less because the water is gradually flowing down the canal system.
Speaking on the occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised the Provincial Disaster Management Committee, the competent authorities and the joint forces for implementing the plan to prevent and solve the problems caused by the floods.
The senior minister made a number of recommendations to the provincial disaster management committee to be prepared and take timely and effective response measures to reduce the impact to a minimum and prioritize human life.
