He would like to dedicate and pray for the soul of Mrs. Neav Chanthana to be born in heaven soon, in peace, not to be wasted. Biden says the United States is ready to negotiate with Russia to establish a new framework instead of the New START Strategic Arms Control Treaty
Washington: US President Joe Biden has insisted that Russia should show readiness to cooperate with Washington in the field of nuclear weapons control. This is according to the release by Sputnik on Monday, August 1, 2022.
Biden said Washington was ready to work with Russia to negotiate a new framework for nuclear weapons control that would replace the Strategic Arms Reduction Treaty, known as the New START.
However, Moscow is not the only party Biden wants to see at the negotiating table. He said Beijing, as a signatory to the Nuclear Non-Proliferation Treaty, must also participate in talks dedicated to controlling the number of nuclear warheads.
Royal Government launches key action plan to attract more tourists to Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): The Royal Government of Cambodia on August 1, 2022 announced the launch of key implementation mechanisms and action plans under the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Management and Development Commission to contribute to attracting more international tourists. Visit Siem Reap again.
It should be informed that on March 30, 2021, the Royal Government has already approved the "Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035" and also decided the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Management and Development Commission.
Minister Thong Khon briefed the meeting on the working mechanism of the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Management and Development Commission (TCDC) to support the implementation of the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035 as follows:
First. The Executive Committee is the permanent staff to lead the implementation of the regulations and instructions of the Chairman of the SEC. In particular, direct and coordinate the implementation of the action plan of the master plan.
Second. The five sub-committees are: * Sub-committee on tourism product development * Sub-committee on tourism promotion and attraction * Sub-committee on strengthening the quality and sustainability of tourism development * Sub-committee on environmental management * Sub-committee on infrastructure development and strengthening Connect.
Third. Separate tourist destination management units for the six priority areas include: * Phnom Kulen National Park * Tourism area around Banteay Srei Protected Area * Angkor Heritage Area * Siem Reap City Area * Tonle Sap Lake Area * New Siem Reap Tourism Area.
Fourth. Secretariat to coordinate the implementation of all daily activities of the NCDD.
Along with the announcement of the implementation of the "Action Plan of the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2022-2023" as the Chairman of the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Development and Management Committee, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth gave the following recommendations:
First. Relevant ministries and institutions under the mechanism of the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Management and Development Commission to implement the recommendations of the Prime Minister on the occasion of the closing ceremony of the conference to review the work of tourism, to summarize the plan to restore and promote Cambodia's tourism in and after the crisis. Kovid-19.
Second. Continue to develop Chong Khneas Port in accordance with tourism port standards and study the design and development plan of Chong Khneas Port for the short, medium and long term.
Third. The Ministry of Tourism must study, locate and develop the new Siem Reap tourist area.
Fourth. The Executive Committee shall prepare the budget for 2022-2023 for the Ministry of Economy and Finance to review and decide.
Fifth. The five newly formed sub-committees shall prepare their work programs and cooperate with the Secretariat to implement the action plan of the Siem Reap-Angkor Tourism Management and Development Commission.
Sixth. The Secretariat shall organize a training course on the Siem Reap Tourism Development Master Plan 2021-2035 for stakeholders, especially the Tourism Target Management Unit, as well as local authorities, the private sector and relevant communities.
7th. The Executive Committee on Tourism Promotion and Attraction of the Executive Committee shall discuss and cooperate with the provincial administration and the private sector in Siem Reap to urgently prepare a promotional strategy for a separate Siem Reap tourism destination in accordance with the route set out in the plan. Chief of Siem Reap Tourism Development, 2021-2035.
9th. Continue to strengthen the quality and scope of mobile and internet services in Siem Reap, especially in priority areas and remote tourist destinations to promote national tourism and attract more international tourists.
10th. Angkor Institute continues to study and develop a ticket policy for Angkor resorts that are attractive to international tourists.
