(Phnom Penh): The problem of overweight trucks not only destroyed some national roads or provincial roads, now the problem has spread to some rural roads, where traders use rural roads to avoid the target. Weighed on national or provincial roads and caused damage to all roads.
On the morning of August 1, 2022, Mr. Chrun Therawat, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Rural Development, confirmed that the problem of overweight trucks is also a major problem leading to damage to rural roads after a small number of vehicles escaped inspection. On national and provincial roads.
At a press conference held by the Royal Government Spokesperson under the theme "Five years of achievements of the Ministry of Rural Development", the senior official said that "transportation, including overweight transport is a source. "Which is pushing our rural roads to be damaged."
According to Mr. Chrun Therawat, regarding the overweight transport on rural roads, the Ministry of Rural Development has always worked closely with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to prevent overweight transport, and the Ministry of Public Works Subsequent penalties.
With this challenge, the Ministry of Rural Development, which is in charge of all rural roads, will cooperate with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to set up a proper commission to place the same weight as the national road. He claimed that the Royal Government to build a road costs a lot of money, so it must be well maintained to ensure long-term use.
The transport formula found that one truck over 10 tons was equivalent to 10,000 vehicles traveling on the road. If one truck weighs more than 30 tons, it is equivalent to 810,000 vehicles traveling on the road, that is, if the number of vehicles overweight is multiplied three times in a row, the number of vehicles traveling on the road will be found.
In addition, Mr. Chrun Therawat, from 2018 until now, the Ministry of Rural Development has built infrastructure to connect 2,827 kilometers of new rural roads, including: red gravel road, concrete road and two-story paved road. (DBST).
Separately, the achievements under the national budget for the year (2018-2022), the Ministry has maintained through the rural road maintenance program (Chapter 61 budget) a total of 17,503.87 km and 440 all kinds of artistic structures.
In that, the direct investment project (Chapter 21 budget) builds a total length of 2,472.7 km, 85 concrete bridges with a total length of 3,504 meters and a total of 2,657 art structures. It should be noted that the construction, rehabilitation, maintenance and upgrading of rural roads under the national budget has achieved 100% of the annual plan. Cambodian Association of Real Estate Professionals Issues Petition in Support of the 10th Amendment to the Constitution
