According to a press release from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Cambodia, as the chair of ASEAN, has begun hosting the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings within the ASEAN framework from July 29 to 5. August 2022 in Phnom Penh in live form.
The 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings include:
* Meeting of the ASEAN Nuclear Non-Proliferation Commission * Meeting between ASEAN Foreign Ministers and Representatives of the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights * 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers * Post-ASEAN Meeting of Foreign Ministers with ASEAN Dialogue Partners * 23rd ASEAN Plus Three Foreign Ministers 'Meeting * 12th Asia-East Asia Summit Foreign Ministers' Meeting * 29th ASEAN Regional Forum Meeting
Please be informed that AMM was established in 1967 by the Bangkok Declaration after ASEAN was established. The AMM meets at least four times a year and may convene special meetings when necessary to discuss issues that require urgent attention from ASEAN. AMM regularly reviews and discusses ASEAN Community Building Efforts and its strategic direction, as well as the functioning of ASEAN External Relations.
