In a meeting attended by police leaders and directors of private security service providers and private security agency recruitment enterprises at the National Police General Commission, Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi made the following recommendations:
First, continue to promote the proper implementation of legal standards, sub-decrees, prakas of the Ministry of Interior and the instructions of the General Commission of the National Police in the implementation, as well as the work related to the private security sector. This includes defining the procedures for recruiting agents, the use of uniforms, equipment for agents, and so on.
Second, please pay close attention to the selection of security agents in accordance with the conditions. This point must be done carefully to avoid the intrusion of malicious components with the intention of committing various crimes under the guise of recruiting and embedding activities in the company or institution.
Encourage companies or establishments to prioritize the recruitment of former officers or members of the armed forces who have retired from public service to work for the company, as they may be more knowledgeable about prevention and some of the jobs that can be done. Help companies or institutions.
Third, continue to cooperate with the General Commission of the National Police in more depth and continue to cooperate with the Capital-Provincial Police Commission in doing their work related to the management of the work activities of the company as well as the establishment. This requires a lot of practice, because this collaboration ensures the sustainability of the operation of the institution or company.
Support each other between reducing crime at the local level, and when reducing crime at the local level, create customer comfort, confidence, dependence on the need for services that are the basis of the company's life and death. Doing business.
Fourth, the authorities must pay attention to the institutions in their geographical area, especially the provinces with complex geography, to control the locations that use private security agencies. For companies or establishments to take care to manage their agents tightly, this management is very important because they are afraid that their agents will turn to outside communication and act at the target illegally.
Fifth, promote and support the training of private security agents by requesting the Department of Private Security Management to continue to open this training to further strengthen the capacity to improve skills.
