Regarding this case, Mr. Kim Hak, Village Chief 1, Tumnup Rolok Commune and Community Leader, said that for the location where the above land was poured and these activities were done for two days, he rented machinery and bought land from his nephew. And for the relevant documents are asking for permission from the authorities, but apparently the land has been cleared almost completely.
Separately, Fisheries Administration Officer Mr. Chim Chamroeun, Sangkat Chief of Fisheries Administration, said that the above activities are not allowed by law, requiring to follow the procedure.
After receiving the information from the joint working group at the district level, Mr. Ong Chaly, Deputy District Governor and Chairman of the Working Group, discussed with the Fisheries Officer as well as the request from the people. The machinery stopped and stopped pouring soil to clear the flooded forest and required the excavated soil to be removed only at the end of the rainy season.
