Mondulkiri is a natural gem of rich biodiversity for scientific study in the Northeast of Cambodia.
(Mondulkiri): Mondulkiri Province is located in the northeastern region of Cambodia, 382 kilometers from Phnom Penh. This border province has a total area of 14,288 square kilometers, covered by forests, mountains and plateaus rich in valleys and streams.
This is the largest wildlife sanctuary in Cambodia. Officials and conservationists have also expressed concern over the increasing presence of traps being used by hunters to capture all kinds of wildlife. Original.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary is not only a dense wildlife sanctuary that can sell carbon credits, but also a protected area of international importance for wildlife conservation and other biodiversity. .
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra confirmed that in addition to the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary, Mondulkiri Province also has other wildlife sanctuaries that are rich in rare and endangered species are present in the forest as well as tourist sites. Lots of nature and waterfall locations.
The leader of the Zero Trap Campaign also called on people to end their traps, stop eating meat and come together to conserve this invaluable wildlife to continue to serve the tourism sector as a source of income. Know how to dry for the motherland and as well as leave it for the children of later generations to know.
