2,000 mangrove seedlings planted in Trapeang Sangke fishing community, Kampot province
(Kampot): 2,000 mangrove seedlings were planted in Trapeang Sangke fishing community in Trapeang Sangke commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province. The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, with the participation of more than 100 leaders of the Ministry of Environment, Provincial Administration, Communities and the Cambodian Young International Chamber of Commerce (JCI) on the morning of July 31, 2022. .
On that occasion, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment emphasized that the cooperation of this tree to cultivate the spirit of love for natural resources among the public and especially to create greenery, increase the diversity of all kinds of biodiversity, especially fishery resources to protect the environment. Coastal areas will help withstand climate change.
According to statistics, Cambodia has more than 56,000 hectares of mangrove forests in four provinces of Cambodia, including Kampot, Kep and Sihanoukville, which are coastal provinces.
The senior official said that the mangroves are now facing extinction due to human and natural factors, and human factors are still the main factors leading to the disappearance of mangroves.
Faced with this problem, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment confirmed that the authorities have strictly enforced the law against the perpetrators and at the same time put in place economic measures to create a local economy to reduce pressure on natural resources.
"People living along the coast rely on mangrove forests for their livelihoods, such as family fishing or small-scale fishing or ecotourism," said Neth Pheaktra.
According to Mat Him, president of the Trapeang Sangke fishing community in Kampot province, the mangrove forest is a fishing ground for fishermen and a villa for biodiversity.
He said that since 2014, Trapeang Sangke fishing community has been organized as a natural tourism area with the support of the authorities and national and international tourists. The community's major project focuses on mangrove restoration. Since 2010, the community has planted more than 600,000 mangrove trees.
"Participating in mangrove planting has helped create jobs, prevent migration and encourage children to attend school, and we have jointly planned to build a natural oxygen plant," said the community leader.
It should be noted that the planting of mangroves has played an important role in conserving natural resources and reducing various natural disasters, because mangroves are important bodyguards in preventing storms, floods, increasing habitat for all biodiversity, as well as Socio-economic rehabilitation for people in the community and fishermen who live and work in the coastal areas of Cambodia.
Reforestation enhances forest cover, which is an important habitat for biodiversity to contribute to the conservation of fish species, especially reducing environmental and social impacts. The Association of Medical Nursing Technical Students of the University of Health Sciences issued a petition in full support for the 10th Amendment to the Constitution
