Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, told Fresh News that there are four types of goods that the Ministry of Commerce does not grant exclusive rights to import or record exclusive rights to any individual or company. There are all kinds of used goods or second-hand goods, medicines for humans and animals, fertilizers, pesticides and some prohibited goods such as weapons, drugs and poisons.
"In this exemption, we see that second-hand goods cannot be monopolized, medicines cannot be monopolized, fertilizers and pesticides cannot be monopolized," he said. Also. "Therefore, the public should be aware that it is imperative that we do not condone any infringement of privacy rights, and that we have received a complaint or request for protection of the rights of the copyright holder or the recipient."
At the same time, he stated that although fertilizers and pesticides do not provide exclusive import rights, but the import of agricultural equipment such as tractors, washing machines, etc. is under the control of the brand, which the Ministry must record the letter of exclusive right to import and Distribute goods because this type of goods has competition between many brands that are imported into Cambodia.
However, this monopoly does not cover those who buy for personal use or goods used for non-commercial or social purposes, meaning that even if the goods are registered for import, they are exclusive. If an individual buys or imports goods from abroad for personal use or for charitable activities, assistance to NGOs, technical experiments, etc. are possible.
Mr. Pen Sovichet stated that the business registration or the receipt of the record and the exclusive power of attorney are for pure and new goods only, not covering the goods that have already been sold and the goods that are already used. Or second-hand goods.
Please be informed that in the first half of 2022, the Ministry of Commerce received and recorded 34 letters of exclusive rights to exclusive importers from abroad to negotiate sales in Cambodia, which increased this number to 414. In the past 5 years.
