(Mondulkiri): The Zero Trap Campaign in the Protected Areas, initiated and led by the Ministry of Environment and in collaboration with international organizations working on the conservation of natural resources, has been running for 152 days on July 31 after being announced. Officially on March 3, 2022, World Wildlife Day.
The Zero Trap campaign focuses on six provinces in the eastern highlands, including Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Kratie, Mondulkiri, Ratanakkiri and Kampong Thom. These six provinces have large protected areas and areas with a lot of wildlife hunting.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Campaign Working Group, said that for 150 days, the campaign went smoothly, with a series of campaigns in Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Kratie, Mondulkiri. After the Zero Trap Campaign in Mondulkiri Province on July 29, 2022, the campaign will continue to shoot at Kampong Thom Province in August and Ratanakkiri Province in September.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra assessed that people are beginning to understand that wildlife meat and specimens or blood of wild animals are not a medicine or a tonic or help their health, but instead may improve their health. They are affected because in the flesh of wild animals, there are many kinds of viruses, sometimes lethal, that can kill us even faster.
