Community Aid for Hope issues statement in support of the 10th Amendment to the Constitution
(Phnom Penh): The leaders and all members of Aid of Hope for the Community have announced their full support for the 10th Amendment to the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The statement noted that the amendment really filled the gaps in the constitution to ensure the interests of the nation, especially to ensure that the executive branch can function normally and not be stuck in any circumstances. Performing missions to the nation and the motherland in accordance with the provisions of the Constitution and the laws of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The statement added that the amendment was necessary to ensure respect for the fundamental principles of the Constitution: liberal democracy, pluralism and constitutional monarchy.
In this statement, the Community Aid for Hope condemned a number of unscrupulous individuals who expressed pessimism over the initiative to amend the 10th Constitution and additional laws aimed at ensuring the normalization of national institutions without a clear basis. The actual content of the proposed amendment now is a statement that distorts the facts, completely different from the actual content of the proposal to amend the 10th Constitution.
Community Aid for Hope solemnly supports the 10th Amendment of the Constitution and is optimistic and optimistic that all national institutions will continue to fully implement the Constitution, in particular continue to support and protect it. Peace under the leadership of the Royal Government of Cambodia to ensure peace, political stability, democracy and development in Cambodia.
