(Phnom Penh): A young Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie was crushed to death by a container truck at 8:30 pm on July 28, 2022 in front of Borey Santepheap 2, Street 30m, Sre Chomrov Village, Sangkat. Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
According to a military police officer, the victim, named Major Khuon Visal, was a gentleman who loved work, respected discipline, and was loved by his friends and relatives.
For the last three years, Brigadier General Khuon Visal has been on a mission with the team to prevent and organize order at Luang Mey Hospital, which was set up to treat 19 Kovid patients until the situation improved and the treatment center was closed. However, the mission of Prince Khuon Visal continues to protect the Kovid 19 treatment equipment at Luang Med Hospital.
On the morning of July 29, 2022, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army, and Chairman of the Sub-Committee on Security and Order Management at Target and Saktalysak Areas. The team brought 4 million Riels, 30 cases of pure water to attend the funeral of Prince Khuon Visal and sent condolences to the family of the deceased.
At the same time, Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, also sent a team to bring 2 million Riels to attend the funeral and sent condolences to the family of the deceased.
Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, also donated 20 million riels, clean water and 30 cases of soft drinks, 4 bags of rice to the family for preparation. Funeral in advance and subsequent colleagues in the Phnom Penh Gendarmerie to join the festival, along with the budget of the National Gendarmerie family, initiated by General Sao Sokha, will be handed over to the families of the dead later.
Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang expressed his deepest condolences to the family and relatives of the deceased for the loss of Prince Ek Khuon Visal, a young man who was determined to give up his homeland, a rare human resource in the army. The Royal Gendarmerie in general is an important resource for the Royal Gendarmerie of Phnom Penh, in particular, and a good child in the family.
It should also be noted that the National Police Sports Unit of Cambodia, led by Mr. Chheng Sopheak, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Sports Council of the Ministry of Interior, led the athletes to compete in 6 sports, including: WT Taekwondo Table tennis, wrestling, judo and karate, and the event will take place from July 22 to 31, 2022.
