(Takeo): Mr. Sok Sokan, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Kirivong District Local Party Working Group, stated that the solidarity of the district, commune, party, district-commune party and district-commune authorities To bring success to the Cambodian People's Party in Kirivong district in the election of the 5th mandate Commune / Sangkat Council.
He said that the above three characters are important and necessary elements that make the living standards of the people of Kirivong district constantly improve and live in harmony with honor, warmth and dignity and increase confidence. For the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party in Kirivong district.
This statement was made on the occasion that Mr. Sok Sokan chaired a meeting to disseminate the results of the meeting of the Extraordinary Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party to the Kirivong District Local Party Working Group, the 12 Commune Commune Party Working Group, Kirivong District Party Committee. And 12 commune party committees at the Kirivong district party headquarters on Saturday, July 30, 2022.
The meeting was also chaired by Dr. Chiv Keng, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Honorary Co-Chair of the Kirivong District Local Party Working Group. The party working group visited all 12 communes, with the participation of 166 district party branch members and chairmen of the 12 commune party committees.
Mr. Suth Khon, Vice Chairman of Kirivong District Party Committee, read out the report on the Commune / Sangkat Council Election of the 5th Mandate and the Work Direction towards the 7th National Assembly Election 2023 of the CPP Extraordinary Central Committee Meeting. Cambodia. Meanwhile, Mr. Tek Tong Lim, Chairman of the District Party Committee, read out the report on the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election 2022 in Kirivong District.
Mr. Sok Sokan also commended and appreciated the free and fair commune council elections in Kirivong district in a neutral environment, security, order, non-violence and intimidation.
In order to express his deep gratitude to all the working group and to congratulate the election results in Kirivong district, Mr. Sok Sokan also handed over congratulatory letters and prizes to Kampot and Ream Andek communes that won 5 seats. / 5 As well as congratulatory letters and prizes to the party working group at the polling station and counting the ballots ranked 1st to 5th.
At the same time, he also handed over a letter of thanks to His Excellency the Honorary Co-Chair of the Kirivong District Local Working Group. And Kirivong District Party Youth Working Group.
Finally, Mr. Sok Sokan also reminded the CPP in Kirivong district at all levels to carry out the work consistently in accordance with the work direction set and must adhere to the party's strategic commitment is "strive to maintain advantage. "Win and continue to expand the advantage of winning in the 7th legislative election."
