Working Group of the Youth Organization of the Cambodian People's Party in East and Southeast Asia issues a petition in support of the 10th Amendment of the Constitution
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Heng Sour, Chairman of the Working Group of the Youth Organization of the Cambodian People's Party in East and Southeast Asia, as well as all the leaders and members of the Working Group of the Youth Organization of the Cambodian People's Party in East Asia. And the Southeast have declared their full support for the 10th Amendment to the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The petition states that the amendment really fills a gap in the constitution to ensure the national interest, especially to ensure that the executive branch can function normally and not be stuck in any circumstances. Carry out missions to the nation and the motherland in accordance with the provisions of the Constitution and the laws of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The petition states that the amendment is necessary to ensure respect for the fundamental principles of the Constitution: liberal democracy, pluralism and constitutional monarchy.
Through this petition, the working group of the Cambodian Youth Organization in East and Southeast Asia rejects the pessimistic views of the unscrupulous people on the initiative to amend the current constitution without a clear basis and inaccurate. Certainly, the proposal for the amendment now is a statement that distorts the facts, completely different from the actual content of the proposal for the 10th amendment to the Constitution.
