Iran arrests Swedish citizen for espionage, according to state media
Tehran: Iran's intelligence agency said on Saturday that it had arrested a Swede for spying, but did not specify his composition. This is according to the publication by Reuters on Saturday, July 30, 2022.
"A citizen of the Kingdom of Sweden has been arrested for espionage," Iran's state news agency reported, citing a statement from the intelligence agency. It was not immediately clear when the arrests were made.
The suspects were under surveillance by intelligence agencies during several previous trips to Iran due to their suspicious behavior and communication, according to a Swedish Foreign Ministry spokesman. This Saturday, the ministry could not immediately be reached for comment.
In May, the Swedish Foreign Ministry announced that a Swedish man had been detained in Iran just days after the government issued a restraining order against illegal travel to Iran. Mention the deteriorating security situation.
