Cambodia Hosts First Special Meeting in 2022 for 4 Days
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia Hosts the First Special Meeting 2022 of the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights (ICHA-AICHR) at the Cambodiana Hotel, Phnom Penh for 4 days from 30 July to August 2, 2022.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, Representative of Cambodia to the AICHR and Chair of AIS 2022 and attended by representatives of all ASEAN Member States to AICHR and the ASEAN Secretariat.
Ms. Ouch, Editor-in-Chief of the General Department of Administration and Complaints of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee and Assistant Secretary of the ICHA Secretariat representing Cambodia, said: The height of the protection of human rights in the ASEAN region, and the member countries of the ASEAN, there are 10 countries, including Cambodia, the meeting was attended by representatives of all countries, including the ASEAN Secretariat.
According to Ms. Ouch, the author of this meeting will look at:
First: AISA Annual Report. Second: AISA 2023 Priorities. Third, on the progress report of the Icha Vision Paper 2019 to 2022. Fourth: on the rights of children, the rights of persons with disabilities, the rights of indigenous peoples, climate change, and violence against children.
She claimed that on the last day of the meeting, on August 2, 2022, Mr. Keo Remy, on behalf of the ASEAN Chairmanship, would meet with the ASEAN Secretary-General in the morning and in the afternoon lead the Acha delegation from 10 countries, including the Secretary-General. ASEAN to meet with the Minister of Foreign Affairs.
