Professor Laurent Seme is visiting Cambodia for the first time since taking office as Asia-Pacific Director in May 2022. During his visit to Cambodia, he paid a courtesy call on his counterpart, leaders, ministries, higher education institutions and diplomats.
During his visit, Mr. Ser Me met with leaders of AUF member universities, including: Institute of Technology of Cambodia, Royal University of Fine Arts, Academy of Digital Technology of Cambodia, University of Health Sciences, Royal University of Phnom Penh, National Institute of Education, University. Royal School of Law and Economics Royal School of Administration, National University of Management, National Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations.
During his meetings with university leaders, exchanges on innovation projects, collaborations in various fields, accuracy, pedagogy and further training for students and professors were discussed.
Prof. Ser Me also met with Dr. Um Romney, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, in charge of STEM science training at the high school and university level. He then met with Mr. Chhiv Yi Seang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
The Regional Director ended his mission by meeting with Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, highlighting the importance of quality training of teachers in bilingual classes.
The Minister requested that, if possible, establish a French-language training network in all AUF member higher education institutions and that multilingual politics be very favorable in Cambodia and play an important role in the sustainable development of the Cambodian economy. The Minister also initiated a conference in August with the participation of speakers from AUF member universities on the use of French as a science, culture and economics.
This was confirmed by Professor Laurent Seme in a press conference on the afternoon of July 30, 2022 at One More Restaurant.
