(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Rice Federation has set a plan to increase rice exports from Cambodia to the United States next year as it sees potential markets and opportunities for Cambodian rice exports in the first seven months of 2022. Only 228 tons of rice went to the United States.
Oknha Song Saran, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, recently paid a business visit to the United States to study the opportunities and possibilities that have strengthened the rice trade.
Duke Song Saran told Fresh News that during the business visit, he met with city council members, communities, entrepreneurs, food distributors and other investors organized by the Consulate General of Cambodia in Long Beach and California.
He claimed that the meeting seemed to be very successful in mobilizing and strengthening trade between US and Cambodian companies, which improved export opportunities to the US market.
He said that because the US market has high standards, regular quality rice will not be able to be exported, so the federation will focus on exporting fine and organic rice.
Through a study of the market in the United States, the President of the Cambodian Rice Federation observed that the rice of neighboring countries, Cambodia, Thailand and Vietnam, which have long penetrated this market seems to be very successful. In particular, Cambodia still faces some challenges, especially transportation problems and rising transportation costs, while Cambodia has not yet been able to allow large vessels to dock and not yet stockpile rice.
"This is an opportunity for us to expand our market," he said. In the past, we have had a lot of problems with transportation, and Cambodia is a small country that exports to him (the United States), which makes it difficult to transport rice to his country. "We are looking for a solution as we are gaining support and the possibility of exporting by 2023."
On this issue, Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, said that the US market is as potential as the EU market.
He added that Cambodia's luxury rice exports have been attractive in the US market, especially for Asian Americans, so Cambodia will be able to expand its export market and compete with rice. Neighbors.
