(Mondulkiri): As of June, in the first half of 2022, the Department of Environment of Mondulkiri Province has prepared a total of 70 cases of natural resource crimes, of which 7 have been fined and sent to court. 63 cases in Mondulkiri province in accordance with the legal procedures on protected areas and related legal provisions.
According to the summary report, Mr. Keo Sopheak, Director of Mondulkiri Provincial Department of Environment, spoke at the opening ceremony of the Zero Trap Campaign in Mondulkiri Province on July 29, 2022, yesterday, chaired by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment and Chairman of the Trap Campaign. Zero with the participation of the provincial administration, partner organizations, students and community members.
Taking this opportunity, he added to the strict action against those who are still trapping and hunting all kinds of wildlife in the protected area and in the geographical area of Mondulkiri province is the law enforcement officers. Will continue to strengthen law enforcement and patrols in the cause of protection and conservation of wildlife and biodiversity in accordance with the purposes and objectives of the Law on Protected Areas.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra pointed out that large-scale natural resource crimes in protected areas no longer occur, but small-scale crimes have occurred, which the Ministry of Environment and relevant authorities have been pursuing the law responsibly. . The Ministry of Environment will continue its mission with high responsibility and professionalism in managing and conserving protected areas in Cambodia for generations to come.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra reiterated that if there is no demand, there is no supply, those who eat wild animals should give up the habit of eating wild animals and do not believe that wild animals are a tonic or medicine. On the contrary, he said, wild meat can pose a high risk to the health of consumers because wild meat is not properly examined and embedded with deadly viruses.
According to Mr. Chak Mengheang, Deputy Governor of Mondulkiri Province, wildlife and natural resources are very important to achieve the development goals of the old eco-tourism destination, but natural resource crime in Mondulkiri Province is still a challenge. Therefore, all parties must be involved in preventing trapping, hunting and wildlife trafficking, as well as the destruction of natural resources.
He said that the wildlife trade has had a positive impact on all kinds of wildlife, such as deer, deer, deer and other wildlife.
