ADA Acquisition and ILID International School Award Certificates and Study Materials to Young Children Graduating in 2021-2022
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of July 30, 2022, ADA Accident and ILID International School organized a program to award graduation certificates and hand over study materials to children who graduated in 2021-2022.
The certification ceremony was attended by Ms. Khun Rachana, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Representative of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Vorn Samphas, Country Director of ADAAC and Mr. ILID Director. Teachers, as well as many students and parents.
Through past efforts, the Alliance for Early Childhood Education, which is part of the iLead Community for Education, has supported the education of community schools in Kandal, Takeo, Prey Veng, Kep, Kampot, Preah Sihon and Koh Kong provinces.
In addition, proceeds from the Alliance's International School for Early Childhood Education are used to feed 200 young children daily, as well as to build 165 hand-washing facilities for them. Well.
At the same time, Mr. Vorn Samphas, Country Director of ADAAC Cambodia, said, "Together we make learning full of motivation, participation and fun to build a great world for children." "Can grow and prosper."
On this occasion, Ms. Khun Rachana, Undersecretary of State, Representative of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, added that ADA Active has actively contributed to the education sector in Cambodia, especially to support early childhood education. .
"Through the Alliance for Education, the school is non-profit and all proceeds are spent on project activities, especially for children and youth in need," she said. In the community. "Through this activity, connecting children in rural communities with children studying in the city has helped them to support and learn to live together."
In addition, Ms. Khun Rachana also praised the partnership of the Alliance for Education, which has helped to improve human resource development, especially focusing on quality young children and the environment. Security. She continued to thank the teachers who participated in training students in this partnership, we contribute to the development to achieve the vision of the national plan on early childhood development.
In addition, representatives of ADA Action and ILED International School provided teaching and learning materials to 25 community kindergartens, as well as materials for the digital library to Rabbit School, a special education school for children with intellectual disabilities. .
