Senior official of the Ministry of Environment: Ecotourism plays an important role in improving the lives of local people and contributes to the conservation of natural resources as well as the development of society.
Mr. Di Rado, Deputy Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, considered that the campaign to promote the potential of natural resources and birds in Cambodia that we are all doing now is an opportunity for the public to better understand the value of biodiversity and systems. Ecology and spirit, please join us to continue to set an example as a good example for the care of our environment on a regular basis.
At the same time, the Undersecretary of State stated that the protected areas of Cambodia are an important part of the country's great natural resources and provide many environmental, economic, social and cultural benefits.
Mr. Khvay Atiya added that the Ministry of Environment has increased the system of protected areas with an area of 41% of the total land area and modernized the management of institutions and natural resources. The protected area system is an important habitat for wildlife, including birds, which is one of the most important and beneficial components of natural resources in Cambodia.
