Phnom Penh CPP Releases Statement in Full Support of the 10th Amendment to the Constitution
(Phnom Penh): Members of the Phnom Penh Municipal Committee of the Cambodian People's Party (CPP) have issued a statement fully supporting the 10th amendment to the Cambodian Constitution.
On this occasion, there was also the invitation of Ms. Chea, Vice Chairman of the Standing Committee, members of the working group in charge of the commune-village, including the party committee in the district-commune party, working group of women and youth around the district, a total of about 250 people.
To begin with, the ceremony paid homage to the national flag, the party flag and the deceased. After that, Mr. Chap Chanvithya, President of Leuk Dek District Party, read out the announcement issued by the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party to the ceremony.
She further emphasized that the conference went smoothly in the spirit of unity, democracy and responsibility for the national interest and the people of Cambodia. The meeting evaluated the report of the results of the 5th Commune / Sangkat Election 2022, with the Cambodian People's Party receiving overwhelming votes, making the party a glorious victory.
She added that this success demonstrates the political maturity of Cambodia's multi-party liberal democratic process, with elections held on time and maintaining political diversity at all levels. At the same time, the meeting also solemnly supported Samdech Techo Hun Sen as the Prime Ministerial candidate for the 7th legislature of the National Assembly and supported His Excellency Hun Manet as the future Prime Ministerial candidate.
Moreover, under the wise and prudent leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister and President of the Cambodian People's Party, the party has a long-term plan, vision and solidarity to continue to lead God. The Kingdom of Cambodia for a long time to come under the umbrella of the Constitution and the cool shadow of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
She also noted that the conference noted the strengths, weaknesses and challenges posed by internal factors such as extremists, which often cause political instability, affect the economy and society. . In addition to internal factors, Cambodia is also under pressure from the geopolitical competition of the superpowers, which causes the world order to fall into uncertainty, danger and rapid change.
After hearing the announcement of the results of the meeting of the Extraordinary Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, the members of the People's Party throughout Leuk Dek district became more aware of the importance of this meeting and made a commitment to continue their efforts. How to protect the interests of the people towards victory in the election of the 7th legislature, which will be held on July 23, 2023.
