Senior official of the Ministry of Environment: More and more restaurant owners have volunteered to stop trapping illegal wildlife by announcing not to sell wild meat dishes
During the Zero Trap Campaign in Mondulkiri Province on July 29, 2022, yesterday, the owners of 32 restaurants in the province announced that they did not sell any meat from all kinds of wild animals, and they were praised and received Known from the Ministry of Environment.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra congratulated the restaurant owner in Mondulkiri province for participating in the conservation of wildlife by announcing that he will not sell food from all kinds of wildlife meat and report to the authorities in case of wildlife sale.
A senior Ministry of Environment official said: "This is one of the successes of the Zero Trap campaign, which has convinced restaurant owners to engage with the relevant authorities to curb illegal hunting and wildlife trade."
(Phnom Penh): On July 29, 2022, 55 vulnerable families, including the elderly and the disabled, living in 10 communes in Tuol Kork district, Phnom Penh, received food donations. And budget for livelihood from the working group of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch, Sangkat-Khan, led by Mr. Chea Pisey, District Governor and Honorary Chairman of Khan Sub-Branch with Mrs. An Phalla.
The equitable activities of the Tuol Kork Red Cross Sub-Branch were also attended by Mrs. Oknha Van Luy, Honorary Vice President of Khan Sub-Branch, Mr. Keo Sophea, Chairman of Khan Sub-Branch Committee, Khan Sub-Branch Working Group and Sangkat CRC.
Mr. Chea Pisey on the occasion of giving humanitarian donations said that with the high attention from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, both Samdech always Always advise the Cambodian Red Cross team at all levels to consider the well-being of vulnerable people throughout the country, regardless of race, color or political affiliation.
