The Cambodian Human Rights Committee (CCHR) presents the results of a meeting of the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights's Assistant Working Group Meeting.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Human Rights Committee, on behalf of the Chairman of the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights (ICHA) 2022, convened a meeting of the ICHA Representative Support Team at the Cambodiana Hotel on July 29, 2022.
The meeting was chaired and coordinated by Ms. Long Sonita, Deputy Representative of Cambodia to AICA and attended by the Assistant Representatives of AICA of all ASEAN Member States and the ASEAN Secretariat.
To begin with, Ms. Long Sonita, Chair of the Meeting, expressed her respect and gratitude to all AISA Assistants and the ASEAN Secretariat for attending the meeting by invitation.
The meeting then reviewed, discussed and revised the contents of four draft reports related to ACHA meetings and previous meetings between ACHA and stakeholders.
The meeting also reviewed three documents for the meeting between Aicha and the ASEAN Foreign Ministers, including:
* First: Icha 2022 Annual Report * Second: Icha President's Statement to the ASEAN Foreign Ministers * Third: Aisha 2023 Priority Program / Activities
In addition, the meeting also discussed the progress of the concept document on the priority program of Icha 2019-2022 related to children's rights, health rights, clean water, rights of indigenous peoples, rights of people with disabilities, the effects of climate change, trafficking People and violence against women, children and children.
After review and revision of the support team, all of the above documents will be submitted to the first special meeting of AICA for review and approval.
Finally, the Assistant Representatives of all ASEAN countries in AICA expressed their appreciation and congratulations to the Cambodian Deputy Representative and the ICHA-Cambodia working group for organizing and leading this meeting well with proud results.
