NEC Holds Training on Census Estimation for 2022 Voter List and Voter Registration
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of July 29, 2022, the National Election Committee (NEC) organized a training course on Census Statistics for census and voter registration. 2022 to the Chairman of the Deputy Chief of the Secretariat of the Capital and Provinces for the Election of the NEC (NEC), the Chief of the Legal and Technical Services Division and a total of 85 NEC officials at the NEC office.
Mr. Som Soreida stated that in order to provide support to the NEC in preparing the voter list, which ensures the accuracy, completeness and up-to-date, all relevant authorities and units must conduct this census on a regular basis. Every year, based on the election law, regulations and procedures, joint guidelines between the Ministry of Interior and the NEC and other legal documents in force.
At the same time, Mr. Som Soreida introduced to the President and the professional section of all the following:
* First, pay attention to the correct implementation of the NEC's guidelines on the census of population estimates for the examination of the 2022 voter list and registration and the Joint Instruction No. 019 S.N. Dated 26 May 2021 on the preparation for the annual review of the voter list and voter registration between the Ministry of Interior and the NEC.
* Second: Disseminate widely to all stakeholders in their capital and province about the work of collecting statistics, especially the people in the villages, communes, sangkats, so that they can cooperate in their roles with the commune / sangkat authorities.
* Third: Follow the work calendar to collect population statistics in communes / sangkats, which are determined and distributed by the Capital and Provincial Departments of Operations of the General Department of Legal and Technical Services.
(Pursat): Mr. HUN Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, on July 29, 2022, assigned Dr. Heng Sok Kong, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia to inaugurate the tower. Aqua Tower Water Purifier and AquaSan Sanitary Ware at Preah Sihanouk Krakor Secondary School in Chheu Teal Khpos Village, Kbal Trach Commune, Krakor District, Pursat Province.
He added that the water purification tower is very important to contribute to the health and well-being of the people through the production of one thousand liters of clean and safe water that can be distributed to teachers. Teachers, students and the people around the school can use it without worrying about using unclean water or well water that contains some harmful substances that can cause disease or risk to your health.
In addition, it also helps to improve livelihoods and reduce poverty by teachers and students do not have to buy pure water to drink as before, just bring a bottle of water to drink and can take water home. Also and improve the quality of education by students have enough time no need to go far to find water to use and drink.
At the end, Mr. Heng Sok Kong also distributed Mr. Hun Many's gift to 35 teachers, each of whom received 20,000 Riels, 250 students each received 2 notebooks and 2 pens. And a budget of 5,000 riels. Finally, the presidium and the participants of the whole ceremony also planted a tree as a souvenir in Sihanoukville Krakor Secondary School.
