(Mondulkiri): The Zero Trap Campaign, an initiative of the Ministry of Environment on March 3, is a national campaign aimed at raising awareness of the impact of using illegal animal traps to save wildlife in Cambodia.
The presence of all kinds of wildlife living in natural forests is considered as an important part of Cambodia's heritage and with an important part for the development of the national economy, especially the presence of wildlife is also a part of economic development. People living around all natural resource protection areas through eco-tourism, including the creation of various tourism products to serve tourists to their area.
He said the campaign had been announced in several provinces, including Mondulkiri, focusing on the use of conservative marketing methods to address the crisis, traps and other threats. To Cambodia's protected areas and biodiversity.
"Enterprises and value chains that include ecotourism, reducing emissions from deforestation and degradation (REDD +), and conservation-friendly products can really provide," she said. "A powerful motivation to address the trap crisis and other threats to Cambodia's biodiversity."
"At the same time, joint measures and strict enforcement of the law are essential to stop the demand for wildlife meat and close all wildlife markets," said WWF Director Seng Teak.
"The key to addressing the root causes of poaching and wildlife trade is to ensure that people living in and outside protected areas can participate more closely in wildlife conservation, on a natural and sustainable basis," he said. "Sustainable economic development."
Mondulkiri is the fourth province in the eastern region of the Mekong River to participate in the Zero Trap Campaign in Protected Areas to stop illegal trapping and poaching and to make protected areas safer. Biodiversity of all kinds and for generations.
Cambodia, Thailand set up cycling event to promote Koh Kong and Trat destinations as safe tourism destinations
(Koh Kong): The Cambodian and Thai sides have collaborated on a friendly cycling event in order to strengthen the Cambodian-Thai friendly cooperation and promote Koh Kong and Trat provinces as special safety tourism destinations to celebrate the journey to sports. SEA Games and ASEAN Para Games 2023, hosted by Cambodia.
This event was held on July 29, 2022 under the cooperation between Koh Kong Provincial Administration and Trat Provincial Administration and the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia with more than 600 cyclists, including 192 cyclists in Koh Kong Province and There are more than 421 cyclists from Thailand, such as from Trat, Serey Saket, Sa Kaeo, Nakhon Ratchasima, Surin, Uttol, Upper Maha Sarakham and Chiang Mai.
The event was also held in the presence of Mr. Kareem Hammat Nossri, Under Secretary of State for the Ministry of Tourism, Representative of Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, Ms. Mithona Phuthong, Governor of Koh Kong Province and Mr. Thuon Sinan, President of the Asia Pacific Tourism Association. Senate and former Minister of Tourism and Sports and Mr. Narong Thepsena, Deputy Governor of Trat Province.
The Cambodia-Thailand Friendship Cycling Event was supported and congratulated by Thai cyclists and the people of Koh Kong Province, with government officials, people, students coming out to greet the streets from the border in front of the Koh Kong Resort Hotel. Head to Pak Klang pagoda to pay homage to the religious ceremony and then continue to finish at Bang Kayak community.
