(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of July 29, 2022, General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, paid a courtesy call on Brigadier General Moniko Estota Abang, Commander of the Philippine Army Special Forces Command and a delegation. General Command.
On that occasion, Brigadier General Moniko Estota Abang thanked His Excellency the Commander-in-Chief for the warm welcome and mentioned the visit of the delegation to Cambodia in order to strengthen the cooperation between the two countries' armies. Two, especially on counter-terrorism training.
In response, General Vong Pisen thanked the Philippine Army for assisting in the training of human resources in the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, stating that this was the right choice and decision of Cambodia.
General Vong Pisen recalled that Cambodia and the Philippines have had historical and traditional relations since the 16th century, and established diplomatic relations in August 1952 and re-established ties during that time. 1995.
General Vong Pisen said that in addition to achieving the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding between the two countries' Ministries of Defense in 2017, the Philippines has helped train the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) on staffing, logistics and other skills. The 70th Brigade also collaborated with the Philippine Army to plan future training.
In addition to the cooperation between the two armies, the Commander-in-Chief also highlighted the recent exchanges between the Cambodian and Philippine Armed Forces, which have borne fruit and given the utmost importance to strengthening peace in the region as well as strengthening ties. And bilateral cooperation. 77-million-year-old dinosaur skeleton sold for $ 6 million
