(Phnom Penh): During the 199 Kovid Crisis, the Royal Government of Cambodia, with one hand, prevented the spread of the disease and with the other hand tried to hold on to the people so that they would not fall and seriously affect their livelihood until they go hungry to eat every day.
The Royal Government of Cambodia's consideration of daily life for those who are severely affected, or we can say that for the poor people, the Royal Government has provided a series of social assistance, including monthly allowances.
From June 2020 until now, the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has raised more than 70 people living in poverty and affected by the global epidemic. Ten thousand families equals nearly 2.8 million people.
Mr. Theng Panhathorn, Director General of Planning of the Ministry of Planning, at a press conference of the Royal Government Spokesperson's Unit on the five-year achievements of the Ministry of Planning on the morning of July 29, 2022, said: "The Cambodian government is so far around 700,000 poor families who have received this support, if we consider the population of about 2.8 million."
The senior official also claimed that through direct interviews with the people, they were very excited and surprised by the consideration of the Royal Government, they did not expect that when suffering from Kovid. 19 The Royal Government not only prevents and mitigates the effects of the national economy, but also contributes to their livelihoods.
According to Mr. Theng Panhathorn, on July 27, under the coordination of the National Council for Social Protection in cooperation with UNDP, praised and appreciated the cash support program of the Royal Government of Cambodia and saw that it is true. Really help the people and also made a public announcement about this assessment.
Please be informed that the cash support program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19 was launched on June 24, 2020 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The program aims to support and facilitate the lives of more than 680,000 poor and vulnerable families with equity cards, implemented over the past 25 months and at a total cost of approximately $ 744 million. Beneficiaries, development partners, national and international civil society organizations and the general public.
The Cambodian Labor Advisory Association issued a statement fully supporting the National Assembly's approval of the 10th Amendment to the Constitution.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Labor Advisory Association on July 29, 2022 issued a statement expressing its full support for the National Assembly's approval of the 10th Amendment to the Constitution.
In its public letter, the Cambodian Labor Advisory Association considers that the 10th amendment of the Constitution at this time is very important in accordance with the principles set out in the Constitution to ensure the general leadership of the country. Runs smoothly and sustainably in all circumstances.
The Cambodian Labor Advisory Association strongly supports the requirement that the top leaders of the Cambodian nation have a single nationality, Khmer nationality. This is the right decision to maintain the independence, sovereignty and territorial integrity of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which is the basis for building and developing a sustainable Cambodian socio-economy.
The Cambodian Labor Advisory Association is committed to continuing to work with the Royal Government of Cambodia to restore and promote the economic development of Cambodia, which has a top national leader of the same Khmer nationality, in line with the current amendment to the Constitution.
