Minister of Health Instructs Capital-Provincial Governors to Increase Education and Disseminate Standards on Standard Operating Procedures for the Management, Care and Treatment of Kovid 19-Home Patients
(Phnom Penh): Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission for Combating Kovid 19 on July 29, 2022, sent a letter to all provincial governors to increase education. And widely disseminate standard operating procedures for the management, care and treatment of Kovid 19-patients at home.
In this letter, the Minister of Health stated that the Ministry of Health has established standard operating procedures for the management, care and treatment of Kovid 19-asymptomatic and mild patients at home, as stated in Proclamation No. 296, dated June 20, 2021.
At the same time, most people have been quick to test for Kovid-19 on their own, get positive results, and in mild cases, and opt for home treatment. Therefore, in order to increase education and disseminate widely to the public, the Ministry of Health has prepared a summary of standard operating procedures for the management, care and treatment of 19's Kovid patients at home (attached) to facilitate implementation. .
