(Phnom Penh): A new book entitled "Secrets Behind the Scenes" that reveals the behind-the-scenes stories of ASEAN and world leaders has received strong support from readers after the book was published in These days. This is according to Mr. Puy Kea, the author of this book and a veteran journalist.
At a press conference on Friday afternoon, July 29, Puy Kea stated that he had spent 10 years compiling the book, which is more than 200 pages long. That is different from the books that have been published in the country. The title and cover of the book embody something until the reader has opened or read it and realized that it is inside.
"There are a lot of stories that have been leaked from major international meetings in the region and other countries, including stories about famous leaders of ASEAN and the world, especially life," he said. "Love, work habits, leadership attitudes and disagreements over some issues in the region, as well as territorial disputes."
