Samdech Techo Hun Sen and senior officials of the Communist Party of Vietnam agree to push the remaining 16 percent of the border post (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Mr. Do Van Chien, Secretary of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of Vietnam and Chairman The Central Committee of the Vietnam Fatherland Front has agreed to push up the remaining 16 percent of border posts.
The agreement was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen allowing a delegation of the Vietnam Fatherland Front led by Do Van Jian to pay a courtesy call and discuss bilateral relations on the occasion of the 55th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic ties between the two countries. Both on July 29, 2022 at the Peace Palace.
Regarding border demarcation and border demarcation with Vietnam, Cambodia has achieved 84% of the work progress and is working to negotiate to speed up the completion of this work as soon as possible.
In response, Do Van Jian expressed his pleasure at the visit, which is a good opportunity to strengthen relations between the two countries, the Front and the Party, and on that occasion, he brought greetings from the Vietnamese leadership. From the party president, from the president, from the Prime Minister of Vietnam to Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
He praised the measures taken by Samdech Techo Prime Minister and the Royal Government of Cambodia to successfully prevent the spread of Kovid, with regional and global vaccination rates and good results. And restored the economy.
In response, the Prime Minister thanked the Vietnamese Prime Minister and other Vietnamese leaders for bringing greetings to the Cambodian People's Party as well as the Cambodian people. Sangkat as well as wishes for the success of the upcoming parliamentary elections in 2023.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister as well as guests recalled the long journey that the two parties went through together to help each other, especially Samdech reminded of Samdech's struggle and the support of Vietnamese friends in helping to liberate Cambodia and prevent the return of the Khmer Rouge regime and subsequent aid.
Next year, the 45th anniversary of the founding of the Cambodian Army, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and relevant ministries will arrange for the repatriation of the remains of the remaining 49 Cambodian fighters to return to their homeland.
During the dialogue, the Prime Minister also congratulated Vietnam on its good management of the epidemic of smallpox so far in Vietnam, which has significantly decreased, and Samdech Techo took this opportunity. Congratulations to Vietnam for organizing a good SEA Games, which gives Cambodia the opportunity to win more medals and gain experience for organizing the 2023 SEA Games.
He expressed hope that the visit of the Vietnamese delegation would be a good time for a wide-ranging communication.
Finally, the head of the Vietnamese delegation wished Samdech good health and wished him success in his role as chair of ASEAN in 2022 and wished Cambodia success in organizing the SEA Games in The coming 2023 will be successful.
Finally, Samdech Techo Prime Minister asked him to bring greetings and wishes to the Vietnamese leadership, including the Party Secretary General, the President, the Prime Minister, good health and long life to continue to cooperate with each other. Better for the benefit of both countries.
