Discover China's technological advancement
BEIJING: Over the past decade, China's science and technology sector has made significant progress, with China rising to 12th place in the global rankings of innovative countries. The highest in 2021, which in 2012, China ranked 20th on the list.
These outstanding achievements are not accidental, but these achievements are the result of good leadership and effective planning and policy implementation of the Chinese government, combined with the active participation of the Chinese government. Active from all stakeholders, such as the Chinese private sector and people, as well as the favorable conditions of China's strong economic structure.
China's technological advances not only benefit China itself, but also greatly benefit the whole world, especially developing countries. Developing countries need new technologies to accelerate their economic and social development, and China has the ability to produce and supply such technologies to developing countries at affordable prices.
Article by Prof. Dr. Nak Chendarith, Director of the Cambodian Center for 21st Century Maritime Silk Road Research at the Royal University of Phnom Penh Senior Official, Ministry of Environment: The situation of natural resource conservation has improved, Cambodia continues to expand the carbon credit market in the market International Volunteers
(Mondulkiri): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, stated that the complete peace factor under the implementation of the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Prime Minister has given Cambodia full time and possibility to consider and strengthen To protect and conserve the remaining natural resources.
Currently, the conservation of natural resources is better, Cambodia has been successfully selling carbon credits in the international voluntary market since 2016, starting with the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary in Mondulkiri Province and the carbon credit project in the field. Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary has become a model for the implementation of carbon credit projects in other protected areas in Cambodia.
This statement was made by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment on the morning of July 28, 2022, while leading a group of journalists to understand the conservation work at the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary in Mondulkiri Province. .
Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary has been under the protection and conservation of the Ministry of Environment since 2016 with a total area of Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary is not only a dense wildlife sanctuary that can sell carbon credits, but also a protected area of international importance for wildlife conservation and biodiversity.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment said that the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary is of international importance in the conservation of Asian elephants, reptiles, including yellow-cheeked vultures, white-tailed monkeys, horned frogs, ostriches and many species of birds. 75 species of endangered species are on the IUCN Red List.
Ms. Chhay Kim Hiek, Head of the Red + Keo Seima Community Unit of WCS, which is implementing a joint project with the Mondulkiri Provincial Department of Environment of the Ministry of Environment, said that for 2022, the community at Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary will receive $ 600,000 from Sales of carbon credits in the voluntary market tripled compared to 2021.
"For 2022, the proceeds from the sale of carbon credits in the voluntary market shared to the community in Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary will increase from 200,000 in 2021 to $ 600,000," she said. "It has tripled compared to 2021, with 20 villages divided according to their scores for participating in the protection of natural resources."
Phnom Penh Municipal Police Prepares Nearly 600 Personnel to Maintain Security and Order at the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Municipal Police has organized a total of nearly 600 police forces to protect security, order and facilitate traffic at the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting (AMM) to be held from July 29 to August 6, 2022 This is according to Colonel San Sok Seiha, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, who confirmed to Fresh News on July 29.
Lt. Col. San Sok Seiha confirmed that on July 29, 2022, Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Commissioner of the Phnom Penh Municipal Commission, chaired a meeting to disseminate the plan for security, order and traffic in the Ministerial Meeting. The 55th ASEAN Overseas (AMM) at the Phnom Penh Municipal Commission.
Colonel San Sok Seiha said, “During that meeting, Lt. Gen. Thet decided to organize a total of nearly 600 police forces, such as the intervention force, the police force at the district police inspectorate and the administrative police station, traffic police force, and law enforcement force to "Cooperate to protect security, order and facilitate traffic during the AMM meeting."
The spokesman added that Lt. Gen. Thet had made strong recommendations to all forces in the above areas to work together to implement the plan with great care to ensure security, traffic order. To facilitate the delegation of ASEAN Foreign Ministers attending the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting (AMM) and related meetings to be held in Phnom Penh.
What Lt. Gen. Thet emphasized was to enhance the image of Cambodia on the occasion of hosting the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting (AMM) from July 29 to August 6, 2022. In the near future.
