Minister of Public Works instructs students at the Royal School of Administration to be leaders
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of the Royal School of Administration, gave a lecture on "Innovative and Qualitative Leadership in Public Administration" to the 12th Generation Senior Officials and 2022 Interns. Royal School of Administration.
* 1: Leadership means the use of formal or informal power in orienting and coordinating work with others. He explains that official authority when a person is appointed or delegated. But he stressed that if there is only official power but no informal power, it is not certain to lead them. As for the term informal power, he tried to explain a lot about how to build relationships.
* 2: Leadership means another person who influences a group of people to achieve a goal. It is in this sense that he warns that there is only power but no influence, because if a leader instructs them, it is not easy to use power improperly, they do not listen.
He said that from 1992 to 2021, the Royal School of Administration trained students, senior officials, intermediate students, Kramakar staff, interns, senior officials, administrative officers, intermediate officials, kramakars, as well as short-term trainees and new officers. A total of 16,606 people (3,807 females or 23%).
