(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia plans to re-organize the "Interfaith Forum" after a two-year absence due to the Kovid 19 crisis. This program is ready to be held in early September 2022 at the Koh Pich Center and Exhibition under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
This was stated by Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice President of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NEC) during a meeting to discuss the organization of the 6th Inter-Forum Forum at the Ministry of Interior on July 28, 2022
Every year since 2017, the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking, chaired by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, has been collaborating with major religious leaders in Cambodia to organize interfaith forums to pray for the people. Cambodians, as well as the people of the world, are blessed with freedom from the abuses and human trafficking of modern parliament.
The importance of this program is to show the harmony of religion in Cambodia, which always agrees to cooperate and support each other with gentleness, without conflict, without quarreling, without causing division and disaster in society, on the contrary. The harmony of religion has played a key role in building individual peace of mind and social security, as well as helping to strengthen the spirit of all, to work together to overcome the incitement of human trafficking criminals.
Ms. Chou Bun Eng said, "In Cambodia, we have a religious harmony that makes it possible to organize interfaith forums, while some countries in the world can not organize interfaith forums. In the past, some countries also praised the harmony of religion in Cambodia.
Interfaith forums are often organized on a large scale, with religious leaders attending religious ceremonies at the same time, at the same place, with the same goal, and with the participation of government officials. A lot of people.
