On this occasion, Mr. Do Van Chien congratulated Cambodia on its success in organizing the 5th Mandate Commune / Sangkat Council Election. At the same time, he praised the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia in launching effective measures to prevent Kovid-19 disease successfully.
Do Van Chien praised the growing friendship and cooperation between the two countries, which has grown steadily despite the difficult circumstances of the global Kovid-19 epidemic. He noted that the trade volume between Cambodia and Vietnam reached 9 billion US dollars by 2021 and hoped to reach 12 billion US dollars by 2022.
At the same time, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin considered that the presence of the delegation of the Vietnam Fatherland Front at this time shows the continuation of the traditional friendship, solidarity and good cooperation between the two countries that have existed for a long time, especially Between the United Front for the Development of the Motherland of Cambodia and the Vietnam Fatherland Front for the better.
In addition, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin praised the excellent cooperation in all fields between the governments of the two countries for the benefit of both nations, including the achievement of significant bilateral trade growth. Notably, the two countries have recently successfully cooperated in the fight against Kovid 19, reopening the country and resuming economic and tourism activities.
On that occasion, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin expressed his congratulations on the achievement of the Memorandum of Understanding on the Cooperation Program between the Front of Cambodia, Vietnam and Laos for the period 2020-2023. Samdech is optimistic that Cambodia-Vietnam will continue to implement this Memorandum of Understanding into practical activities and achievements for the benefit of both nations.
Mr. HUN Manet: The older Ream generation is a role model for the younger generation because it is a generation full of hope, vision and perseverance (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Dr. HUN Manet, senior official of the Cambodian People's Party and As the candidate for the future Prime Minister of Cambodia, the senior Ream generation is a role model for the younger generation because it is a generation full of hope, vision and perseverance.
In a video posted on Facebook on Friday morning, July 29, 2022, Mr. HUN Manet expressed his admiration for the struggle, dedication, courage and long-term vision of the Cambodian leaders. Young people during the national liberation struggle from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
Mr. HUN Manet emphasized that because of this clear vision, the younger generation can liberate the nation, prevent the return of the Khmer Rouge and build a prosperous country like today.
The history of Cambodia shows that under the forces of the United Front for National Salvation, with the support of the Vietnamese army, defeated the Khmer Rouge regime to liberate the country on January 7, 1979. After conquering the country, the Khmer Rouge army continued to fight for control of the country, a difficult time of the Cambodian regime, while many Vietnamese experts were working in Cambodia.
That period was a difficult time for the Khmer leaders of that generation, with one hand having to resist the return of the Khmer Rouge, with the other hand striving to build a national society and ensure the survival of the people.
Mr. Hun Manet also highlighted that if the young people of that generation did not have a clear and long-term vision, the Khmer Rouge could take back the country or Vietnam could lead Cambodia, because then all the skills were Vietnamese, because Cambodia had to lose all the rich Knowledge during the Khmer Rouge regime.
"By this time, Vietnam has already led all institutions, because we do not have the vision to build our strength, we do not have the vision to strengthen the country's ability to become an independent country," Hun Manet said.
