He stressed that the provision of compensation and cash implementation to poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19 was made without discrimination on the basis of political affiliation. Real poverty. And the assessment of any family is not done by any individual, it is done by an automated machine.
Keo Bopha, a representative of the railway community, said that she was currently applying for an equity card for 36 of the more than 80 families in her community, who had already been interviewed by the authorities. She said that she had just applied for the equity card because she had never known the information and benefits of the card before.
She expects that the poor and the sick will be evaluated to receive this card for free use in the hospital and with the support of the Royal Government.
As of July 2022, there are more than 680,000 poor families in and out of Phnom Penh and in the countryside, with a total of more than 2.7 million members, and are receiving support from the program. Cash for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19, a social assistance program of the Royal Government, which was officially launched on June 24, 2020.
Mr. Theng Panhathan, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of Planning of the Ministry of Planning, said that compared to June 2020, in 2022, the number of cardholders has increased significantly, which is around 2,000. Family per month.
