Commentary: Vesak is an important opportunity for monks to learn dharma, rules and regulations.
(Phnom Penh): "Bon Vesa" is a major festival of Buddhism and can be considered as one of the most important festivals in Buddhism, as it is also a law of God. The Buddha required all monks who practiced the religion to wait for the rainy season in each pagoda for three months, according to the Buddha's precepts, from the 1st day of the month of Asat to the 15th day of the month of Assoch.
Every year, on the day of the "Vesa Festival", the Khmer people, who are pure Buddhists, prepare relics and other food items to support the monks and use them during the rainy season. For this year 2022, the "Rainy Day Festival" will take place from the 1st day of the month of Asat on the 14th of July - until the 15th day of the month of Assoch on the 10th of October 2022.
His Excellency Nhean Phoeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Cults and Religions and a member of the National Festival Organizing Committee, told Cambodia-China Friendship Radio that the three-month rainy season is an important opportunity for monks to strengthen their knowledge and discipline and rules:
Please note that this period of remembering the rain for 3 months is a period of special value because it is a sign to awaken the Buddhist clergy to increase their efforts to fulfill their vows, vipassana business more than ever. As for the devotees, the devotees also saw clearly the content of remembering the rain of the monks.
That is why they try so hard to support the monks in various ways, such as: Candles, oil, saddak, Dak Ben, Pchum Ben, to express their sympathy, to share the hardships and to be full of benefits for themselves. That too.
Communities at Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary Receive $ 600,000 from Carbon Loan Sale
(Phnom Penh): Under the commitment and policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia to protect its natural resources, including the Ministry of Environment, Cambodia has become one of the leading countries in Southeast Asia in the sale of carbon credits on the market. Volunteer.
For 2022, the community at Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary will receive $ 600,000 from the sale of carbon credits in the volunteer market, a threefold increase compared to 2021.
Ms. Chhay Kim Hiek, Head of Red Cross Keo Seima Community Unit of WCS, said, “For 2022, the proceeds from the sale of carbon credits in the voluntary market shared to the community in Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary will increase from 200,000. "In 2021 to 600,000 US dollars, which is three times more than in 2021, with the division of 20 villages according to their points to participate in the protection of natural resources."
According to Ms. Chhay Kimheak, for the implementation of the REDD + project, a large part of the budget was allocated directly to the local community for management by the organization, opened a bank account and set up a committee for budget management with the help. Coordinated by WCS to develop their base.
Meanwhile, Mr. Net Pheaktra added that the benefits of the REDD + project at the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary have benefited 20 villages, each of which receives between $ 10,000 and $ 10,000 a year. However, for 2022, the sale of carbon credits in the voluntary market amounted to $ 600,000, increasing the amount of money that each village receives through activities and income from the sale of carbon credits.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued that REDD + project provides benefits: reduce forest loss, reduce biodiversity loss, improve the livelihood of local communities through the use of REDD + benefit allocation budget to supplement the investment plan budget. Commune. The REDD + project is internationally recognized.
The Ministry of Environment has been cooperating with the Wildlife Conservation Society of Cambodia (WCS) to implement the REDD + project since 2016, since the Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary was transferred to the Ministry of Environment.
