The 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings within the ASEAN framework will start tomorrow
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia on July 28, 2022 issued an official statement that Cambodia, as the chair of ASEAN, will begin to host the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting. And related meetings within the ASEAN framework from July 29 to August 5, 2022 in Phnom Penh.
The 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings include:
* Meeting of the ASEAN Nuclear Non-Proliferation Commission * Meeting between ASEAN Foreign Ministers and Representatives of the ASEAN Intergovernmental Commission on Human Rights * 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers * Post-ASEAN Meeting of Foreign Ministers with ASEAN Dialogue Partners * 23rd ASEAN Plus Three Foreign Ministers 'Meeting * 12th Asia-East Asia Summit Foreign Ministers' Meeting * 29th ASEAN Regional Forum Meeting
On the occasion of the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting, there will be three separate tripartite meetings between Cambodia and the ASEAN Secretariat, with three ASEAN dialogue partners including Norway, Turkey and Switzerland.
In addition to the ASEAN Sectoral Dialogue Partners and the six countries that are members of the Treaty of Amity and Cooperation in Southeast Asia (TAC), the other four countries will be invited as guests of the 2022 ASEAN Chairmanship. Papua New Guinea, Morocco, East Timor and Azerbaijan.
During the 55th AMM and related meetings, Cambodian Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, is expected to hold a number of bilateral meetings with his foreign counterparts.
