Offending drivers ready! Koy Sodani, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, stated that the program to deduct the driving license of the offender will be launched from September (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport, in collaboration with the Ministry of Interior, may start implementing the revocation of driving licenses of offenders from September 2022.
Ms. Koy Sodany said, "The Ministry of Public Works and Transport, in collaboration with the Ministry of Interior, has organized a program to deduct points for the revocation of driving licenses, which we have set up to 12 points, which may start. "Implemented from September only, do not require drivers to bring along the road is a driver's license."
Ms. Koy Sodany further stated that the three important documents to be attached when driving on the road include: vehicle ID card, vehicle driver's license and technical inspection certificate (check), which will help confirm the driver driving. In accordance with the law that requires the original, without allowing the use of copies.
Please be informed that in relation to this program to deduct driving license points, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has stated that from 2022 onwards, the Ministry will not allow drivers to break the law to pay and be released. As an additional penalty measure, the Ministry will create a new app to record the score according to the number of mistakes of the driver, if the mistake is repeated many times, the driver's license will be revoked.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol further stated that when implementing a vehicle that violates the law, law enforcement officers will apply for a driver's license and scan this program on the driver's license. . Once the score is deducted, the driver's license will no longer be valid.
The senior minister continued that for drivers who break the law, it is not a claim that they have paid and is free, it is a fine and will deduct extra points to not be able to use the driver's license. According to the Minister, the withdrawal within 6 months or 1 year according to the law.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol further stated that the driver violated the law and deducted 12 points, the driver's license will no longer be valid.
