(Kampong Speu): Prey Vihear Farmers 'Agricultural Community Market, which is a gathering place for farmers' agricultural products, has been officially launched to meet the basic needs of farmers who need a place to sell agricultural products.
Nhem Sareth, Country Director of Heifer International Cambodia, says that once the farming community is able to build and own the agricultural community market, they will be able to manage the community-level marketing system as a driving force for mobilization. Innovation and distribution of agricultural products from family farms to a wide range of markets.
He said that the market will help solve the challenges of farmers, producers and farming communities in the collection and transportation of agricultural products such as chickens, broilers, meat, vegetables, etc. From its members to marketers or buyers in the community.
"Indeed, the role of the agricultural community market is to be a hub and have many other functions, such as a business forum between producers, buyers, collectors and the agricultural community for doing business in collecting, selling and distributing," he added. "In key places and markets."
According to the country director of Heifer International Cambodia, Prey Vihear Farmers' Community Agricultural Market will be able to earn at least $ 600 to $ 800 per month for the first two years.
It should also be noted that Prey Vihear Farmers' Agricultural Community Market has set up 19 stalls for rent and sale of agricultural products to farmers and producers who are members of the agricultural community.
