Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum Receives a Scholarship Winner to Study in Japan
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of Cambodia, this morning, July 28, 2022, allowed 24 successful candidates for the Japan Scholarship for Human Resource Development in Cambodia (JDS). Continuing to study in Japan for the academic year 2022-2023, pay a courtesy call to receive the recommendation from Samdech at the Senate.
The President of the Senate instructed all female candidates during their studies in Japan to pay attention to the implementation of a number of issues, such as: respecting and strictly enforcing all laws and regulations of the respective countries. Both school rules and regulations.
It should be noted that these 24 female candidates are civil servants working in the ministries and institutions of the Royal Government who have passed the scholarship examination to study in Japan for a two-year master's degree for the academic year 2022-2023. Development of public administration, economy, technology, jurisprudence, international relations, quality of education, health, clean water, strengthening of rural areas, strengthening of agriculture and governance skills.
Recently, four political parties submitted a joint petition to the National Assembly and declared their opposition to the 10th Amendment to the Constitution. The petition alleges that the amendment severely undermined the parliamentary system, reducing the power of the National Assembly, bypassing the National Assembly in appointing a prime minister who empowers political parties outside the National Assembly to make direct proposals. The King appoints an elite Prime Minister.
According to Mr. Keut Rith, this statement is incorrect, it is not clear and does not understand the true content of the process of amending the 10th Constitution and the system of governing the country under the parliamentary regime. He added that any amendment to the constitution is to fill the gaps in the constitution and to ensure the protection of the interests of the whole nation.
Mr. Keut Rith further stated that therefore, the 10th Amendment did not violate the power of the National Assembly to form the Royal Government through the parliamentary system, and the statement of the four parties that submitted the petition to the National Assembly was Incorrect and distorted from the actual content of Article 119 new (two), which is the subject of the request for amendment now.
The clarification of the Minister of Justice was made at the plenary session of the National Assembly this morning, July 28, 2022, to discuss and approve the draft Constitution on the proposed amendments to Article 19 (a), Article 89, Article 98 (new). Article 102 (new), Article 119 (one) and Article 125 (new) of the Constitution and Article 3 (new) and Article 4 (4) of the new Constitution, including four other agendas.
"This statement is just an additional echo of the words of analysts and some politicians or political parties," Keut Rith said.
He said that in particular, the amendment to fill the gaps of the Constitution and the guarantee of state institutions, especially the executive branch, has the main mission to lead the general work of the state, the process is running smoothly, not stuck. Sustainability in all circumstances to fulfill the mission of serving the best interests of the nation and the people of Cambodia.
He said the amendment was not made while Cambodia was in a state of emergency.
The Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, promulgated on September 24, 1993, has been amended 10 times, including this time. This amendment aims to ensure national sustainability as well as the national interests and the people of Cambodia.
The draft constitution on the amendment of the eight articles of the constitution and the constitution, which the Ministry of Justice presented, has the following detailed contents:
Article 89- New (As amended March 1999): At the request of at least one-tenth of the members, the National Assembly may invite one or more members of the Royal Government, accompanied by dignitaries who are experts in a particular field, to comment on the National Assembly on issues of special importance.
Article 98 (new): The National Assembly may remove a member of the Council of Ministers or remove the Royal Government from office by approving a motion of reprimand by an absolute majority of the total number of members of the National Assembly. In the event that the Royal Government is removed from office by the National Assembly, the Royal Government to be removed from this position will only have the task of leading the day-to-day work until a new Royal Government takes office.
The motion against the Royal Government was submitted to the National Assembly by one-third of the total number of members of the National Assembly so that the National Assembly could discuss it.
In the event of war or in other special circumstances where elections are not possible, the Senate may renew its term once a year at the request of the King.
The proclamation of the extension of the term of the Senate shall be decided by at least two-thirds of the total number of senators.
In the circumstances described above, the Senate meets daily on a regular basis. The Senate has the right to decide to terminate the above special circumstances if the situation allows. However, the decision to end the special circumstances in which the nation is in a state of emergency must be decided jointly by the National Assembly, the National Assembly and the Senate, except for the implementation of Article 86 of the Constitution.
If the Senate is unable to convene due to necessary reasons, especially when foreign forces occupy the territory, the declaration of a state of emergency shall proceed automatically.
Before taking office, the Council of Ministers shall be sworn in as stated in Annex 6.
At the end of each term of the National Assembly, the outgoing government has only the task of leading the day-to-day work until a new government takes office.
Article 125 (new): In the event that the Prime Minister is absent from time to time, the Prime Minister shall appoint a Deputy Prime Minister as the Acting Prime Minister to take charge of the Council of Ministers temporarily.
If the post of Prime Minister is permanently vacant due to the death or resignation of a new Council of Ministers, it shall be immediately appointed in accordance with the provisions of this Constitution. The President of the National Assembly shall convene an urgent meeting of the National Assembly and take any other necessary action as soon as possible within seven days after receiving a request from the party with the largest number of seats in the National Assembly.
In the event that the post of Prime Minister is permanently vacant due to the death of the Council of Ministers, which will be vacated under the leadership of the Deputy Prime Minister who has been appointed as the Acting Prime Minister, only the duties of directing the day-to-day work until A new cabinet takes office.
The resignation of the Prime Minister shall be made by a letter of resignation which shall be sent to the King and sent to the President of the National Assembly. In this case, the outgoing cabinet must continue to lead the work of the Royal Government until the new cabinet takes office.
Separately, the two articles of the Constitution are as follows:
The new Article 3 and Article 4 of the new Constitution, aimed at ensuring the normal functioning of national institutions, are amended as follows:
Article 3 (new): In the event that the procedure of the new Article 82 (one) and Article 119 (two) of the Constitution cannot be achieved at the request of the party with the largest number of seats in the National Assembly, it may proceed. Vote in a package to elect the President, Vice-President of the National Assembly, as well as the Chairman and Vice-Chairman of the Commission, at the same time giving confidence to the Royal Government.
Article 4 (New): The preparation of the list of components for election and trust shall be as follows:
The list of the President and Vice-Chairmen of the National Assembly, as well as the Chairmen and Vice-Chairmen of all the specialized committees of the National Assembly shall be prepared and proposed by the political party with the largest number of seats in the National Assembly and shall be sent to the senators of the National Assembly. The President of the National Assembly shall be elected from among the members of the National Assembly who have only Khmer nationality.
The members of the National Assembly are elected by determining the oldest member of the National Assembly. In the event that the National Assembly Senator is unable to perform his / her duties, the position of the National Assembly Senator shall be assigned to other senior members of the National Assembly in the following order.
