Stung Treng Municipality Organizes Public Forum on Consultation on Solid Waste Management and Services
(Stung Treng): In the morning of July 27, 2022, Stung Treng Municipality Administration organized a public forum on consultation on the management and provision of solid waste services in Stung Treng City in the presence of Mr. Say Kosal, Governor and Mr. Nin Sok. On the members of the Municipal Council, including the Board of Governors, Mr. and Mrs. Chairman, Deputy Director of the relevant departments and more than 400 people.
Mr. Say Kosal stated that the purpose of this public forum was to promote new mechanisms for solid waste management in Stung Treng and to listen to the challenges of the people and traders to find common solutions in waste management. And other waste to make Stung Treng city orderly and aesthetically pleasing.
He said that at present, solid waste in Stung Treng town is collected about 36 tons per day and 12,960 tons per year. Due to solid waste, the town has not yet been properly packaged and stored in accordance with the rules and standards of environmental hygiene.
In addition, a small number of people continue to dump rubbish on the streets and in public places by refusing to use the garbage service and not paying the garbage service fee, which affects the environment and affects people's health and livelihood. Daily air pollution, especially affecting the beauty of the village, commune, city and province as a whole.
The mayor added, however, that these challenges can be addressed by changing attitudes, lifestyles, businesses, producers and municipal waste disposal companies, as well as setting up and operating systems. Manage urban solid waste effectively.
He also confirmed that the president will continue to wear the mask for an additional 10 days to prevent the spread of the virus, and that he will conduct frequent tests to detect the recurrence of the virus.
