The Ministry of Interior will launch an operation to check the residence of foreigners in Cambodia, except for diplomats, to check the legality and find the traffickers (Video inside) (Central): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, said that the Ministry The Ministry of Interior will launch an operation to check the lives of all foreigners in Cambodia, except for diplomats, to check the legality and find the people involved in human trafficking.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng said this at the closing ceremony of the first generation of level 1 and level 2 police leaders at the Police Academy of Cambodia in Dei Edth commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province on July 26, 2022.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that in order to eliminate suspicions and loopholes in human trafficking, the Ministry of Interior must launch a large-scale operation to inspect the lives of all foreigners, whether in hotels, construction sites and companies, except Only diplomats. According to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, the Ministry will prepare a very thorough plan to find the target of human trafficking.
"Those who come to work at various construction sites, all investment companies must be inspected, and this inspection is not for any purpose, but to find out whether those who come to Cambodia are entering legally or not. In Cambodia, there is no labor law and find out who is the target of human trafficking. This is the confirmation of the Minister of Interior.
The United States on July 19, 2022 released the 2022 Report on Human Trafficking. In the report, the United States placed Cambodia, Vietnam, Macau, China and three other ASEAN countries on a watch list at Level 2 to Level 3, commonly known as blacklist, which is a bad level. The United States alleges that Cambodia and those countries made little effort and did not adhere to the standards of eliminating human trafficking.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Chairman of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking, on July 23, 2022, issued the first reaction after the US State Department downgraded Cambodia to third place in the fight against human trafficking. At the inauguration ceremony of the school building in Kandal province, Samdech Krala Hom claimed that although Cambodia received such a ranking, it did not relax its work in eliminating human trafficking.
Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice Chair of the National Committee for Combating Trafficking in Persons (NEC), considered the US Government's report to have blacklisted the Royal Government of Cambodia. People are reports made without a clear basis.
