Mr. Tum Niro, Director of the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, advised farmers to change from raising family cows to semi-industrial cows to improve family livelihood, ensure quality, safety and hygiene that will provide benefits. Of artificial insemination, which saves both time and labor, high fertility rate and reduced infectious diseases.
Mr. Chea Thavrith, Deputy Governor of Stung Treng Province, said that the current vaccination of cattle is part of the prevention of other diseases, however, it also needs care from its cattle owners. . If there is a suspicion that the animals are infected, immediately report to the village veterinary agency, if any disease occurs, to avoid the spread of infectious diseases.
