(Kampot): Dr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Kampot Province, on July 26, 2022, called on the authorities and people living along the Cambodia-Vietnam border to plant palm trees to prove their national identity.
Such a call was made during the celebration of the 9th of July 2022, which was held in Prek Kris commune, Kampong Trach district, Kampot province.
At the same time, the provincial governor also reminded the authorities of the people in the country, especially the people in Kampot province who live in the border areas with friendly countries to know how to preserve this heritage as history for future generations. This action is also in response to the Royal Government's National Forest Policy Program, which has implemented forest sector reform and identified forest issues as a priority to restore and develop the nation.
The provincial governor said that the planting of saplings and palm seedlings on both sides of the Cambodia-Vietnam border in Prek Kris commune now shows the patriotic spirit to preserve and preserve the ancestral heritage, especially to preserve history for children. Later generations.
