The following is the Royal Decree of the King: The Department of Private Security Management continues to hold the 39th Private Security Agency Training Course to strengthen the quality to participate in maintaining security and social order.
(Phnom Penh): The Department of Private Security Management of the General Commission of the National Police this morning, July 27, 2022, continued to hold the 39th Private Security Agency Training Course under the chairmanship of Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Department of Private Security Management.
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey said that the opening of the private security agency training course was highly supported and cared for by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, and Lt. Gen. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner. And leaders at all levels.
He continued that the private security sector is a sector to contribute to maintaining security, order and safety for the society and is an important support force of the competent forces to prevent and suppress crimes and participate in the implementation of the policy "village-commune. "The neighborhood is safe."
Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey affirmed that the private security sector is inextricably linked. The private security sector must have high quality and benefits for the protection, security, safety and public order, so all private security agencies must have the capacity to understand And have a clear professionalism as a full-fledged private security agent.
Recently, the General Commission of the National Police, which has a private security management department as its staff, organized this training course with the main purpose of understanding the duties and obligations of the private security sector on maintaining security, order and strengthening the capacity of private security agencies. Aims to increase the effectiveness of social security protection.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Director of the Department also sincerely commended and encouraged all private security agencies to pay attention to protect, maintain security, safety, order, property, life of the people and participate in disseminating and implementing village policy. Safe communes, especially private security agencies, have joined the blockade of Phnom Penh to prevent Kovid 19 from causing major targets in the past.
Taking this opportunity, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey would also like to encourage private security agents stationed in condominiums, apartments, hotels, guesthouses, casinos, nightclubs to report drug offenses, kidnappings, human trafficking and other crimes. Others.
