The US space agency NASA and other international partners hope to continue operating the space station until 2030, as Russia is reluctant to commit beyond 2024.
The International Space Station is jointly owned by the Russian, US, European, Japanese and Canadian space agencies. The first fragments were launched into orbit in 1998, and the station has been in continuous operation for nearly 22 years. It is used to conduct scientific research in zero gravity and test instruments for future space travel.
Preah Vihear Provincial Authority announces the suspension of transit for all types of vehicles from the 5th Gopura flagpole to Poytadi of Preah Vihear temple
(Preah Vihear): The Administration of Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province, on July 26, 2022, issued a notification on the suspension of transit for all types of vehicles from the 5th Gopura flag to the Poytadi of Preah Vihear Temple. .
According to the announcement of the Choam Ksan District Administration, which was received by Fresh News this evening, it was confirmed that: "From the flagpole near the fifth gopura to Poytadi, there are landslides, deep potholes and slippery conditions that can eventually cause accidents when passing through."
In order to maintain the safety of the public and contribute to the promotion of the preservation of ancient infrastructure, which is a World Heritage Site, the Choam Ksan District Administration would like to announce the suspension of transit for all types of vehicles from the 5th Gopara flag point to Poytadi of Preah Vihear temple from the date of this announcement.
