Customs Commander orders strengthening tax collection on remaining duty-free vehicles and prepares for crackdown after July 31 deadline
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, on July 26, 2022, issued a letter to the Director of the Branch Department and the Office of Customs and Excise on strengthening efficiency. Of the collection of taxes and duties on existing duty-free vehicles in the remaining countries, especially the preparation of the upcoming campaign to crack down on duty-free vehicles.
To increase the efficiency of collecting taxes and duties on existing duty-free vehicles in the remaining countries, especially when the deadline for allowing duty-free right-hand drive car owners to come in to pay taxes or register is approaching. Kun Nhim advised the director of the branch department and the Customs and Excise Office as follows:
1. Must be widely disseminated to the public in their respective geographical responsibilities, the announcement of the ACC dated July 25, 2022.
2. Continue to provide tax and tax collection services, especially the registration of right-hand drive tax-free existing in the country to be more active and better. In case of need to extend the administrative time until 8:00 pm, including Saturday, Sunday and on July 30, 2022, which is the last day to allow the owner of the right duty-free car left to fulfill the tax obligations. Or the registration must be postponed until the closing time of the administrative time until 10:00 pm.
3. From August 1, 2022 onwards, all Customs and Excise units must mobilize and use appropriate forces to carry out an active and rigorous crackdown on all types of duty-free vehicles in all areas, such as public places, businesses and businesses. .
It should be informed that the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has allowed the owners of right-hand drive duty-free and existing duty-free vehicles in the remaining countries to come to pay the tax or register all of them with the deadline set by the 31st. July 2022.
The following is a letter from the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia: Minister of Commerce: As the chair of ASEAN, Cambodia launches a number of initiatives to promote ASEAN digital integration.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, emphasized that as the chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia has launched a number of initiatives to promote ASEAN digital integration.
"As chair of ASEAN in 2022, Cambodia has developed a number of initiatives to promote ASEAN digital integration, such as feasibility studies, technology transfer models for projects related to the SDGs, addressing challenges related to sustainability, and a framework for promoting the growth of ecosystems. "New digital business in ASEAN." This is the confirmation of Mr. Pan Sosak.
Minister Pan Sosak also expressed his belief that this workshop will provide a good opportunity for speakers and participants from government and private institutions to discuss and exchange ideas with each other to contribute to the integration of the digital economy in the ASEAN region. More comprehensive and environmentally friendly. Readers' views: "Are unions formed to protect factions or to protect the common good?"
(Phnom Penh): It is not new that some unions or associations and non-governmental organizations always act to protect the interests of the people within their jurisdiction or to protect individuals and groups as tools created by Opposition groups, especially those formed by foreigners for political, geopolitical and geopolitical purposes.
Why can they say that? Because NagaWorld decided to terminate the employment contracts of more than 300 employees due to the Kovid-19 crisis. This global crisis has lost tens of millions of jobs around the world. "Who can protest against a company layoffs?" "Certainly not."
The only legal way to protest, in any democracy, is to ask companies to comply with the terms of the contract termination by paying benefits to terminated employees. If the company agrees to provide compensation and benefits in accordance with the law, then the union has no reason to protest.
Last weekend, Chhim Sithor's faction members Yang Sophoan and Vorn Pov joined a demonstration with a handful of former NagaWorld employees and incited the protesters to break through the barricades angrily. Authorities allege violence against protesters. These tricks have been used for decades and are already well known.
In such a situation, should the authorities allow this group to continue to make rainstorms? Certainly not, because the authorities have a duty to protect the public interest, not to protect the interests of individuals, especially individuals and groups who engage in illegal activities.
On the other hand, if the authorities continue to be tolerant and allow such anarchic activities to continue, Cambodian society will not be happy.
Officials: Processing companies start to order a series of trout, ready to export the first 40 tons to China soon
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hav Viseth, Deputy Director General of Fisheries Administration, said that recently, fish processing companies in Cambodia are gradually ordering white fish to be processed for export to China according to the export plan. Initially, it was 40 tons.
Speaking to Fresh News on the afternoon of July 26, 2022, Mr. Hav Viseth confirmed that "the export of trout to China will start soon, obviously from last week until now, processing companies "Fish in Cambodia order a ton of white meat from aquaculture farms every day for processing and exporting to China."
He said that the order of less per ton per day is due to the processing company lack of manpower and less experts, if more orders will make processing not yet.
"For the first time, Cambodia plans to export 40 tonnes of trout to China," he said. Currently, the company is in a hurry to process all 40 tons of plans to export quickly, this is the first step in testing whether Cambodian trout are popular in China? "If there is a lot of support, Cambodia will increase the next step in exports."
Please be informed that the Chinese side has agreed and allowed the three trout farms that have been registered and registered with the Fisheries Administration to bring trout to China.
According to the Fisheries Administration, in 2021, Cambodia's aquaculture output totals more than 400,000 tons, of which trout yields about 30% to 40% of Cambodia's total aquaculture output.
Mr. Sok Raden, Chairman of the Board of the Cambodian Aquaculture Association, urged the farmers to raise fish to a good standard to meet the Chinese market, the water must be good, the fish must be good meat and Be standard.
The Kantha Bopha Foundation Support Committee of Cambodia in Phnom Penh decided to raise funds for Kantha Bopha Hospital through the use of QR Code
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has already decided to establish a committee to support the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia to help people who come to receive medical services at Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed that this meeting was held to raise funds to help Kantha Bopha Hospital by deciding to raise funds by using QR Code to place in various places in Phnom Penh, such as town, public service places. Citizens in companies, markets, hotels, restaurants, etc. to make it easier for people to participate in the budget by volunteering to support Kantha Bopha Hospital.
Mr. Khuong Sreng added that the Royal Government paid close attention to this work until all the capital-provincial authorities set up this fund to help Kantha Bopha Hospital, while this hospital has played an important role in helping the people. Poor people in all provincial capitals throughout Cambodia.
The Governor of Phnom Penh emphasized that this work must be done voluntarily and without coercion, so the Khan authorities as well as all relevant units must take care to implement it is not forced by individuals. Each. Must continue to disseminate this work more deeply to subordinates as well as local people so that they can volunteer to support Kantha Bopha Hospital.
The Support Committee of the Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia in Phnom Penh has the role and task of disseminating, calling and inspiring the movement to mobilize donations from officials at all levels under the administration of Phnom Penh to support the operation of Kantha Bopha Hospital.
On July 26, 2022, the CDC and the Singapore Business Federation (SBF), supported by the Embassy of Singapore in Cambodia and the Embassy of Cambodia in Singapore, organized a workshop on Cambodia: "Understanding Business Opportunities in Cambodia".
"As of June 2022, 127 Singaporean investment projects have been approved by the Council for the Development of Cambodia and are in operation," the CDC said in a statement. "Projects in tourism, manufacturing, infrastructure and other sectors totaling 1.53 billion US dollars."
This workshop is organized with the participation of
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary-General of the CDC, thanked Singaporean investors and business people for choosing Cambodia to invest in the past.
"The investment environment in Cambodia is favorable as a solid foundation for Singaporean investment to seize the overwhelming opportunities in agriculture, food, services and manufacturing," he said. "Singapore investment in Cambodia is very important. Please call for more investment from potential Singaporean investors who will contribute to the rapid recovery and development of the Cambodian economy."
The Minister emphasized the importance of the Investment Law of Cambodia, which was adopted in October 2021, which encourages investors to implement a responsible business environment and investment and business environment. Its day.
Mr. Sok Khoeun, Cambodian Ambassador to Singapore, outlined the Economic Diplomacy Strategy 2021-2023, which was launched in early 2021, with the aim of promoting trade, investment, tourism and culture in order to contribute to national economic development and promote Cambodia in the arena. Regional and international.
"Cambodian diplomats have been working and strengthening their efforts to promote and implement this economic diplomacy strategy to attract more investment and tourists to Cambodia," he said.
