New water station worth more than 110,000 USD to supply more than 500 families in Stong district, Kampong Thom province has been put into operation
(Kampong Thom): The Prum Srey Community Water Supply Station, worth more than $ 110,000, was officially inaugurated to supply the needs of more than 500 families in three villages in Rong Roeung Commune, Stong District, Kampong Thom Province.
The inauguration ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Say Kim Lam, Governor of Stong District on July 26, 2022 in Prum Srey Village, Rong Roeung Commune, Stong District, Kampong Thom Province.
According to the report, Prum Srey Community Water Supply Station can supply water to 3 villages: Prum Srey, Svay Rieng and Kantong Rong with a total of 524 households.
According to the same report, the construction of this water station is under the support of World Vision, with a total budget of 405,789,400 Riels, including the contribution of the Department of Rural Development of Kampong Thom Province 14,000,000 Riels and Another community budget of 50,789,400 riels, a total of 470,578,800 riels, equivalent to more than 117,600 US dollars.
Addressing the people, Mr. Say Kim Lam said that the achievement of clean water now because the country has developed in all areas from urban to rural and also because the country is completely peaceful under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun The Prime Minister of Cambodia will have the full support of World Vision.
At the same time, Mr. Say Kilam called on all families to use clean water for everyone, in which the Rongroeurng commune administration must pay attention to providing clean water to all of them, especially poor families and widows. And vulnerable families.
