The first ASEAN Youth Dialogue focuses on discussions to prepare for the future of new youth jobs
(Siem Reap): The first ASEAN Youth Dialogue hosted by Cambodia ended on July 26. The meeting focused on youth discussions in preparation for a new job in the fourth generation of the Industrial Revolution.
The Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron, said in a press conference after the first ASEAN Youth Dialogue on the afternoon of July 26, 2022, that this dialogue is a discussion on ASEAN issues that provide opportunities. Young people know about issues related to how young people can participate, how to build the ASEAN community, etc.
Mr. Hang Chuon Naron added that how can young people participate in policy making for the benefit of young people, especially in relation to the Industrial Revolution 4.0, which requires readiness, especially in relation to 21st century technology, how education should respond? In particular, providing opportunities for young people recommended for the leadership of ASEAN ministers to consider.
At the same time, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron also urged ASEAN youth to prepare for new job opportunities in the fourth generation of the Industrial Revolution. Those technologies will kill old jobs and emerge new ones that we could not have anticipated.
According to the ASEAN Youth Ministers, eight recommendations have been made to ASEAN leaders, including on governance, science, technology and innovation, job creation for the future, and infrastructure. Fifth, environmental growth; sixth, climate change; seventh; narrowing the development gap; ASEAN;
Please be informed that the ASEAN Youth Dialogue was held for 2 days, on July 25 and 26, 2022 at Sokha Hotel, Siem Reap. The meeting was funded by the Republic of Korea. In addition to the ASEAN youth, there were also about 300 Korean youths in total. Summary of important news events for July 26, 2022
