(Koh Kong): An intervention police officer from the Royal Cambodian Police Inspectorate, Keo Panha, drove drunk and hit a motorbike, killing a girl and seriously injuring her mother while she was being treated at the Koh Kong Provincial Referral Hospital. The incident happened on the night of July 24, 2022, and the perpetrator tried to drive and remove the license plate to escape.
The victim, Chhang Chanit, 38, (severely injured) and Phoeun Dara, a 12-year-old girl, died in Stung Veng village, Stung Veng commune, Khemarak Phoumin city.
Mr. Preung Sarath, a representative of the victim's family, said that his family's case has not yet received justice, so he demanded justice from lawyers and relevant authorities at all levels to help provide justice. And compensation in the form of emotional compensation for damage to their families.
He said that after receiving the disaster on his family, he seemed very shocked and deeply saddened by the loss of his lovely daughter, who lived with him and took care of his grandmother. Severe physical illness as well. During the evening care of his grandmother, Mr. Dup's wife went for a walk, but she should not have had such an unfortunate accident.
It should be noted that for two days now, the news of the traffic accident that caused the deaths and serious injuries has been closed without any news, but only leaked to the media today.
Yus Chanvichet, Royal Cambodian Police Inspectorate, said he was working on the case and that the perpetrators had been caught. The Royal Cambodian Police Inspector said that it is now possible to find a solution for the families of the victims to pay compensation in order to be able to restore the economy, livelihood and traditional festivals.
Separately, to the question of whether the perpetrator can be released from legal punishment in addition to the compensation already paid? The inspector did not respond via telegram.
