Minister of Commerce: Effective implementation of competition law will create a level playing field
(Phnom Penh): The Competition Committee of Cambodia (CPC) held its first meeting for all members to meet and appear after the Royal Government issued a decision on July 14. Ago. The meeting on the morning of July 26 of the Cambodian Competition Committee is also to review and discuss the internal regulations on the work regime and some other related work.
The meeting was held at the Ministry of Commerce under the chairmanship of Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the CPP. Also invited by the leaders and members of the KPR. Many.
Minister Pan Sosak congratulated the members of the CPP. Newly appointed and expressed optimism about the opening of this first meeting, which marks the beginning of the implementation of the law on competition in Cambodia.
The Law on Cambodian Competition was promulgated by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 1021/013, dated October 05. 2021.
The competition committee consists of a total of 15 members, 10 of whom are representatives from relevant ministries and institutions and 5 are independent individuals (one former judge, two economists and two lawyers) who pass the selection process. This committee consists of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud "KPR". As a staff to allow the CEC Gain full rights to perform their roles and responsibilities.
In front of the members of the Competition Committee of Cambodia, Mr. Pan Sosak stressed that the effective implementation of the law on competition will create a level playing field for doing business in Cambodia to compete through various means, including Innovating high quality and low prices of products and services that benefit consumers and boost the national economy.
In this morning's meeting, the meeting agreed to approve the internal regulations on the working regime of the CEC. For members of the CPP Implemented work effectively and continued to discuss other matters in the next meeting. A senior official of the Ministry of Culture reminds that all literary and artistic works created are automatically protected.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Long Pon Siriwat, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, stated that all literary and artistic works that are created are automatically protected.
A senior official of the Ministry of Culture said this at a seminar on copyright and related rights on the protection of intellectual property and dispute resolution mechanisms held at the Ministry on July 25, 2022.
As a party to the Bern Convention, Cambodia also requests "B" the right to resolve disputes without resorting to the International Court of Justice (ICJ) mechanism for resolving disputes of infringement, that is, in order to protect the outcome. The interests of Cambodia, which are in the process of enforcing copyright and similar rights on behalf of less developed countries.
At the same time, all dispute resolution mechanisms for the violation of the use of works are resolved in two main ways: (1) the non-judicial dispute resolution mechanism is a coordinated work with the Department of Copyright and Related Rights of the Ministry. Culture and Fine Arts as a staff has been implemented in the past and (secondly) the mechanism of settlement of court proceedings in case the owner or the plaintiff can not coordinate.
Today, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, the founder of the Law on Copyright and Related Rights, has successfully resolved and mediated a number of disputes, including domestic and foreign disputes, under a win-win political mechanism to reduce settlement. By the judiciary to maintain cultural harmony under one roof of peace.
Please be informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia has warned all creators of works of art against plagiarism without permission because it is related to legal issues. This was stated by Mrs. Kittisangkhab Dr. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the 24th National Cultural Day, March 3, 2022 at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall.
