NEC Announces the Application and Registration of National, International Observers and Political Party Agents
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued a notification on the submission and receipt of applications for registration of national and international observers and political party agents for voter registration and voter registration. Election 2022.
Through the announcement received by Fresh News on July 26, 2022, the NEC has informed all national and international NGO associations and political parties on the submission and receipt of applications. Register the following national and international observers and agents of political parties:
First, the submission and receipt of applications for registration of national observers
* The deadline for submitting and receiving applications for registration as a National Observer is from September 20, 2022 to February 11, 2023.
* Associations or non-governmental organizations wishing to participate in the observation must complete the application form for registration of observers and must submit their application for registration of observers at the NEC office every working hour from 7:00 to 11:30 and afternoon from 14:00 to 17:30 (Office of Political Parties and Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations, 9th floor).
* National observers who have been officially recognized and authorized by the NEC and have received the National Observer ID card from the Capital-Provincial Election Secretariat (CEC) and have the right to observe the census process. And the 2022 Voter Registration in the capital-province where it is named in the list of national observers of that capital-province.
Second: Submission and receipt of applications for registration of international observers
The application deadline for registration as an international observer is from September 20, 2022 to February 18, 2023.
* International NGOs wishing to participate in the observation must complete the application form for the registration of observers and must submit their application for registration of observers at the NEC office every working hour from 7:00 am: 00 minutes to 11:30 and afternoon from 14:00 to 17:30 (Office of Political Parties and Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations, 9th floor).
International observers who have been officially recognized and authorized and have received an international observer ID card from the NEC have the right to observe the entire voter list and voter registration process in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The NEC confirmed that the submission and receipt of applications for registration of political party agents
* The application for registration as an agent of a political party must be signed by the chairman or representative of the political party who has received a written transfer from the president of the political party. This transfer does not allow the transfer of rights, except in the letter of transfer that contains the content allows for the transfer of rights.
* The deadline for submitting and receiving applications for registration of political party agents is from October 13, 2022 to February 11, 2023.
* A registered political party in accordance with the Law on Political Parties has the right to appoint some of its agents as required by the party to observe the examination of the voter list and voter registration at the commune / sangkat halls and at the commune voter registration offices. Sangkats determined by the NEC.
Political parties must apply for registration as an agent to the Commune / Sangkat Council (ECCC) on Form 1007, which is provided free of charge. A political party can make a copy of Form 1007 to be used in applying for registration of its political party agent.
The NEC hopes that the Association of National, International Non-Governmental Organizations, Political Parties, the CPP and the CPC will work together to promote the 2022 voter list review and registration. Successful.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications (MPTC) on July 26, 2022, issued a new notice to stop the use of devices to increase service capacity or expand services that have a serious impact on mobile services (Video inside) (Phnom Penh). One by stopping the use of devices to increase service capacity or expand services that have a significant impact on mobile services.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications would like to request all citizens who are using service boosters and / or service expansion devices to dismantle, remove and stop using these devices at home.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications also urges all stakeholders to immediately stop the import of service boosters and / or expansions of all types that are not recognized by the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia to avoid legal action.
At the same time, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has been urging mobile operators to exchange equipment and technology, as well as build additional antenna stations to expand coverage and improve service quality.
The Ministry urges all citizens and stakeholders to cooperate to improve the quality of mobile phone service.
