3,000 Mangrove Trees Planted in Kep Province to Celebrate International Day for Mangrove Ecosystem Conservation
(Kep): To celebrate the International Day for the Conservation of Mangrove Ecosystems, July 26, 2022, the Ministry of Environment, Kep Provincial Administration and Vonfertity (Vital) Co., Ltd. have jointly organized 3,000 mangrove tree planting events in Phum Thmey Fishing Community, Sangkat Prey Thom Krong. Kep, Kep Province, in order to promote sustainability and environmental awareness and participate in the restoration of mangrove forests along the coast of Cambodia.
This event is expected to be an important message to cultivate citizens to love the environment and participate in the conservation of natural resources even more.
Attending this important event were Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Som Piseth, Governor of Kep Province, Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, General Director of OneFrternity (Vital) Company, Mrs. Vital and hundreds of new fishing community members.
The mangrove planting event is part of Vital's third year of large-scale social activities in collaboration with the Ministry of Environment and the Kep Provincial Administration under the umbrella of the 25R Fund, which has a minute to give back to society and part of The foundation is to contribute to the development of Cambodia to be greener for the present and future generations, in line with the theme "Mangroves promote the fresh source of nature".
Mr. Som Piseth praised and appreciated Vital's initiative and thanked for choosing Kep for this project.
At the same time, the provincial governor also encouraged all departments as well as the general public in the province to continue to participate in planting more mangrove to ensure the protection of the environment and improve the beauty of the green city.
He added that the provincial authorities "have been paying close attention to environmental protection, conservation of natural resources to prevent climate change, global warming, drought, floods and other natural disasters, especially the use of natural resources." "For a long time."
