On that occasion, Mr. Kay Numa also thanked Samdech Techo Ministry of Health officials, all volunteer doctors who took care to help Minibia workers to survive the spread of Kovid 19 disease. Of the more than 6,000 workers, only 78 were infected with Kovid 19. More importantly, even during the Kovid 19 epidemic, his factory was operating normally, with no production and supply chain failures.
