Mother and child riding a motorbike crashed into a pond, killing two and leaving one dead
(Siem Reap): A mother and her son were riding in a motorbike taxi when the steering wheel fell into an ancient pond and was restored, causing two people to drown. This incident happened at almost 11 am on July 24, 2022 at Trapeang Slaket pond, 6 meters deep, in Phum Prayuth, Sangkat Teuk Vil, Siem Reap City, Siem Reap Province.
The victims who died in this incident were: 30-year-old Thuong Chier, a housewife, and 9-year-old Thong Sovanpanha.
Dam Thieng, the 63-year-old father of the victim, described that on July 24, 2022, he heard his daughter tell him that he wanted a bamboo tree to build a fence around the house to attach to the net and went out to cut bamboo. To the east of the house is about 600 meters.
When the nephew went home first, the victim got on a motorcycle taxi with her two children back home. Suddenly, at the point of Slaket pond, which is an ancient pond that has just been restored, in Phum Prayuth, Sangkat Teuk Vil, Siem Reap province, the driver of the motorbike fell into the pond.
After the motorcycle fell into a pond, a child sitting in front of it got ashore and ran to tell his grandfather and grandmother about the incident. The victim's father searched but could not find him. It was not until 10:30 that the authorities and the people were surprised to help search, but still did not find until 12 o'clock to find the body.
The victim's father said that in the past, his daughter was a very good person, since she had a family break up with her husband, she felt uncomfortable because of the pressure from her husband, even to visit relatives. He never went, which made him think a lot, not eat or drink. She was later taken to a hospital, where doctors said her son was overthinking, causing stress and combining with her husband.
