Heavy rain inundates Suong market in Tbong Khmum province, but does not damage traders' equipment
(Tbong Khmum): A few days ago, in Tbong Khmum province, especially Suong city, there was a continuous rain, causing flooding in low-lying areas, fields, ponds, canals, and on the night of the 24th to the 25th, there was a continuous rain. Recently, it caused the flooding of Suong Market, but did not affect the equipment of the traders, just disturbed the people to enjoy a little business, but now the water is gradually receding.
Mr. Chea Naron, Governor of Suong City, said that in July, there was a lot of rain, which caused the low-lying areas to be full of water, such as canals, rice fields, ponds, etc. And on the night of the 24th to the night of the 25th of July 2022, a series of rains caused the flooding of Suong Krong Suong market, but did not cause any material damage to traders.
As of 1:00 pm on July 25, 2022, the water level has dropped and the traders have returned to normal, and the municipal authorities will continue to monitor the situation. There are more subsequent actions.
