(Phnom Penh): The agricultural sector is a pillar to support the Cambodian national economy, the export of agricultural products, especially fresh fruits has become an important policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia to improve the living standards of farmers and promote national economic growth.
In fact, before the Kovid-19 crisis, Cambodia's agricultural exports to international markets increased year by year, especially the acquisition of the Chinese market, a large potential market for Cambodian agricultural exports. In that, more and more types of Cambodian agricultural products have appeared in the Chinese market.
However, Cambodia's agricultural exports in the context of Kovid also face some problems, according to the Cambodian Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, in the first five months of 2022, the export of some fresh agricultural products of Cambodia to international markets, especially markets. China, Cambodia's largest market, has declined significantly due to a number of factors, such as tightening controls on goods to prevent the spread of Kovid-19.
However, as a new achievement under the recent Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, the assessment of phytosanitary requirements for the export of fresh longan fruit from Cambodia to China has reached the final stage. The positive results that can be exported in the coming harvest season, during August or September, according to Mr. Ngin Chhay, the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture of Cambodia.
In addition, a number of Cambodian agricultural products are also being negotiated for direct export to Chinese markets, believing that they will receive approval and recognition from the Chinese government, which will increase the number of Chinese people. Get to know and taste fresh Cambodian produce.
Under the auspices of the "Belt and Road" initiative and the Cambodia-China Free Trade Agreement, as well as the steel ties, the Chinese government is currently studying the possibility of strengthening and expanding trade and investment with Cambodia. Agriculture is also a priority.
Therefore, we can be confident that under the joint efforts of the two countries, China and Cambodia will finally be able to overcome the obstacles affecting international exports such as the Kovid-19 crisis by then. In China's large and potential market will increase the presence of Cambodian products, especially more and more agricultural products.
