(Phnom Penh): Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, stated that all goods and trading instruments imported from abroad for sale in Cambodia should not be registered as intellectual property or exclusive trademarks. Compete equally to benefit consumers through price competition.
However, a spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce said that the registration of trademarks or intellectual property to the exclusive importer was to prevent the importation of counterfeit and substandard goods. In addition, granting exclusive sales rights to any individual or company is an agreement between the overseas product owner and the exclusive distributor.
Speaking to Fresh News, Tycoon Lim Heng said that the registration of intellectual property or exclusive trademarks of products imported from abroad is contrary to the law on consumer protection, fair competition law and free market policy in Cambodia can also affect the modernization of the national economy. But for products made locally or installed, it is protected by law and encouraged by the new investment law.
He added that this case also contributes to the reduction of counterfeit goods or counterfeit goods imported, while this problem is also occurring in the Cambodian market, which affects consumer rights and affects the rights of brand owners.
He explained that intellectual property is a private right, when the owner of the trademark comes to protect the Ministry must protect, and for the exclusive importers who file the exclusive import documents, the Ministry must recognize the right to distribute within a certain period. Because the brand owner is the one who gives the rights to that person.
He added that, however, in the case of importers of any brand to sell in Cambodia and did not take the exclusive application letter to the Ministry of Commerce to request the competent authorities such as the Anti-Counterfeiting Commission or the protection. No, when someone imports the same brand and when there is a protest or complaint to another importer, the Ministry will find it difficult to take action against the same importer.
He said that even if the import of goods for sale exclusively, can not affect the price conspiracy or pricing, because the brand owner will try to refine its quality and put the price appropriate to the cost of production and make the price. Sell down to sell to get more volume.
"I also recognize that there is a conflict between those who want to compete freely and brand owners who want to protect their brand," added Pen Sovichet.
According to the spokesman, the registration of the trademark will expire for 10 years, which the trademark owner will have to re-register, otherwise he will be entitled to use the trademark.
China launches second room as part of its space station construction process
BEIJING (Reuters) - China on Sunday launched the second of three rooms needed for the construction of its space station, which is expected to be completed before the end of the year. This was released by the AFP news agency on Sunday, July 24, 2022.
With a length of nearly 18 meters and a weight of 22 tons, the Vin Thean room has space for three astronauts to sleep and a space for various experimental work. While the new room will serve primarily as a science laboratory, it will also serve as a reserve for control over the entire station in the event of an emergency.
