At the same time, the Ministry would like to remind all people living in Cambodia to be more vigilant and actively participate in the implementation of measures to prevent the spread of chickenpox in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health. In the past, individuals, families and communities have continued to take care of the following measures to prevent the spread of their own and other diseases:
1: For suspected cases or sick cases
Ask people around you, especially family or relatives or other affected people, to track down the infected person.
2: For the general population
Practice good hygiene and clean living by cleaning your hands with soap and alcohol and prevent respiratory infections.
Avoid direct contact with people with the disease or suspected individuals, including sexual contact, especially skin or blisters, until the disease is cured.
Avoid touching the patient's or suspect's equipment, such as clothes, pillows, plates, spoons, glasses, water, etc., and wash or wash the equipment of this person separately.
* Asymptomatic suspects should not be subjected to sedation and can work normally, just being careful not to touch others during the 21-day follow-up visit after contact with a person with chickenpox. This.
* Eat well-cooked food and keep food hygiene and cooking well.
* Anyone with a rash accompanied by fever and the above symptoms should immediately consult a doctor right next to you and be isolated immediately until a diagnosis. Be clear with laboratory analysis as well.
* Local authorities must continue to educate people on health and raise awareness of infection prevention in their communities.
3: For doctors working in health facilities (both public and private)
* Awareness raising and education of caregivers and health workers must be carried out to prevent and stop the spread of disease in a timely manner, especially health workers must take strict and careful personal protective measures with infection control. Infection in the hospital properly.
Practice prevention of infection in hospitals or health centers in accordance with medical techniques that have been trained and guided in the context of prevention of Kovid-19 disease.
When encountering suspected cases or patients with this disease, wear personal protective equipment (PPE) before contact with suspected patients or individuals. All hospitals and health centers must monitor and report any suspected cases in order to continue the investigation.
* Monitor and identify the first case, cluster of infections, source of infection to prevent re-infection as soon as possible.
Strengthening the disease surveillance system in hospitals is very important to be able to detect suspected cases or cases quickly and take timely health measures to prevent transmission in families and communities.
4: For international travelers
* There is no ban on travelers from any country entering Cambodia, just be careful and monitor the situation of passengers entering Cambodia.
* Report any unusual and suspected symptoms to a health professional along with the patient's travel history and report to the local authority or competent authority.
5: Technical cooperation
In addition to the above measures, the Ministry of Health is working closely with the World Health Organization (WHO) to monitor the global spread of chickenpox in the region and in the country, and is stepping up surveillance for those infected. And those directly affected to disconnect the cable in a timely manner.
6: For more information
