(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Taxation, stated that the inspection of all enterprises doing business in Phnom Penh is to promote tax registration and tax payment. Equally, while the General Department of Taxation observes that some new businesses are doing business without tax registration.
Mr. Kong Vibol confirmed this while the team of the General Department of Taxation is ready to inspect all enterprises that are doing business in Phnom Penh from July 25, 2022.
He stated that in 2016, 2017 and 2018, the General Department of Taxation had already inspected once, finding that many businesses have not yet come to register for tax properly, and recently some business locations that have New openings, especially for Chinese, have not yet been taxed in accordance with the law.
The General Department of Taxation states that in the case of enterprises that have already registered for tax, they should prepare some copies of documents such as patent tax (last year) or tax registration certificate or tax registration certificate or tax receipt or Enterprise branch certificate (in case of enterprise branch).
In case the enterprise is not yet registered for tax, some copies should be prepared such as Khmer identity card or passport of the business owner or representative and the certificate of registration or business license from the relevant department or ministry or institution (if any). .
