The Ministry of Health and authorities at all levels are closely monitoring the case of Nigerians who contracted chickenpox and fled Thailand to Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health of Cambodia in cooperation with relevant authorities at all levels are Carefully research and monitor the case of a Nigerian who had chickenpox but escaped treatment in Thailand and headed to Cambodia.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Health, Ms. Youk Sambath, told Fresh News this morning, July 23, 2022, after receiving a report from the Thai authorities regarding the escape of a monkey patient, now the Ministry of Health and the authorities are Interlocking cells at all entrances to the Thai border, whether international gates, regional ports or corridors and waterways.
Ms. Yok Sambath stated, "After receiving high guidance from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, all health officials stationed at all ports in cooperation with authorities at all levels are preparing." "Authorities are burning hands and feet at all ports, whether on land or inland, and our emergency response officers at the border are ready."
At the same time, Banteay Meanchey provincial governor Oum Rath also issued an urgent order to all local authorities in his province bordering Thailand to search for Nigerians with similar identities after sharing information that the man He fled Thailand after being diagnosed with foot-and-mouth disease and came to Cambodia.
On July 18, 2022, Thailand announced the first case of chickenpox in its country, but a 27-year-old Nigerian man escaped after receiving News of positive test results.
Phuket Health Authority said that after receiving the results of the test, the patient refused to receive treatment and turned off his phone to contact the hospital. The Nigerian man arrived in Thailand on October 21, 2021 and has been staying in a condominium in Patong, Phuket since November last year.
