Many youth groups support raising tobacco taxes to save lives
Song Dirak confirmed to Fresh News this morning, July 23, 2022, that he fully supports the initiative to increase the tobacco tax, as the tobacco tax in Cambodia is currently limited. Low, such low taxes will encourage more consumers and more victims. Conversely, if tobacco taxes increase, state tax revenues increase, and deaths, disabilities, and tobacco use also decrease.
Please note that recently, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has organized various campaigns and forums related to the ban on public and private educational institutions, all forms of cooperation with tobacco companies and demand an increase in tobacco taxes. To make young people avoid tobacco use as well.
First, to identify and disseminate widely on the prohibition of the use of smoke of all kinds of tobacco products, exhibitions, advertisements of tobacco products around the premises and in public and private educational institutions.
Second, it must be carried out with great care to educate and disseminate knowledge related to the dangers caused by the use of inhalation of all kinds of tobacco products.
Third, do not partner with the tobacco industry for any purpose, such as charity activities, study visits, internships, exchange experiences or research.
Fourth, do not receive support or sign a memorandum of understanding with the tobacco industry to support all forms of educational activities.
Sixth, it is not allowed to provide places or yards of public and private educational institutions for organizing promotional programs or exhibitions, which are programs of the tobacco industry.
Seventh, to participate in eliminating the use of tobacco products in all forms. Institutions must immediately stop cooperating with any public and private outreach activities that violate the above content and correct them in accordance with the spirit of this instruction.
