Deep affection for the country and the people of Cambodia also led Thai Susumu to volunteer as Cambodia's Honorary Consul in Sendai, Japan to facilitate investment between Japanese investors in Sendai and Cambodia. .
On his way to and from Cambodia more than 20 years ago and now, Thai Susumu was amazed at the growth and development in Cambodia. The Japanese man described the situation in Cambodia, which he saw more than 20 years ago and now as two different countries.
Mr. Thai Susumu said, "Through my journey to Cambodia, it has been about 20 years now. I observed that 20 years ago, Cambodia had not yet landed in Cambodia, but when I looked at Cambodia from a plane window, I saw that Cambodia was dark more than 20 years ago. Dark, do not know where? Where is the city? "But compared to now, like two separate countries."
Thai Susumu also noted security concerns. He said security issues between the past 20 years and now are very different.
"At that time, I arrived in Cambodia immediately and heard that there was theft, insecurity, shooting here and there. Twenty years ago, when I arrived in Phnom Penh, there were many thefts. My translator did not dare to take me outside the hotel for fear of theft. "So compared to today, we have a lot more peace of mind than before." This is the confirmation of Mr. Thai Susumu.
Mr. Thai Susumu noted that now Cambodians as well as foreigners travel in Cambodia safely and normally like other countries. He also saw that in relation to the previous buildings, he saw only Wat Phnom and Canadia. But now there are many high-rise commercial buildings owned by foreign investors as well as locals.
"Twenty years ago and now I say it is as different as two separate countries," he said. Thus, we have a lot of things different from before, which confirms that due to the wise leadership of Samdech Techo, he has maintained peace, security, safety, both physically and mentally. Maintaining all this stability allows investors to look at investment opportunities in Cambodia. This is a good economic expansion policy of Samdech Techo.
