(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Kheang Phearum, Deputy Director of Planning and Investment of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall, chaired a meeting to resolve the request of six vendors at Phsar Leu, asking for their intervention to be able to sell at their original location.
The recent meeting was also attended by relevant departments and units, representatives of Sihanoukville Administration, representatives of Sangkat 4, the President of Phsar Leu, the President of Sihanoukville Business Center (China Market) and the six business owners who own Request.
After discussing and listening to the opinions, the meeting agreed and decided as follows:
* The provincial administration supports the honest eating habits of the people, but does not support the sale of food on the streets, gates or market entrances, which affects the order and aesthetics, especially the risk of spreading Kovid disease. -19
* Request the traders to understand and cooperate in organizing order in order to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 by finding a suitable location in the market.
* Ask the market manager to study the vacant space in Phsar Mek to provide a place for the 6 traders in case they want to continue selling in the market and can not afford to rent a stall
* Instruct the market manager and traders in the upper market to continue to implement the content of Resolution No. 185/21 dated August 10, 2021 to be more effective. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Department of Tourism Holds a Dissemination Course on Tourism Development Plan Update 2021-2025
(Preah Sihanouk): In order to implement the five-year tourism development plan of Preah Sihanouk Province 2021-2025, the Department of Tourism of Preah Sihanouk Province this morning, July 22, 2022, held a dissemination session chaired by Mr. Tith Chantha, Acting Minister of Tourism. And Mrs. Hiek Him Moly, Deputy Governor.
Ms. Hiek Him Moly said that in order to implement this five-year plan successfully, it requires the participation of all stakeholders to improve the quality of tourism in Sihanoukville to receive more tourists in line with The long-term vision of the Royal Government.
She said that the Royal Government considers tourism as a green gold and one of the priority sectors to contribute to the growth and socio-economic development through job creation, investment, poverty reduction, supporting the development of related structures and conservation. The cultural wealth and natural resources of the nation are important.
Sihanoukville has been identified by the Royal Government as a multi-purpose model economy in line with the Industrial Development Policy 2010-2025 and in the National Tourism Development Policy and Plan based on the unique potential of economic and natural resources, including ports. International beaches and beautiful islands with waterfalls attract more tourists to visit and relax every year.
In fact, in the first half of 2022, Sihanoukville received more than 2 million visitors, an increase compared to the first half of 2021, with just over 590,000 tourists.
On that occasion, Mr. Tith Chentha emphasized that the meeting on the dissemination of the updated plan on tourism in Sihanoukville 2021-2025 is a continuation plan that the working group has been implementing for the past 5 years. Strategies for tourism development.
He said that the plan is a joint study on all relevant areas such as infrastructure, tourism achievements, development in the coastal islands in the city of Sihanoukville, because Sihanoukville is an important pole in the coastal area. Attracts millions of tourists each year, both domestic and international.
He added that due to the Kovid 19 crisis, the world as well as Cambodia has declined in tourism, and now, after the Royal Government of Cambodia has reopened tourism, Sihanoukville has seen a significant increase in the number of tourists. Internal tourists, both domestic and international guests, especially on the occasion of major festivals as well as weekends.
He added that another factor is that in Phnom Penh, the demand for housing is high but expensive, especially houses or land in the center of the city, so the need for living is an affordable condo in the center of the capital is easy to do. Journey. For each condo equipped with privacy, there is a swimming pool, a gym, a restaurant and a comfortable living.
He said that in the first six months of this year, the condominium market has grown significantly, the growth of domestic purchases and investment in the condominium sector has increased, and foreign investment began to increase gradually, as in today's ERA program. Also invited are investors from Singapore.
