Currently, the company has about 1,500 agents to provide services for buying, selling and renting condos in Cambodia. With more than four years of ERA Cambodia presence in the Cambodian market, the company has partnered to sell more than 30 major condominium projects, with a combined investment of billions of dollars.
According to the press release, a video was recently posted by the owner of the Facebook account "Yeay Kum Teuk Cha" and shared on social media about a woman who expressed her anger at Smart Assata Company for cutting the money. For no apparent reason when he topped up his phone.
After checking and questioning Ms. Kol Sok Kum, who was the one who encountered this problem, it was found that her deduction was due to this phone number still owed money when the phone could not be called. When recharging, the company deducts the money and pays it back immediately.
She also stated that she did not know about the loan, which made her angry about cutting money for no reason.
In this regard, in order to prevent cases of unauthorized borrowing, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has advised all mobile operators to stop using the loan service to avoid further confusion. The goal is to protect the interests of consumers.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications would also like to inform the public that in the past, Pay close attention to the protection of consumer rights, especially the issue of deducting money from the operator without knowing the reason or connection of other services without knowing, etc., with the implementation of the common code * 1200 # To allow users to unplug unnecessary projects.
Meanwhile, users who have other problems related to telecommunication services can also complain to the Department of Consumer Protection of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications by phone 6789 to solve.
