(Phnom Penh): Accurate and in-depth understanding of the behavior of a nation or country requires an in-depth understanding of the cultural and traditional values that influence the mindset and attitude of that nation or country, otherwise judgment Ours may be a serious mistake. In the same way, in order to properly and deeply understand China's attitude in international relations, we need to understand the traditional cultural values of the Chinese people.
Among these key values, harmony can be considered as the most influential value on China's foreign policy. For the Chinese, harmony is the unification of differences, enabling differences to coexist peacefully. In other words, harmony refers to living together and prospering together, even though all nations or countries have different traditional cultures.
In international relations, what the Chinese government most desires is a world of harmony, peace, stability and common prosperity. . In other words, the Chinese government recognizes and values diversity and sees that countries with different civilizations can coexist peacefully in the global community.
Based on these values, China has always supported and promoted multilateral mechanisms in international relations, as well as opposed the policy of interfering in the internal affairs of other countries and forced other countries to follow suit. The policy of peace and non-interference in the internal affairs of other countries, which China has always adhered to and implemented, is one of China's prominent identities that is well known around the world.
