Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea: Investors interested in Cambodia's potential as 98 projects approved in the first half of $ 3 billion
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (ECCC), emphasized that investors are interested in the potential for investment in Cambodia during the first six months of 2022. Increase compared to the same period in 2021.
In the first half of 2022, the Council for the Development of Cambodia approved 98 new projects and production expansion projects with a total investment of more than 2,998 million US dollars, creating 72,329 jobs. Compared to the same period in 2021, the number of investment projects increased by 11 projects while the investment capital increased by 29 million dollars.
He stated that the interest in investing in Cambodia because the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has vaccinated the people to the highest rate, which makes the community immune.
Mr. Sok Chendasophea stated, "Investors are interested in the potential of Cambodia. I have summarized the figures for the first half of 2022, showing that compared to the first half of 2021 is better and increased. Up.
He pointed out that the increase in investment is due to the government's vaccination measures for the people, but this increase compared to the year before Kovid-19 is still low.
Despite the increase in investment, the minister noted that "investment has begun to pick up, but to reach the figure of 19 when there is no Kovid, it will be a while, but there is hope and a lot of good signs."
He stressed that the Russia-Ukraine war crisis, not just Cambodia, all countries are concerned, and that concern is the rise in oil prices, rising energy prices, rising transportation costs and rising food prices. Origin. Investors in the world are often inactive in times of war crisis because it is unpredictable and no one dares to talk about any period of time on the economy, and this is what investors are afraid of. Most.
He hopes that this crisis will be resolved and if the crisis from the impact on the world economy is relieved, Cambodia is ready to receive investors.
He added that the Council for the Development of Cambodia will continue to promote and attract investment by further strengthening the investment maintenance mechanism and continue to participate in the implementation of various reform measures of the Royal Government, especially measures that facilitate investment for investors in And abroad.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun: Demining mission in Sihanoukville liberates farmland from threats to residents and tourists
(Preah Sihanouk): On the morning of July 22, 2022, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, held a meeting with demining officers (CMAC) in Kampong Seila district with the participation of district authorities, government officials and armed forces. Weapons.
According to a report by the Southern Demining Unit, the demining operation was successful due to the support of the Chinese government. There are 5 demining teams operating in Sihanoukville with a total staff of 36, including 4 women who started demining operations from March 1, 2022 and will complete the demining by the end of the month. July 2022 is coming.
The Southern Demining Unit cleared 1,737,013 square meters of unexploded ordnance (173 hectares), found and destroyed 34 mines and 93 unexploded ordnance. Meanwhile, in clearing mines, the team encountered obstacles, weather, rain, wind almost every day, most of the minefields are mountainous and far from the road can not reach some of the minefields travel many kilometers.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun brought greetings and memories from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to the five groups of CMAC staff who led the work in Sihanoukville.
The provincial governor added that the area cleared of mines and munitions has helped boost the socio-economic situation and tourists are no longer afraid of landmines. And people and tourists can walk into the forest, climb mountains, as well as attract investors in our land of Sovannaphum can increase jobs for our youth in the future.
The mission to clear mines and unexploded ordnance is to contribute to improving the lives of the people and the socio-economy. The Royal Government of Cambodia, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has taken care to address the mine sector, eliminate landmines and unexploded ordnance that endanger people and socio-economic processes.
