Minister of Information Donates Rain Candles to 5 Pagodas in Koh Sotin Commune, Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group for Local Assistance in Koh Sotin District, Kampong Cham Province To 5 pagodas in Koh Sotin commune, Kampong Cham province.
The Vesa Candle Offering Ceremony was held on Friday morning, July 22, 2022 at Wat Serey Mongkul, Kbal Koh, Village 3, Koh Sotin Commune, Kampong Cham Province, to prepare candles, candles or oil for the monks, nuns, practice and rituals according to Buddhist traditions. .
It should be noted that for this year's Vesak Festival, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, together with the national team to help Koh Sotin district, as well as to visit all 8 communes throughout the district, brought candles, gifts, relics and suffixes to all. The 27 pagodas in Koh Sotin district, Kampong Cham province, during the rainy season for 3 months to contribute to support the monks who live in the pagoda to learn various disciplines during the 3 months of this rainy season.
Vesa festival is an important festival in Buddhism, an important time for monks and nuns to study the Dharma and discipline consistently according to the Buddha's teachings. Believers in Buddhism often celebrate the festival by bringing rice, drinks and other items to the monks as much as possible.
For each pagoda during the three months of the rainy season, it is not allowed to travel far and wide during the day and night, unless there are important duties such as parents who are seriously ill or going to perform dharma, etc., determined to return. Within 7 days. The rainy season is celebrated every year from the 1st day of the month of Assad to the 15th day of the month of Assoch.
On this occasion, Mr. Khieu Kanharith brought football to two youth football teams in Koh Sotin commune for training, capacity building and better cooperation.
Separately, in the morning of the same day, Mr. Khieu Kanharith visited and gave money to Mr. Mao Neth, a member of Kampong Cham Provincial Council, who has a physical illness and is being treated at his home in Sangkat Kampong Cham, Kampong Cham City.
