Japanese: More Japanese Investors Interested in Investing in Cambodia Due to Peace and Political Stability (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): As the Honorary Consul of Cambodia in Sendai, Japan, Thai Susumu Facilitate a lot of work to pave the way for Japanese investors to invest in Cambodia.
In an interview with Fresh News, Thai Susumu noted that since Cambodia opened its consulate in Sendai in 2019, there have been many Japanese investors interested in investing in Cambodia.
"Compared to the recent period when Cambodia and Japan reopened their respective countries, new Japanese investors have approached me to inquire about investment opportunities in Japan," he said. Cambodia.
According to Thai Susumu, companies that contacted him to invest in Cambodia included companies in agriculture, healthcare and labor recruitment in Japan.
Mr. Thai Susumu claimed that Cambodia is now preparing to establish a branch of the Chamber of Commerce in Sendai to provide advice and information related to investment in Cambodia. Mr. Thai Susumu expects that through this branch of the Chamber of Commerce will contribute more contacts to Japanese investors to Cambodia.
"Right now, a lot of people are looking forward to the opportunity for our official opening, they will be joining the membership of our Chamber of Commerce in Japan. We expect you to have "More Japanese investment through the opening of our Chamber of Commerce representative office in Japan."
Regarding the reasons and factors that lead more Japanese investors to invest in Cambodia, this Japanese man presented four factors. The four factors are: peace and political stability, a new emerging economy in ASEAN, a large young workforce and good relations between the two governments.
Mr. Thai Susumu clarified this detail: Point 1: I say that because of the wise leadership of Samdech Techo, he created stability and security for the people of Cambodia. On the other hand, we have good political stability at this point, which attracts investors to look at investment opportunities in Cambodia because our country is peaceful and we do not have a war like other countries.
So the first important thing is that we have good peace, we keep safe for investors to see this opportunity. So this point I think is the most important.
Point 2: Our country is a growing economy in ASEAN. As the most emerging emerging economies in ASEAN. It is possible that our economic growth is higher than some ASEAN countries.
Point 3: Cambodia, we are full of young people with strength, intelligence and physical strength, especially our young people have kept pace with the new era of technology such as AI or technology. Knowledge is also a force, so it is an attraction for Japanese investors.
Point 4: I think the relationship between the two governments is good. It is the good relations between the two governments that make the people of the two countries have good relations. In particular, we see that the people of Japan and the people of Cambodia have never had any conflict with each other, we love each other and have a long-standing friendship with all other countries.
According to the report, in 2021, Cambodia and Japan had a total trade volume of more than 1.7 billion US dollars. Cambodia exports more than $ 1 billion to Japan and Cambodia exports more than $ 600 million from Japan.
Cambodia's exports to Japan include clothing, footwear, furniture, cosmetics, paper, office supplies, leather, animals, metals, and more. In particular, the goods that Cambodia brings back from Japan include: machinery, cars, meat, electricity, furniture, paper, cotton, all kinds of products, plastic products, sports equipment, all kinds of spare parts and so on.
In terms of investment, from 1994 to 2020, there were 144 Japanese investment projects in Cambodia with a total capital of more than 2.7 billion US dollars. System in Siem Pang village, Sekong commune, Siem Pang district
