Flooding of National Road 5 in Kampong Tralach District due to the opening of the flood gate at Anlong Chrey Dam in Kampong Speu Province, but the authorities did not stop the traffic
(Kampong Chhnang): Due to the opening of the sluice gate at Anlong Chrey Dam, Kampong Speu Province, and a series of rains, National Road No. 5 between km 39-40 in Kampong Tralach and Samaki Meanchey districts of Kampong Chhnang province was flooded this morning. July 22, 2022.
Mr. Chhay Leaphea, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, said that due to heavy rains, the authorities were forced to open the Anlong Chrey Dam to avoid any collapse, thus causing the waterfall to fall below. And flooded National Road No. 5. He said that if the sky at the top continues to rain, the flood may flood the national road at this point.
As for the measures, the authorities and the Department of Public Works are taking measures to block the sand on the national road so that water can enter the canal under the bridge at the above point. In particular, the traffic at the above point can still travel without interruption, so for travel, drivers of all types, please be careful.
However, in the event of severe flooding from above, traffic on National Road 5 at this point may be temporarily cut off. Director of Preah Vihear Provincial Public Works Department warns officials not to be complacent about issuing driver's licenses, especially those who do not come to the exam and all overweight trucks must be weighed
