Myanmar decides not to send representatives to ASEAN Foreign Ministers 'Meeting in Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Myanmar has decided not to send representatives to the 55th ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting and related meetings in Phnom Penh starting at No end of July. This is according to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation in an interview with the Cambodian National News Agency (AKP).
According to Prak Sokhon, even if Myanmar waives its right to attend these meetings, it will not lose its seat in ASEAN. He said, however, that Cambodia did not give up on finding a solution for Myanmar and tried to pave the way to bring the country back to ASEAN.
Mr. Prak Sokhon added, "Myanmar's answer is still the same. Non-political representatives may not be appointed to those meetings. "However, Myanmar's position in ASEAN remains."
According to Prak Sokhon, the nine ASEAN countries have agreed that as long as there is not enough progress in Myanmar, Myanmar's participation is only a non-governmental representation.
Please be informed that during the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting on 17 February 2022 in Phnom Penh, Myanmar did not send a representative to attend the meeting, but listened to a link.
