(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Commerce expressed his appreciation for the activities of those who do business in the electronic system, or in other words, online, who came to apply for registration, license and notification of business. Of them at the Ministry of Commerce.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Commerce, stated that as of July 19, 2022, 7,104 people had applied for licenses and licenses to conduct e-commerce transactions. And 15,800 notices of electronic business.
Mr. Pen Sovicheat made this statement at a press conference on "Achievements of the past five years of the Ministry of Commerce" organized by the Spokesperson of the Royal Government on the morning of July 21, 2022.
Please be informed that e-business people can still apply for a license or e-business license through the following procedures:
Legal entities, branches of foreign companies and sole proprietorships that conduct e-commerce operations without the permission of the Ministry of Commerce must apply but shall be subject to penalties in accordance with applicable law.
Legal entities, branches, foreign companies and sole proprietors who are just starting to operate or intend to conduct e-commerce can apply for a license or e-commerce license without penalty.
* A natural person with a turnover below the turnover level as a small taxpayer may continue to notify the Ministry of Commerce to obtain an exemption from the requirement to apply, or if the natural person still wants to obtain a permit, Apply for a business license electronically without penalty. Commentary: Youth groups urge all relevant institutions to implement a ban on partnerships with tobacco companies
(Phnom Penh): Youth groups have urged all relevant institutions to implement a ban on partnerships with tobacco companies as tobacco destroys consumers' health, harms the environment and hurts the national economy.
Prohibition of educational institutions from cooperating with tobacco companies is a national response and obligation to the International Convention on Tobacco Control, Article 5.3. This was stated by the best candidates in the final public speaking competition, which was held on the morning of July 21, 2022 at the Phnom Penh Pedagogical Institute in the presence of Lok Chumteav Kim Sethany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
The main content of Article 5.3 of the Convention is: (1) The tobacco industry and public health are in conflict of fundamental interests and cannot be reconciled. (2) The tobacco industry should not be motivated to establish or operate their business because tobacco is a product that causes the death of consumers. Article 5.3 is an important article of the Convention on Tobacco Control, which Cambodia has ratified since 2005.
The implementation of this article reflects Cambodia's willingness to protect tobacco control policies from interference by the tobacco industry. The World Health Organization (WHO) has made it clear that the tobacco industry has been operating for many years with the intention of undermining the role of government and the World Health Organization in implementing public health policies to combat the spread of tobacco use. .
It should also be noted that tobacco is not a necessary product, but it provides side effects that are a burden for the government to address. In Cambodia, about 15,000 people died prematurely from diseases caused by tobacco use, and an estimated $ 649 million was lost. Tobacco use causes premature death, and tobacco companies need new smokers to stay profitable.
(By: Cambodia-China Friendship Radio) A book on "Democracy in the Chinese Way" compiled by Dr. Chea Monirith has been published in the Cambodian Senate.
(Phnom Penh): The book "Democracy in the Chinese Style" was published on the morning of July 21, 2022 at the Senate Library of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Phnom Penh, with the participation of many officials, professors and students. The 80-page book is divided into three main chapters: Chinese-style socialism, Chinese-style ideals, and Chinese-style diplomacy.
His Excellency also encouraged the ceremony, especially the officials of the General Secretariat of the Senate and the students of Asia-Europe University who participated in this morning program to continue reading carefully on the research work of Dr. Chea Monirith and encourage the library Continue to cooperate with the Cambodia-China Progress Researchers Association to increase the number of research books from China.
Through this recently published book, Dr. Chea Monirith highlights the provisions of democracy, emphasizing that democracy is not a uniform model or a completely the same configuration for all countries around the world.
