Three people arrested for clearing forest land in a protected area in Kampong Thom province's Prasat Balang district have been released on bail.
(Kampong Thom): Three people living in Samaki commune, Prasat Balong district, Kampong Thom province, who were detained by the authorities on charges of clearing forest land in a protected area at the end of June 2022, were sentenced by a provincial court judge. They were released on bail after a search found that they had not committed the alleged crimes.
The three people are:
1. Name: Vorn Vy, Male, 50 years old, currently living in Trach Village, Samaki Commune, Prasat Balong District, Kampong Thom Province. Than Mony, male, 31 years old, currently living in Kampot village, Samaki commune, Prasat Balong district, Kampong Thom province, is the owner of a tractor. Ran Ron currently lives in Doung village, Doung commune, Prasat Balong district, Kampong Thom province, and works as a tractor driver for Than Mony.
It should be informed that on June 27, 2022, the police raided a tractor and arrested two people involved in the clearing of a forest land in Prasat Balong district, Kampong Thom province, including Vorn Vy, who was The owner of the land and Ran Ron, who was hired to drive the tractor.
Authorities later stored the tractor at the Palm Police Administration post in Prasat Balong district. The owner of the tractor, Than Mony, after realizing that his tractor was arrested by the police and the police called to the police station, he immediately rode a motorcycle to Post Doung and was handcuffed by the police.
In Criminal Case No. 489, dated July 1, 2022 of the Kampong Thom Provincial Court, the three men were charged with "clearing, encroaching, burning and clearing forest land for ownership."
At the request of the intervention of the CPP Committee of Samaki Commune, as well as the insistence on seeking justice from the families of the above three people, as well as the attention of the authorities and local authorities who know the land background. Clearly, this case is also respected to the Governor of Kampong Thom, Mr. Nguon Rattanak.
The provincial governor also intervened and ordered the relevant departments in the province to cooperate with the prosecutor's office of the provincial court to study this case for sure.
After being granted bail, the three residents, including their families, also thanked Provincial Governor Nguon Rattanak, President of the Provincial Court and the prosecutor of Kampong Thom Provincial Court, as well as relevant professional officials who helped find the culprit. To them who are honest citizens and committed to fulfill their obligations, court requirements and legal procedures.
