Three consecutive days of rain caused the flooding of Svay Rieng field market in a short time and flooded some people's rice fields
(Svay Rieng): Three consecutive days of rain from 19 to 21 July 2022 caused the short-term flooding of Svay Rieng Veal Yont Market and flooded some roads and flooded rice paddies. Of some citizens as well.
According to reports from residents in districts and cities in Svay Rieng province, the three-day rain flooded rice fields because crops, especially some roads, were very slippery.
At the same time, Veal Yon Market in Svay Rieng City, a large market, was also flooded, making it difficult for traders to sell, and the flood did not flood for a long time because the relevant authorities organized a sewer on the streets in Svay Rieng. Wider, can release water in just 2 to 3 hours.
However, Svay Rieng municipal authorities have deployed garbage to block the sewers to avoid clogging the drains, and for the flooding of rice in some districts in Svay Rieng province, people have installed water pumps. From the rice fields, but due to the heavy rains, the rice fields of some people rotted and did not grow, forcing the people to wait for the water to recede before sowing rice again.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, moderate to heavy rainfall across the country due to the effects of low pressure system and moderate southwest monsoon will continue until the 21st. July weakened slightly after the low pressure systems on Thailand, Laos and Vietnam moved up slightly.
Legal Aid of Cambodia in Cooperation with Kampot Provincial Information Department Holds Training Course for Journalists on Media Law
(Kampot): Legal Aid Organization of Cambodia (LAC) in collaboration with Kampot Provincial Information Department on July 21, 2022 held a training course for journalists on the Law of the Regime at Khemara Guesthouse in Kampong Bay South Village, Sangkat Kampong Bay, Kampot city.
The training was attended by Mr. Ok Samnang, Director of Kampot Provincial Information Department, Mr. Run Saray, Executive Director of Legal Aid of Cambodia, Mr. Un Chanthol, Lawyer of Legal Aid of Cambodia, and local journalists. Kampot about 30 people. This training course lasts for one day.
Mr. Run Saray said that this training course was given by the speakers who are lawyers of the Legal Aid Organization of Cambodia, who presented the law on the media and related laws, as well as the problems that are facing in the work of journalists and solutions in Aims to raise awareness to reduce challenges in practicing journalism.
According to the director of the Kampot Provincial Information Department, this is the third time that the Legal Aid Organization of Cambodia has cooperated with the Kampot Provincial Information Department to strengthen the awareness of journalists in Kampot.
Mr. Ok Samnang added that in relation to today's training is very important for journalists because the press is an important part in contributing to the development of society to grow and in a society can not lack the press. Because the press is a mirror that reflects the view of society as a messenger from the people to the authorities and from the authorities to the masses with transparency, trust, professionalism and the law.
The director of the Department of Information also expressed his hope and instructed all journalists to pay attention to the lectures of the speakers and discuss more clearly the law on the press to apply all this knowledge in their work. Better in accordance with the law of the Ministry of Information, different, fast, reliable, anywhere, anytime.
