(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Commerce, confirmed that the Free Trade Agreement between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea (CKFTA), which was officially signed in October 2021, has not yet entered into force. No, because the Korean side has not yet completed its internal procedures.
He confirmed this at a press conference on "Achievements of the Ministry of Commerce for 5 years" at the Office of the Council of Ministers on July 21, 2022.
He said that the Cambodian side has already completed the internal procedures and the approval of the National Assembly and the Senate and sent this notification to the Korean side, but because Korea is time for the presidential election and the formation of the government. The entry into force of this agreement is to wait a little longer.
"We have repeatedly urged Hun Sen during his visit to the Republic of Korea, as well as to the President of the Senate, who also visited the President of the Korean Senate to expedite the legislation," he said. This way to come into force soon.
As a rule, the CKFTA will enter into force 60 days after the two sides inform each other diplomatically of the completion of the internal ratification procedures.
The FTA between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea will further promote Cambodia's exports to the Republic of Korea, such as garments and textiles, footwear, bags, spare parts, electronics, rubber and agricultural products.
