Mobile scales officers raid overweight trucks in Phnom Preuk, Battambang province
(Battambang): A group of mobile scales officers led by Mr. Ek Rath, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Public Works and Transport, on Thursday, July 21, 2022, raided and inspected overweight trucks on National Road No. 59 in Phnom Proek District. Battambang Province.
During the raid, mobile scales officers inspected 15 vehicles belonging to Thai traders buying red corn at the Cambodian-Thai border. According to Ek Rath, the 15 vehicles inspected did not exceed the legal limit.
Mr. Ek Rath considered the non-overloading of Thai traders' vehicles as a sign of vigilance and participation in respect of Cambodian transport laws by Thai traders as well as the Silo group, which is a broker in the country. Cambodia.
However, Mr. Ekrath claimed that he continued to raid and inspect transport activities on the Cambodia-Thailand border ring road to prevent overweight shipments. He also called on all freight forwarders to abide by Cambodia's transport laws to avoid fines or one-year car seizures that could lead to more losses.
Regarding the operation to seize the overweight truck, the Battambang Provincial Department of Commerce claimed that it did not obstruct the procurement of red corn at the border in Battambang province. According to the report, Thai traders continue to come to collect red corn from Cambodia at the border in Battambang province as usual.
