(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, urged the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Phnom Penh and the 14 Khan authorities to take care of all kinds of trees that have been planted in Phnom Penh to help. Inspire people to love and take care of trees as well.
This morning, July 21, 2022, during a tree planting ceremony to celebrate the 9th of July 2022 at Phneat Simpaly pagoda in Svay village, Snor commune, Kampoul district, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Khuong Sreng said that in Phnom Penh, although there is no large area of land for planting trees, this ceremony is always held every year like in other provinces throughout the country, except In 2020 and 2021, this event was interrupted due to the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
Mr. Khuong Sreng added that in Phnom Penh, 200,000 trees have been prepared for planting in the park. For the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Phnom Penh and the 14 district authorities must take care to check all kinds of trees that have been planted because some people steal trees. This is an issue that must be taken care of carefully.
Mr. Chan Rithy, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Phnom Penh, stated that the Tree Day is celebrated on July 9 every year under the high presidency of the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia or His Majesty the King.
Planting trees at Wat Phneat Simpaly Phnom Penh authorities planted a variety of trees such as Kranhong Thnong, Neang Nuon Beng, Koki, Chheuteal, Kinin, Chreak, Koh Sakura, Tnout, Kngok, Tamarind, French, Inle, Raing Phnom, Reang Tuek and Po trees, a total of 11,072 trees. In addition, 33,116 trees were planted in pagodas, schools and public roads in Phnom Penh.
The Phnom Penh Forestry Administration of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Phnom Penh has planted about 30,000 seedlings per year for the monks and distributed to the people to plant for 2022. By the end of June, more than 40,000 saplings were ready to be distributed to schools, pagodas, district halls, public institutions and people.
