He said these issues were hurting global production chains, putting pressure on global inflation and increasing capital outflows from emerging and developing countries, which would put further pressure on currency values and reserves. International in those countries.
"However, Cambodia's economic activity is expected to continue to grow at a high rate of 5.3% in 2021, at 3%, mainly supported by growth in exports of manufacturing, growth in construction and real estate," he said. "And agriculture, with the gradual recovery of tourism."
Mr. Chea Chanto said that the inflation situation is highly uncertain, mainly due to the prolonged influence of the Russia-Ukraine war on oil prices and the implementation of measures to block production areas in China to prevent the spread of the disease. Kovid-19. With oil prices expected to fall, inflation is also projected to slow in the second half.
Mr. Chea Chanto stated that in the above challenging situation, please raise some suggestions for the work direction to be implemented as follows:
1: Maintaining exchange rate stability: As the US dollar tends to appreciate in the international market, the riel will continue to face downward pressure, so the National Bank of Cambodia will continue to use the necessary monetary policy instruments to maintain the riel. Stable to protect the purchasing power of the national currency as well as the income of vulnerable people.
In this direction, continuing to promote the use of the riel from all walks of life, including the public sector, the private sector and the general public, is very important to directly enhance the value of the riel and strengthen the overall monetary and political instruments.
At the same time, the National Bank of Cambodia will continue to pursue a monetary policy that facilitates the management of liquidity in the banking system. It should be noted that the success of strengthening the use of the riel will lead the National Bank of Cambodia to influence interest rate management to better support national economic activity.
3. Monitoring and maintaining financial stability: The global economic situation faces high uncertainty and the international financial market situation also faces constraints. Regular monitoring of the well-being of banking and financial institutions with the introduction of proactive macro- and micro-precautionary measures is essential to strengthen the resilience of the banking sector and maintain financial stability.
In this regard, banking and financial institutions must continue to manage potential risks, especially external factors, and adhere to prudent regulations, while continuing to contribute to economic recovery. The National Bank of Cambodia will continue to implement the crisis exit strategy in a cautious manner in line with the evolving economic and financial situation to strengthen the resilience and sustainability of the development of the Cambodian banking system.
Therefore, banking and financial institutions must continue to co-develop the payment system responsibly and contribute to the prevention of cybercrime. Diversify and strengthen digital customer identification (e-KYC) and strengthen payment system security to contribute to the support of the development of the digital economy of the Royal Government.
Call on all citizens and stakeholders to increase the use of the riel. The riel is the only national currency of Cambodia that represents national identity and provides both economic and social benefits.
6: Branch work of the National Bank of Cambodia Capital-Province: The branches of the National Bank of Cambodia in the capital-province are the representatives of the National Bank of Cambodia to contribute to the economic development at the local level. Past visits have seen an increase in economic activity in the provinces after the situation of Kovid-19 eased, especially the increasing use of the riel and the growing population using financial services.
At the same time, it is proposed to continue to strengthen the Business Sustainability Plan (BCP) to ensure the central bank's role in particular, especially the provision of services to banking and financial institutions and government entities in situations where Kovid 19 disease is not yet complete and Faced with uncertainties eventually.
8. Discipline: Work discipline is an important part of strengthening governance and increasing work efficiency. During the Kovid-19 crisis, staff officers continued to perform their duties responsibly and flexibly.
9. Human resource management: To strengthen the efficiency of the central bank in the digital economy, human resource development is an important priority that must be implemented on a regular basis. Appreciate the efforts of officers and staff who have continuously developed their knowledge, expertise and other skills to enhance the quality and efficiency of work.
In line with the growth of the banking sector and the global financial structure, the Deputy Governor is encouraged to continue to encourage staff officers to pursue further self-study online and to initiate training courses such as accuracy, leadership and supervision. Check the bank according to the actual situation when the problem of Kovid-19 is relieved.
