Then, on December 21, 1994, the Royal Government issued Sub-Decree No. 77 on the Roles, Duties and General Structure of the Royal Cambodian Gendarmerie and the Code of Criminal Procedure, which was approved by the National Assembly on June 7, 2007, clearly defining its jurisdiction. Of the Gendarmerie in Book 2, Content 4, Chapter 4.
General Sao Sokha stated that according to the above legal documents, 29 years ago, the Royal Gendarmerie has built both hard and soft infrastructure and performed the duties and responsibilities set out in the legal documents to contribute to maintaining security and maintaining order. Suppress crime, strengthen the implementation of building the Kingdom of Cambodia as a country of the rule of law.
