Deputy Minister of Commerce Leads a Cambodian Delegation to the 63rd General Assembly of the World Intellectual Property Organization in Geneva, Switzerland
(Geneva, Switzerland): Mr. Ouk Prachea, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce, and Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, led a delegation from the Ministry of Commerce to attend the 63rd General Assembly of the World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO). July 14-22, 2022, with 186 member countries participating.
During the meeting, the head of the Cambodian delegation addressed the General Assembly, congratulating Daren Tang on his election as Director-General of the World Intellectual Property Organization and highlighting the progress of the intellectual property sector in Cambodia. And commends the fruitful and meaningful cooperation with the World Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) in the past since Cambodia became a member in 1995.
The Secretary of State then expressed Cambodia's commitment to continue to actively participate in the World Intellectual Property Organization as a member and to further promote closer cooperation.
He added that he was optimistic, confident and appreciative of Daren Tang's leadership, which would help improve the global intellectual property system, especially support the least developed countries in building intellectual property infrastructure and strengthening the implementation of intellectual property laws. .
On this occasion, the Secretary of State of the delegation requested the Director General of the World Intellectual Property Organization to continue to support and provide technical assistance to train new businesses in the field of intellectual property, the implementation of the action plan of the National Committee for the Management of Intellectual Property in Cambodia 2021-2023, such as List of geographically marked goods.
Finally, the Director General of the World Intellectual Property Organization pledged to continue to support more Cambodian projects to help promote the intellectual property sector in Cambodia. Live broadcast of "Cambodia-China Online Dialogue on Agriculture" hosted by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio successfully
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of July 20, 2022, the live program "Online Dialogue on Cambodia-China Agriculture" organized by Cambodia-China Friendship Radio of the General Radio and Television of China was successfully held.
His Excellency Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, and distinguished guests in the Cambodian agricultural sector discussed in-depth topics on a number of topics, including the expansion of Cambodian-Chinese agricultural cooperation under the "Belt and Road" of Cambodian agricultural products. And phytosanitary products exported to China.
His Excellency Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, praised the "Belt and Road" initiative, which has provided many benefits for Cambodia.
At the same time, HE also thanked the program for paying attention to the progress of Cambodian agriculture and contributing to the promotion of Cambodian-Chinese agricultural cooperation. His Excellency believes that through this discussion, both sides better understand their roles and responsibilities in the comprehensive strategic partnership, which will push the process of building a common destiny of Cambodia and China to another level.
Mr. Lon Yeng, Secretary General of the Cambodian Rice Federation, said that the leaders of the two countries, Cambodia and China, pay high attention to rice exports from Cambodia to China. As of June 2022, under the Sixth Memorandum of Understanding, Cambodian rice exports to China reached 45%. It is believed that under the efforts of both sides, the volume of production, processing and export of Cambodian rice to the Chinese market will break even higher.
Kan Kunthy, CEO of the Cambodian Agricultural Corporation, said he hoped Chinese enterprises could directly invest or co-invest with Cambodian enterprises in processed agricultural products and export finished products to China.
In addition, the dialogue also invited His Excellency Khim Vuthy, Director General of the National Television of Cambodia, and Mr. Lim Chea Vutha, Founder and Director General of Fresh News, the most famous newspaper in Cambodia, and Ms. Arun, Director General of the Cambodia-China Friendship Radio to discuss the expansion. Cooperation in disseminating agricultural information of the two countries now as well as in the future.
