More than 1,000 students receive entrepreneurship training through the New Generation Entrepreneurship Program of Cambodian Entrepreneurs
The new generation entrepreneurship training program went according to plan and ended successfully with great results and support from the students and teachers who participated in each high school, and especially this program was successful. More than 1,000 students from all five high schools received more than the expected number of students.
In the training at 5 high schools, the guest speaker, who is a successful entrepreneur, also gave an active presentation with sharing his personal experience from the first step to becoming an entrepreneur who owns a business. Many today, he shared in detail and presented important tips for the purpose of cultivating the idea of becoming an entrepreneur to the students involved.
The teachers who participated in the training program showed a strong interest in the topic of this training program, which focuses on cultivating entrepreneurial ideas for students to understand what entrepreneurship is, what is a business owner and cultivate thinking. Of students to become young entrepreneurs according to their respective skills.
Many students also expressed their appreciation for the opportunity to participate in this training, as they learned a lot about entrepreneurship, which previously did not understand what entrepreneurship is, and this training is very important for them. Young people need to understand and be well prepared to plan for the future and dare to try to follow their skills.
Khmer Entrepreneur is an institution established by the Ministry of Economy and Finance for the purpose of working directly with partner institutions and stakeholders in promoting the entrepreneurial ecosystem in Cambodia. The vision of Cambodian entrepreneurs is to become a national nursery for the promotion of local entrepreneurship in order to create a number of new businesses and small and medium enterprises with potential in the priority areas of the Royal Government.
With this in mind, Cambodian entrepreneurs have selected four major programs as a mechanism for implementing past activities, including: Entrepreneurship, Entrepreneurship, Capacity Development, Networking and Capital Support Programs.
