The US Seventh Fleet says the destroyer USS Benfold conducts routine operations in the Taiwan Strait, passing through international waters in accordance with international law. However, in a statement, the Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLA) Eastern Military Command described the move as "provocative" and said its forces were monitoring and warning US warships.
"Frequent provocations have shown that the United States is a threat to peace and stability in the Taiwan Straits and a security risk in the Taiwan Straits," the statement said. "The Eastern Military Command will remain on high alert at all times and will strictly protect its sovereignty and territorial integrity."
The USS Benfold also sailed and operated in disputed waters in the South China Sea last week. The presence of US warships near the Taiwan Strait has often angered China, calling it a sign of support for Taiwan, which Beijing considers one of its provinces.
