Japan's US bond holdings fell to $ 1.212 trillion, the lowest level since January 2020, Reuters reported, citing US Treasury Department data. Japan's holdings were $ 1.211 trillion. In April this year, US bond holdings by Japan amounted to $ 1.218 trillion.
US Treasury data also showed that US government debt holdings by China also fell to $ 980.8 billion in May this year, the lowest level since May 2010. Comes at a time when the US debt holdings by China are $ 843.7 billion. In April this year, China owed US $ 1,003 trillion in US debt.
China, the world's second-largest economy, has cut its treasury holdings for the sixth straight month.
Although China and Japan sold US Treasury bills in May, US Treasury yields fell. Yields on the 10-year Treasury note, which began in May this year, were 2.996 percent, down about 15 basis points (0.15 percent) to 2.844 percent at the end of May.
Overall, foreign treasury holdings fell to $ 7.421 trillion in May, the lowest level since May 2021 from $ 7.455 trillion in April. According to Reuters.
