Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth sets out 16 key recommendations to boost tax collection by the General Department of Taxation
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance, presided over this morning, July 19, 2022, a meeting to review the results of tax collection for June and the first half of 2022. As well as the direction for implementation in 2022 of the General Department of Taxation.
On that occasion, the Deputy Prime Minister issued a number of recommendations for the General Department of Taxation to continue to implement more effectively in strengthening tax revenue collection.
The Deputy Prime Minister supported the measures taken by the General Department of Taxation and made the following important recommendations:
1: Continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Economy and Finance in reviewing and consulting at the inter-ministerial level so that the drafting of the new fiscal law is comprehensive and interconnected, as well as responding to the growth of the national economy. Effectiveness, efficiency, legitimacy and consistency of tax revenue management.
2: Continue to strengthen the implementation of the obligation to install beer and non-alcoholic beverage meters of domestic production enterprises (Flowmeter) in accordance with Prakas No. 010 MEF.PrK dated 12 January 2021 of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to strengthen Efficient revenue collection and ensure fair competition.
3: Study on the possibility of adjusting the tax on transportation and all kinds of vehicles for the next year.
4: Continue to strengthen tax registration and update of enterprise information, as well as continue to monitor the fulfillment of tax obligations, all active enterprises and enterprises that have just registered new taxes in order to strengthen the management of tax revenue collection and in order to reduce Related risks.
7. Continue to disseminate and strengthen the implementation of billing rules among taxpayers to ensure efficiency and transparency in the management of tax revenue collection.
8. Continue to disseminate and strengthen the implementation of the Lucky Billing Program in order to strengthen the implementation of billing rules among taxpayers through the participation of the general public.
9. Study and prepare measures to equip GPS and RFID on transport vehicles in order to manage data in tax declaration and strengthen, as well as facilitate the provision of services to taxpayers.
11. Continue to strengthen the provision of property tax services to the public by facilitating the preparation of property tax invoices for each property to the address of the property owner.
12. Strengthen tax debt recording, implement tax debt collection and tighten tax liability measures, especially large tax liabilities, by identifying priority debts.
13. Continue to strengthen the management of the enterprise, request for temporary suspension or closure and request for reopening, with measures to inspect the location of the enterprise directly, monitor the filing of declarations and strengthen the audit of documents.
14. Continue to reform and train human resources, as well as continue to strengthen the implementation of labor laws and regulations, and be gentle but firm, based on the legal aspects of providing services to taxpayers and managing tax revenue collection.
16. Continue to implement the necessary measures as set out in the Circular on the Implementation of the Law on Finance 2022 and continue to implement with attention to the revenue collection strategy 2019-2023.
