Commentary: Joe Biden's visit to the Middle East aimed at pursuing his own political interests is sure to fail.
BEIJING, July 17 (Xinhua) - US President Joe Biden arrived in Washington on Tuesday after concluding a visit to the Middle East. Insult and ridicule the major American media. The New Yorker magazine estimates that the four-day visit highlighted Biden's total failure in Middle East policy.
Please note that energy issues are an important arrangement in this visit. On the day he flew to Israel, the US Department of Labor released the US Consumer Price Index (CPI) in June 2022, showing a 9.1 percent increase over the same period in 2021. Which broke the highest record in nearly 41 years.
At the same time, the so-called US goal of strengthening the alliance in the Middle East also failed. Prior to the visit, US media had reported that Joe Biden would form a military alliance, including the Gulf states and Israel, at a "security and development" summit in Jeddah, Saudi Arabia, until its inception. "NATO in the Middle East."
Faced with the reality, the Middle East is well aware that the United States has never really paid attention to the development of the Middle East, it only considers the Middle East as a political tool and a pawn, if necessary. Also use it, if not needed, give it up.
Of course, a deeper reason lies in the fact that globalization is undergoing dramatic change and that America's national strength is declining. In particular, Joe Biden's visit to the Middle East, which was unsuccessful, showed that US politicians were plotting to view the Middle East as a pawn for geopolitical rivalry and a tool for exploitation. Personal politics has completely failed.
