(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ngin Chhay, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, said that Cambodia has been negotiating with China to establish a special channel to facilitate Cambodia to export all kinds of agricultural products to China more. Fast, which contributes to reducing the lack of market for Cambodian products.
Mr. Ngin Chhay stated this at a press conference on "Achievements of the past five years of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries" at the Office of the Council of Ministers on July 19, 2022.
According to the Director General, this special export port will enable Cambodia to export all kinds of agricultural products to China more easily and faster by accelerating the control of the 19 measures of Kovid or Technical inspection so that Cambodian agricultural products can enter the Chinese market quickly without facing damage.
Negotiations to establish this special export port take place after Cambodia's agricultural exports to China in 2022 face challenges after the country introduced a zero-Kovid policy that made it difficult to export agricultural products in particular. Fresh mangoes, both by land (Vietnam port) and by water, cause this year's mangoes to have no market and fall in price.
Mr. Ngin Chhay also said that Cambodia will also negotiate with the Chinese side to establish direct transport from Cambodia to China without passing through Singapore or Vietnam.
At the same time, Cambodia is negotiating with Korea to export fresh mangoes, as the country may be able to export about 500,000 tons of mangoes from Cambodia per year, which will help reduce the problem of no market in the future. Face.
