Cambodia-China Friendship Association Celebrates 64th Anniversary of Cambodia-China Diplomatic Relations
Diplomatic relations between the two countries, Cambodia and China, were established by His Majesty the King, His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk and Mr. Zhou Enlai, former Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China. This relationship has been continuously strengthened by the leaders of the two countries and reached the level of comprehensive strategic partnership, and is building a common destiny.
The strong ties between Cambodia and China have been demonstrated through frequent exchanges of visits between the two countries' top leaders.
China has always regarded Cambodia-China bilateral relations as a steel relationship that no one can break. Official Cambodia-China relations were established on July 19, 1958, five years after Cambodia gained independence from France.
Over the past 64 years, the traditional friendship between Cambodia and China, pioneered by the previous generation of leaders and carefully cared for by the next generation of leaders of Cambodia and China, has been widely promoted. Constantly.
The two sides have maintained close cooperation in all fields, including politics, economy, trade, culture, humanity, as well as regional and international affairs, with great achievements. Tomorrow, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum will offer cremation for Mr. Somara's wife
