Police crack down on 11 suspects and seize more than 44 kilograms of drugs in Phnom Penh and Banteay Meanchey
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Drug Department cracked down on drug trafficking, arrested 11 people and confiscated more than 44 kilograms of drugs at 5 different locations in Phnom Penh and Banteay Meanchey.
The operation was carried out under the direction of General Santibandit, National Police Commissioner General, and General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the Anti-Drug Crime Plan, under the direct command of Lt. Gen. Lek Vannak, Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes.
Goal 1: At the riverside park in front of Preah Sisowath Quay in Sangkat Chey Chumneas, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, arrested a suspect and seized about 1 kg of drugs.
Target 2: At Condo Queen, Room 602, 6th Floor, Street 308, Village 5, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkar Mon, Phnom Penh, arrested one suspect and seized more than 3 kg of drugs.
Goal 3: Continued to expand the territory to Banteay Meanchey province in front of Hak Huot 2 Hotel in Samaki Meanchey Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province, arrested 3 suspects and seized 20 large packages of drugs about 20 kg.
Target 4: At house 803 in Samaki Meanchey village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, arrested a suspect and confiscated 3 large packages of drugs, about 3 kg.
Target 5: At Chamkar hut in Kilometer 4 village, Sangkat Phsar Kandal, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province, 4 suspects were arrested and 20 large packages of 20 kg of drugs were confiscated.
