Duke Kith Meng Asks to Accelerate the Implementation of Chakra Economic Plans Asean
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Kith Meng, President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and Chairman of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council, on July 19, 2022, delivered a speech and intervened during a cross-sectoral dialogue for economic implementation plans. Online Circular Economy with the participation of ASEAN Economic Leaders, Research Units and Stakeholders of ASEAN Member States.
The dialogue was held to exchange information and good experiences of the Chakra economy in order to seek cooperation from all relevant sectors and identify priority areas and programs that can be achieved quickly for implementation in the ASEAN region, focusing on The three main sectors are agriculture, energy and transportation.
Duke Kith Meng welcomed the ASEAN Secretariat's efforts to implement the Chakra Economy and made the following input on behalf of the ASEAN Business Advisory Council:
* Propose to expedite the implementation of the Chakra Economic Plan by incorporating high-impact projects that can be implemented within two or three years across the ASEAN region, as the Chakra Economic Framework is already in place in the country. ASEAN members also have roadmaps and strategic documents.
* Priorities and strategies that promote economic vitality should be identified through fundraising to support economic growth, especially to support the transition of micro, small and medium enterprises.
Develop a concrete and viable economic implementation plan, especially focusing on reducing the development gap in ASEAN member countries.
* Support the various priority sectors stated in the implementation plan, including: agriculture, energy and transportation.
Mr. Say Sam Al Donates Candles and Gifts to 40 Monks in Preah Sihanouk Province
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Chairman of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Government Working Group, brought candles and gifts to 40 pagodas throughout Preah Sihanouk Province.
The annual rainy season is held during the rainy season, when people as well as monks find it difficult to travel and travel from place to place. The Buddha enlightened the monks to enter the rainy season for three months to study the Dharma, and the Buddhists will support the monks during the three-month rainy season.
The rainy season is a time for monks to practice the Dharma. During this time, the monks did not have to go far. Another important thing that the Buddha disciplined for the monks during the rainy season is that it is strictly forbidden to leave the pagoda for more than seven days.
At the time of the Buddha, during the rainy season, monks and nuns had to stay in the pagoda without having to perform the Ben Bhat ceremony. However, in the present era, because the supply is not enough, so the monks can go to Ben Bat to study, to go to participate in other social activities without any apathy, as they used to say, not to go astray. When going back to the monastery is wrong (before dawn).
It should be noted that each pagoda received a pair of Preah Vossa candles, food and suffixes of 1 million riels.
