Preah Vihear Provincial Public Works Department Continues to Clean Dust and Garbage in Drainage at Sraem Roundabout to Avoid Road Flooding in the Rainy Season
(Preah Vihear): The team of Drainage Office and Wastewater Treatment Station of Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport this morning, July 19, 2022, cleaned dust and garbage in sewer along National Road 62 km. 212 + 000 Sraem roundabout, Sraem commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, to avoid flooding on the road this rainy season.
According to Mr. Samleang Try, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province, he confirmed to Fresh News Agency in Preah Vihear Province, "Our water causes some sewers to be clogged and unable to flow in time, causing some places to have water for a long time, disrupting the business and travel of the people."
At the same time, he said that, looking at the actual situation, which started from natural factors, he also instructed the team of the Office of Drainage and Wastewater Treatment Station of the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport to clean the dust and sewage in the sewer. Roundabout town, Sraem commune, to avoid flooding of roads during the rainy season caused by sewer blockage.
Mr. Samleang Try also stated that as the rainy season approaches, the activities of the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport seem to have doubled, such as road maintenance, drainage, and clearing of trees on both sides of the road. ..... and so on.
He said that during the rainy season, the road was damaged as follows: The chicken coop, the sewer began to be blocked, and the national river began to grow, but following the instructions of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport and Mr. Prak Sovann, Governor of Preah Vihear Province. Pay close attention to regular repairs and maintenance so as not to disturb the travel and living of the people.
