Lifelong Learning Center Building in Kampong Speu Province Officially Inaugurated, Minister of Education: Useful for all students and citizens to study, research and gain additional technical skills
(Kampong Speu): The Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, said that he was very proud of his nieces and nephews who are students studying at Hun Sen Chambok High School for the opportunity to get a non-formal education center. Research on vehicle electronics developed and sponsored by LION CLUB of the Republic of Korea.
He said this while presiding over the inauguration ceremony of the Lifelong Learning Center in Hun Sen Chambok High School in Vallis Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province on July 18, 2022. The building will be a place to learn and apply directly to English and Korean electronics.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron emphasized that "This center is very useful for students and all citizens to study and gain technical knowledge to have the opportunity to earn money to increase family life to a certain extent."
Speaking on the occasion, Dr. also reminded that Kampong Speu is a province that was previously a conflict zone with weapons, hot battle, insecurity and full of landmines all over the land, but under the win-win policy of The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has also turned the area into a potential economic, tourism and agro-industrial area, and in the future the province will also become a commercial area.
Along with this remarkable growth, schools that nurture human resource knowledge have also grown from elementary school to college, from rural to urban.
Along with this growth, informal vocational training centers have also been established, making students and residents of this poor province extremely lucky to have the opportunity to receive Korean and English language training. Techniques for repairing cars and electronics, and especially after graduation, you may have the opportunity to work with a local Korean company or have the opportunity to go to work in Korea.
