Police arrest scammer for president of Cambodian Aquaculture Association in Siem Reap province
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap provincial police have arrested a man in connection with a scam involving the president of the Cambodian Fishermen's Association, who is involved in a business of collecting fish from farmers around Siem Reap province.
The suspect in this scam, 44-year-old Sok Yorn, was arrested on July 18, 2022, according to a complaint filed by Sok Raden, known as the Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Cambodian Aquaculture Association.
Mr. Sok Raden confirmed that he really lost the scam of Sok Yorn, husband and wife, Sin Phalla, as they asked him to join a business to buy fish from the fishermen around Siem Reap. .
At the same time, Mr. Sok Raden appealed to aquaculture as well as fish farmers not to be deceived.
About 80% of teachers at Thnakre High School in Kratie Province went on strike, demanding that the Ministry of Education remove the principal
(Kratie): More than 80 percent of teachers at Thmor Kre High School in Thmor Kre commune, Chit Borei district, Kratie province, went on strike to demand that the leaders of the Ministry change the principal because the principal did not know. Control and take sides, the school will deteriorate to zero.
The case of teachers refusing to teach from July 14, 2022 to July 18 has not yet started teaching, leaving students to miss school and stop scattering the whole school, especially grade students. 12 The exam day is approaching and the teacher refuses to teach.
According to the teachers' group, Mr. Sun Meng Kan, the current principal of Thmor Kre High School, is not in control, he is led by a partisan, he does whatever he wants, he never discusses with the teachers or the deputy principal. Who listens to the opinions of the staff.
He added that at the end of the year, students from 7th to 11th grade had failed the exam, and the class teacher had already failed them. Whichever class, this is the problem he leads.
The teachers would like to request the director of the department or the Ministry of Education to take measures to change the principal of this school so that they can start teaching if he is allowed to continue to manage the school without any progress.
In relation to the above issue, Mr. Sun Meng Kan, Principal of Thmor Kre High School, confirmed by telephone that more than half of the teachers did not attend the strike, and the number of cases where the teachers did not attend the strike was as follows: 2 cases:
Case 1: He went to a workshop at a technical school, he sent a teacher, including three of him, to school for 10 days, and the fact that he went to school made the staff jealous of some of his staff. He did not go to school because he did not teach at Thmor Kre High School for only two years. Instead, he hired a new teacher.
Parents of students are very worried about the teachers' refusal to attend classes, causing their children to miss school, especially students who have failed exams and diploma exams. They asked the Ministry and the leadership to resolve this issue as soon as possible so that their children can return to school on time.
Lay Bora, director of the Kratie Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports, said that he had assigned the district office to inspect and is preparing a report, and this evening the department will visit tomorrow. The department was aware of this case from the first day and the department is looking for measures to prevent the school from closing.
