General Sao Sokha Reminds Some Background of the Establishment of the Gendarmerie
(Kampong Chhnang): Once again, General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, recalled the number of issues of the establishment of the Gendarmerie. The remarks of General Sao Sokha were made on the occasion of the 29th anniversary of the establishment of the National Gendarmerie on July 14, 2022 in Kampong Chhnang Province in the presence of General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
According to General Sao Sokha, from April 17, 1975, the Gendarmerie was abolished, as in other societies in Democratic Kampuchea, and its staff was one of the targets. That the Democratic Kampuchea regime had to look ahead and destroy it.
After the first elections from 23 to 28 May 1993, organized by the United Nations Transitional Authority in Cambodia (UNTAC). According to the decree dated July 14, 1993, the establishment of the General Staff of the Cambodian National Army in the organizational structure of the General Staff also includes the Armed Forces. Therefore, since then, the Royal Gendarmerie has decided to re-designate July 14 as the Royal Gendarmerie Day.
On December 21, 1994, the Royal Government issued Sub-Decree No. 77 on the Roles, Duties and General Structure of the Royal Cambodian Gendarmerie and the Code of Criminal Procedure, which was approved by the National Assembly on June 7, 2007, clearly defining the powers of Royal Armed Forces in the second book, content 4, chapter 4.
According to the above legal documents, 29 years ago, the Gendarmerie has built both hard and soft infrastructure and performed the duties and responsibilities set out in the legal documents to contribute to security, order and crime. Strengthen the implementation of building the Kingdom of Cambodia as a country of the rule of law.
