Bali: Indonesia has lifted tariffs on all palm oil products until Aug. 31 to boost exports and reduce inventories, an finance ministry official said last weekend. According to Reuters.
The decision to abolish the export tax of the world's largest palm oil exporter could push prices further down, which has already fallen by about 50 percent since the end of April, to its lowest level in years. More than a year.
Indonesian palm oil producers are facing increasing stockpiles since the country imposed a three-week export ban until May 23 to reduce domestic cooking oil prices.
Since the lifting of the export ban, Jakarta has enacted a mandatory domestic sales law known as the Domestic Market Obligation (DMO) to keep products locally sourced for cooking. .
At the same time, the country has tried to release stocks by reducing export tariffs and implementing export acceleration programs, but exports have been slow and the company has blamed the problem on DMO laws and shortcomings. Shipping ships.
Vietnam's central bank sells $ 13 billion to stabilize exchange rate
According to VDSC, the central bank's actions are aimed at curbing the depreciation of the Vietnamese dong, easing pressure on foreign exchange rates and balancing the supply and demand of the dollar in the exchange market. Domestic.
In a context where most currencies have depreciated sharply against the US dollar after the US Federal Reserve raised interest rates, the dong has fallen by only about 2 percent this year, indicating that the dong is stable and stable. Listed among the lowest priced currencies in the Asia-Pacific region. According to Vietnam News.
