Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Article People in Area 3 in Koh Russey Commune, Prolay Meas Commune, Kampong Leng District, Kampong Chhnang Province Receive Both Electricity and Legal Benefits
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Keo Rattanak, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) on July 18, 2022, attended the handover ceremony and inauguration ceremony of the project to supply solar power. 162 kilowatts donated by Snetech Group and Chin Group to Electricite du Cambodge in Koh Russey village, Prolay Meas commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province.
Mr. Keo Rattanak stated that in the area of Koh Russey village, Prolay Meas commune, Kampong Leng district, Kampong Chhnang province, this area has never had a large amount of electricity because it is a remote area where people have to cross the river by boat, which makes people Very difficult. And the people in this area are also in the three areas of the Tonle Sap Lake where they have settled for a long time.
The minister said that in the past, people in this area had access to electricity through the use of small solar panels on the roof, but now they have a solar power system with 360 interconnected solar panels with a power of more than 450 watts. In one panel that can supply 173 houses, more than 200 families.
He added that this solar power system is another new gift for the people, in addition to recognizing the legal right to enjoy in three areas, which is the decision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
"Today, they have received a second gift: access to this clean energy solar system, and in the future we will extend it to the national grid, which will allow them to do so," he said. They are more widely used in agriculture.
Minister Keo Rattanak added, "The people have expressed their happiness and appreciation for the consideration of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, and they have changed their minds. "Continuing to support the election for the Cambodian People's Party."
Please be informed that the 162KW solar power supply project is a gift from Snettek Group and Chin Group to Electricite du Cambodge. The project will cost a total of $ 489,485, of which $ 370,000 will be spent by Snetech Group and Chin Group and $ 11.90,000 will be allocated by EDC for the purchase of land. Developed steadily and resiliently
In the first half of this year, China's gross domestic product (GDP) was 56.2642 trillion yuan, up 2.5 percent year on year, according to official figures. Compared to the same period of 2021. Given that in April and May, key production demand indicators fell, China achieved such a result is not easy, this shows the resilience of the Chinese economy.
Since this year, large-scale international commodity prices, especially food and energy prices, have remained high, which has had a significant impact on China's import-led inflation. Therefore, China has used the uncertainty of supply and the balance of domestic prices to counteract the uncertainty of the external environment, cultivating good food and energy, which has precisely guaranteed the stability of basic commodity prices.
In 2022, China's total summer food production will reach 147.39 million tons, an increase of more than 1.434 million tons, compared to 2021, an increase of 1 percent, which provides a strong support for price stability. Commodities, as well as maintaining the living standards of the people, stabilize the general state of the economy and withstand the uncertainties of the external environment.
In addition, in the context of the slowdown in global trade growth, China's total exports and imports increased by 9.4 percent year on year in the same period in 2021. Exports rose 13.2 percent.
In the future, according to the situation, prevention and control of Kovid 19 disease will be better and policy implementation achievements will continue to emerge. Many of the reforms will play a bigger role.
What is the Chinese economy like? The answer to this question is the Chinese economy in the first half of this year, which has overcome obstacles and achieved steady growth. The nation's resilient economy has also boosted the Chinese people's confidence in overcoming all kinds of challenges.
In the second half of this year, there are still many uncertainties, and China's economic recovery is also based on a weak foundation, if we want to maintain economic stability in general, we must continue to work hard. The more difficult it is, the more courageous it must be to move forward.
At present, the good trend of the Chinese economy, which has been stable for a long time, has not changed. The strong resilience of the economy is a clear feature. An appropriate framework will brighten the future of the global economy, which is becoming more and more opaque day by day.
