The National Assembly of Cambodia was honored to address the meeting, giving a number of key recommendations, including: The role of MPs in ensuring that humanitarian corridors for food, medicine and other essentials are open to the common people at all times. Ensuring the production chain, distribution channels, key products such as seeds, fertilizers and other fuels must be exempt from sanctions.
Cambodia Peace Support Session and Initiatives Call for the Establishment of the Institute for Peace and Food Science at the Request of Cambodia for Scientific Research and Strong Recommendations for the Implementation of the Peace and Food Security Program Government, parliament and the private sector, especially public-private partnerships, can provide key solutions to the challenges of peace and food security.
At the same time, the President of the National Assembly of Morocco also confirmed the acceptance of the invitation of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia, to lead a high-level delegation of the Moroccan Parliament to visit and attend the 1st ASEAN Inter-Parliamentary Assembly (AIPA). 43 in the Kingdom of Cambodia in November 2022.
