Israel to boost Asian flights after Saudi Arabia launches airspace
(Jerusalem): Israeli airlines plan to expand and open new routes to India and other Asian destinations after Saudi Arabia opened its airspace to all airlines, a move that will save on fuel costs. Fuel and reduce flight time. This is according to the release by Reuters on Sunday, July 17, 2022.
Riyadh on Friday said its airspace would be open to all airlines, including the Asian route, which previously had the Saudi Arabian corridor for offshore destinations only.
Israel and Arkia Airlines El Al said on Sunday that they had already applied for a permit to fly over Saudi airspace, which would cut flights by about two and a half hours to India and Thailand.
The current route to those destinations popular to Israel by Saudi Arabia is flying south over the Red Sea around Yemen.
