Speaking of a car that the driver fled into the potato collection area, when the mobile scales came in to drive to the destination, there were some people who claimed to be corn farmers and businessmen. Collecting corn to sell to Thailand came out to prevent it from being removed. They demanded that the Cambodian authorities release the car back to Thailand, arguing that if the Thai trader's car was seized, the Thai trader would no longer come to buy their corn.
Despite explanations of Cambodian legal aspects regarding transportation, Battambang Provincial Prosecutor Keo Socheat, as well as mobile scales officials and district authorities, asked them to disperse the protest pending a settlement. They refuse to dissolve. Protesters continue to demand the release of the overweight Thai trader.
