In a press release explaining the guidelines received by Fresh News, it was stated that in the context of the Kovid-19 crisis, the Royal Government of Cambodia has launched a series of necessary measures in a proactive and responsible manner in order to continue Manage the Kovid-19 epidemic and continue to help balance business in the worst-affected areas.
At the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia continues to maintain high vigilance, although Kovid-19 is in a controlled state, and has recently launched a national Kovid-19 vaccination campaign for the booster dose. 3, 4 and 5) aimed at increasing individual immunity as well as socio-economic immunity.
In particular, for the tourism sector, despite the increase in the number of domestic and international tourists, issues such as the continued threat of Kovid-19 and the rise in global inflation remain pressures on the growing number of tourists. Many operators in the tourism sector continue to face challenges in their business.
In this spirit, along with the introduction of measures, policies and strategic plans to control the spread of Kovid-19, especially in the direction of continuing to promote business-business balance in the severely affected areas, the Royal Government understands The need to put in place additional measures to further manage and assess the impact as well as support the recovery of tourism in these difficult circumstances.
In this regard, the Royal Government has cooperated with the private sector and relevant ministries and institutions to introduce additional measures for the tourism sector as follows:
* Second, continue to provide mediation by freezing debt figures by the end of 2019 and excluding penalties for 2022 for tourism.
* Third: Promote businesses in the tourism sector, prepare skills development programs for their own staff and be able to request financial support from the Skills Development Fund (SDF) project as needed. All relevant ministries and institutions must implement this instruction in accordance with their competencies in the most effective manner.
