Deputy PM Hor Namhong: Cambodia reaffirms support for China on Global Development Initiative and Global Security Initiative
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong, Co-Chair of the Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee, said that Cambodia has reaffirmed its support for China on the Global Development Initiative and the Global Security Initiative.
During the meeting, Mr. Hor Namhong praised and thanked the two secretaries for coordinating the work of the Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee, especially the implementation of the action plan of the Cambodia-China Common Destiny Community, which was approved and decided by Samdech Techo Director. Minister Hun Sen and President Xi Jinping, despite being in the midst of facing the Kovid-19 crisis.
The Deputy Prime Minister stated that Cambodia will continue to adhere to the one-China policy.
"Cambodia would like to express its support and wish the Chinese side the success of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, and reiterate its support for China on the Global Development Initiative and the Global Security Initiative." This is according to Mr. Hor Namhong.
The Global Development Initiative was proposed by Chinese President Xi Jinping at the 76th UN General Assembly in Beijing. Xi set out this initiative to adhere to the priority of development, adhere to people-centered, adhere to the environment and environment, adhere to innovation, and adhere to the harmony of people and nature.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong made the request as he and Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China and co-chair of the Chinese side, convened a plenary session of the Coordinating Committee. Cambodia-China Intergovernmental Government via video on July 14, 2022.
Such a request to China from the Cambodian side is an important point in the field of culture, tourism and education at a meeting held at the Peace Palace of the Council of Ministers to implement the comprehensive strategic partnership cooperation to Implement the plan for the next two years (2022-2024).
