The Minister extended a warm welcome to the Ambassador and his colleagues who visited the Ministry of Commerce and thanked Myanmar for its support to Cambodia as the chair of ASEAN 2022.
On that occasion, the Minister informed about the progress of organizing the 19 priority economic achievements of Cambodia under the pillars of the ASEAN Economic Community and requested Myanmar to continue to participate in organizing and supporting the goal to be achieved successfully under the ASEAN Chairmanship of Cambodia.
In addition, the Minister also requested the Myanmar side to consider the possibility of encouraging the import of potential agricultural products from Cambodia, such as: dried mangoes, bananas, avocados, cashew nuts, sweet potatoes, peppers, sesame and palm sugar to the Myanmar market.
At the same time, the Minister also informed the Ambassador about the business and investment potential in Cambodia, as well as the sharp strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia to restore and develop the Cambodian economy, which makes the Cambodian economy expected to grow. 6% for 2023 and 7% next year.
In response, the Ambassador expressed his deep gratitude to Minister Pan Sosak and the leadership of the Ministry of Commerce for allowing him and his colleagues to meet to discuss the work, and the Ambassador reiterated Myanmar's commitment to continue supporting Cambodia as chair of ASEAN in 2022
At the same time, the Ambassador expressed his commitment to strengthen and expand trade cooperation between the two countries and bring the Minister's proposal to the leadership. In addition, the Ambassador requested the Cambodian side to consider the possibility of promoting cooperation in other important areas, including: avoiding double taxation and promoting and protecting investment between the two sides.
At the end, the two sides exchanged views on promoting bilateral trade, promoting closer cooperation between the two countries' chambers of commerce and the private sector through business matching, exchange of business visits, exhibition activities. As well as identifying potential goods between the two countries to further boost exports.
In particular, the two sides expressed their commitment to continue cooperating, coordinating and promoting business and investment activities to boost economic and trade growth between the two countries.
