Cambodia sends 22 more Vietnamese Volunteers and Specialists back to their homeland
(Kandal): After the discovery and excavation of the remains of Vietnamese volunteers and experts in the province of Kandal province in the 21st phase of the dry season 20221-2022, 22 more remains were sent back to Vietnam.
Brigadier General Ho Minh Phuong expressed his deep gratitude to local authorities at all levels, the three armed forces and local people for their cooperation in excavating the remains of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army to repatriate them. The motherland is getting results now.
On behalf of the Governor of Kandal Province, Mr. Nop Dara expressed his deep gratitude to the heroism of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army for sacrificing fresh flesh and blood in cooperation with the Cambodian National Salvation Front to liberate Cambodia from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
He also praised the Cambodian-Vietnamese professional forces and local authorities for facilitating the excavation commission, which was difficult to navigate due to the progress of the building. Exploration.
At the same time, he urged the authorities as well as the people of Vietnam to provide comprehensive information to make this work easier for the Commission to successfully complete the 22nd plan.
It should be noted that during the handover ceremony and repatriation of the remains of Vietnamese volunteers and experts, the delegation also lit incense in front of the relics site and invited monks to come and perform according to the Buddhist tradition. For the happiness, prosperity and full peace of Cambodia-Vietnam as well.
