The National Bank of Cambodia and the Bank of France jointly promote human resource capacity development and financial system strengthening
(Singapore): The National Bank of Cambodia and the Bank of France have signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on enhancing human resource capacity development and strengthening the financial system.
The signing of the MoU is based on the successful implementation of the MoUs signed by the two central banks since 2006.
The new MoU aims to enhance human resource capacity development and further strengthen the financial system. The MoU will also promote international cooperation and exchange of experiences for the benefit of the two central banks.
Mr. Chea Chanto said, "The National Bank of Cambodia and the Bank of France have established a strong bilateral relationship on a long-term and trustworthy partnership, and I firmly believe that the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding "Recently, we will further strengthen technical cooperation for the benefit of both sides."
"We are pleased to have the presence of the French Central Bank Representative in Asia, which will facilitate the implementation of the MoU in line with the expected goals," he said.
