Cambodia's cashew policy, which is expected to address challenges in the cashew sector, such as farmers' cultivation and markets, is currently undergoing scrutiny, which will lead to a submission to the upcoming Plenary Council of Ministers. Face.
On July 14, 2022, Mr. Reach Ra, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Commerce and Deputy Chairman of the Cambodian Cashew Policy Joint Working Group, led the working group to attend a technical meeting to review and discuss the draft national policy on cashews at the office. The Minister is chaired by Mr. Ly Chantola, Vice Chairman of the Council of Jurists and Mr. Na Rana Rith Anandayat, Deputy Chairman of the Economic, Social and Cultural Council as Co-Chair.
Mr. Reach Ra stated that the meeting agreed and completed the complete review of the draft National Policy on Cashew 2022-2027 and prepared the procedure to be submitted to the inter-ministerial meeting before requesting to submit to the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers. Coming soon.
