The General Commission of the National Police sends a message of condolences on the death of Mr. Ung Kiet, Supreme Personal Adviser to the King
(Phnom Penh): The General Commissioner of the National Police has sent a message to Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, and her family regarding the death of Ung Kiet, the King's personal adviser to the King.
In a condolence message signed by Acting National Police Commissioner General Chhay Sinarith, he stated: "Cambodia passed away on Wednesday, the 15th day of the month of Asat in the year of Karl Chatva Sak, BE 2566, which is on July 13, 2022 at 11:50 at the age of 98 years old due to old age."
The General Commission of the National Police further stated that in this sad time, we would like to express our condolences for the loss of Mr. Ung Kiet, an outstanding human resource full of professional knowledge and high experience. He sacrificed his physical, mental and mental strength to serve the nation for generations for the national good, religion, and the King.
We would like to dedicate our prayers to the sacred objects in the world and the merits of the Buddha, the Dharma, the monks to help nurture and take care of the soul of Mr. Ung Kiet to go to his death, not to be wasted.
Chinese family tradition enhances national innovation
In Chinese, country means family, and the Chinese people always value family. As the old saying goes, "Under our sky, family is very important." Along with the continuous reform and opening up, as well as further economic and social development, the living standards of the Chinese people have also improved, and new changes have taken place in the structure of families and lifestyles of the people throughout. Country as well.
Confucius stated that "in order to properly govern the state, it is necessary to manage the family first," which is a clear affirmation of the core values of China's development that motivates and motivates young people to take turns in Increasing the achievements of the nation in line with the trends of science and technology.
To turn China into a digital China, Chinese youths who have joined forces with the nations of the world are entering the pace of accelerating science and technology, in line with Meng Jie's view that "it is a smarter choice." "In the use of favorable circumstances, rather than relying solely on one's intellect."
Historical experience has shown that countries that have modernized by making the best use of the scientific and technological revolution have young people with strong scientific and technological foundations, and countries that have become active in Developing the world by taking advantage of the revolution is all about advanced technology in key areas.
Science and technology respond to the needs of time and have a global impact. In today's world, the scientific and technological revolution is gaining momentum. Chinese youth will share a new generation of information technology through robotics and smart technology, strengthening the chain of innovation more flexible.
Overall, Chinese youth rank among the youth of advanced countries in science and technology, and innovation is playing an increasingly important role in supporting and leading their economic and social development in line with the vision of a prosperous society. Appropriate by striving to overcome all obstacles in overcoming the Chinese-style socialist victory and achieving the Chinese dream of restoring the greatness of the Chinese nation.
Families trained by Chinese successors today are working harder to bring all Chinese families together to promote the healthy growth of the next generation, ensuring development. Digital China and raise the level of civilization, Chinese society and the whole world.
