General knowledge: Which country consumes the most fuel in the world?
(USA): The use and production of fossil fuels is increasing day by day according to the economic activity and consumption needs of each country. Do you know which countries use the most fuel and which countries produce the most energy?
The most fuel-intensive country is the United States, with an average consumption of 20.54 million barrels per day. This is according to data from the US-based International Energy Data Analysis and Management Unit (EIA).
After the United States, China consumes an average of 14 million barrels per day, while Japan consumes an average of nearly 40,000 barrels per day.
In addition, India and Russia are also the largest oil consumers after the three countries.
