"We are seeing the negative effects of that war on every corner of the globe, especially on energy prices and rising food insecurity," she added.
Mr. Keut Rith: All amendments to the Constitution are to fill the gaps in the Constitution and ensure the protection of national interests (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, said that all amendments to the Constitution are to fill the gaps in the Constitution and To ensure the protection of the interests of the whole nation.
In a press conference on the draft of the Constitution on the amendment of Article 8 of the Constitution and the Constitution on the afternoon of July 14, 2022, Mr. Keut Rith stated that "All amendments, including the First to Ninth Amendments "Anything else is done to: First, fill in the gaps in the constitution and second, to ensure the protection of national interests."
He said that the guarantee of national interests is two jobs, including:
* First: To ensure that all institutions run smoothly, sustainably, without any setbacks, in order to be able to fulfill their mission to help society in accordance with the law * and secondly, to ensure that the process works in accordance with the regime Liberal, multi-party democracy under a parliamentary or constitutional monarchy is to ensure peace, stability, national sustainability and the peace of the Cambodian people.
The Minister of Justice also considered those who criticized the amendment of the Constitution as unfair to be unfair.
The Minister considered that those who criticized that the amendment of the Constitution was a bad amendment were those who did not speak for the benefit of Cambodia.
"We raise the pride of the Khmer nation for his politicians to purify themselves through such principles. In relation to the leadership, the country's highest authority, it is accused of being a bad amendment," he said.
Minister Keut Rith added that in addition to the appointment of the Prime Minister, the President of the National Assembly, the President of the Senate and the President of the Constitutional Council are of the same Khmer nationality. Cambodian law also stipulates that the NEC chairman and all nine NEC members have the same Cambodian nationality.
He said: "Determining him to have the same Khmer nationality, what is bad for the national interest, please confirm that when we have two nationalities, we are under both laws, and the law of any country always obliged that citizens. "Each has their own patriotic obligations."
He questioned which country he would serve if the incumbent prime minister had dual citizenship. He also asked if there is any country in the world that allows the top leaders to have a few nationalities?
It should be noted that the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which was promulgated on September 24, 1993, has been amended nine times in a row. This amendment aims to ensure national sustainability as well as ensure the national interests and the people of Cambodia, including:
* The first amendment promulgated by the Royal Kram dated 14 July 1994 to delegate the King's signature to the Acting Head of State
* The third amendment promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 0701/11 dated 28 July 2001 to give the King the right to create and award national medals or medals
* Fourth Amendment promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 0605/018 dated 19 June 2005 to amend the quorum of the National Assembly and the Senate to facilitate the administrative process of both institutions
* Fifth Amendment promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 0306/006 dated March 09, 2006 to revise the procedure for establishing the National Assembly leadership and form the Royal Government
* Sixth Amendment promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 0208/008 dated 15 February 2008 to revise the territorial administration of the Kingdom of Cambodia
* The 7th Amendment, promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 1014/022, dated October 23, 2014, to grant the status of an institution as stated in the Constitution to the National Election Committee
* Eighth Amendment promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 0218/002 dated 27 February 2018 to promote Khmer national values in the cause of defending national independence, national sovereignty and national unity against interference from Outside
