US provides over $ 360,000 to Cambodia for Preah Vihear temple renovation
(Phnom Penh): The United States Government has announced more than $ 360,000 to support the Preah Vihear Temple Restoration Project. This is according to a press release from the US Embassy in Cambodia.
"At the ceremony, Ambassador Murphy announced a new US Government grant through the Ambassador's Fund for Cultural Preservation of $ 360,800 for renovations," the statement said. Temple of Preah Vihear. "This is in addition to the $ 406,000 already provided by the US government for the preservation of this historic temple in northern Cambodia."
Mr Murphy said the United States is proud of its contribution to Cambodia's efforts to preserve Cambodia's cultural heritage and to our joint efforts to repatriate invaluable artifacts. From the United States.
The United States has a fund known as the Ambassador Fund for Cultural Preservation for organizations or partners applying for funding such as: Traffic prevention, antiquities, promotion of protection or preservation of heritage and other works according to the wishes of the applicant, only related to the preservation of culture.
He said that in the past, many departments of the Ministry of Culture have also requested funding from the fund to help cultural conservation projects.
"Today's ceremony is a testament to the strong relationship between the United States and the Ministry of Culture and the Arts," Kritenbrink said. "US initiatives, such as the Ambassador's Fund for Cultural Preservation, demonstrate our long-standing support for the restoration of culturally important historical sites for Cambodia."
Dr. Phoeung Sakona closed the ceremony by expressing sincere gratitude for the US Government's contribution of time and resources in the fight against the illegal trade in cultural property.
"We look forward to continuing our co-operation in our investigations and efforts, training and exchanging information and skills as we rediscover our nation's precious assets," she said.
The United States has provided more than $ 5 million to the Royal Government of Cambodia since 2001 for cultural preservation, including more than $ 3.5 million for the preservation and restoration of the Phnom Bak Kheng temple in Siem Reap and for the Tuol Sleng Museum. . This is according to a press release from the US Embassy.
