ILO continues to support the Ministry of Tourism in training tourism professionals in Siem Reap, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey
(Phnom Penh): The International Labor Organization (ILO), through the ILO-China Partnership Project, has continued to support the Ministry of Tourism in training tourism professionals in Siem Reap, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey provinces after both sides succeeded in The first training of tourism professionals in Siem Reap.
Mr. Liu Yuthong stated that the ILO will continue to support the Ministry of Tourism through the Hoka Project Management Committee to promote additional training in Siem Reap, Battambang and Banteay Meanchey. The International Labor Organization (ILO) will provide training of 125 trainers and 150 professionals in food and beverage service, front office and housekeeping skills.
Secretary of State Pak Sokhom expressed his pleasure at the continued support of the ILO to the Ministry of Tourism, as well as the Hoka Project Management Committee for additional training of Cambodian tourism professionals, which will support the Ministry of Tourism's strategy to strengthen Develop tourism professional skills in a new context, focusing on three approaches: Recover, Retrain and Retain.
The Secretary of State thanked the International Labor Organization (ILO) for supporting the Ministry of Tourism through the Hoka Project Management Committee to train tourism professionals, especially current staff, in the past the ILO has supported the training of trainers. 24 people and 31 experts in food and beverage service and training within the tourism business to more than 200 professionals.
Mr. Chuob Ratana said that in the meeting with the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia, the ILO side also discussed plans to promote cooperation between tourism vocational training schools in Cambodia and tourism vocational training schools in China. Currently, the ILO has about 26 partner vocational training schools.
In addition, the ILO also requested the Hoka Project Management Committee to consider the possibility of conducting Chinese cooking courses for young Cambodian chefs, with the ILO sending Chinese chefs to train in Cambodia or sending young chefs. Cambodian children go to China for internships.
In relation to the tourism professional training, Mr. Chuob Ratana added that every time there is a training session, there is a lot of interest from the trainees who are employees or have worked in the tourism sector, officials of the Department of Tourism in the provinces. Especially in the northeastern region of Preah Vihear, Siem Reap, as well as provinces around the Tonle Sap Lake.
Russia criticizes Western over arms training to Ukrainian troops
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russia's foreign ministry on Thursday criticized the United States and Britain for helping to train Ukraine's armed forces, calling the move part of a "hybrid war" between NATO members. (NATO) to oppose Russia. This is according to the publication by Reuters on Thursday, July 14, 2022
At a news conference, Russian Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Maria Zakharova said Washington had provided Ukraine with "training" for Kiev forces to use US-made HIMARS missile systems. She noted that long-range and more precise missiles than other artillery pieces were being widely used by Ukrainian forces.
Zakharova also criticized Britain's decision to bring hundreds of Ukrainian troops to Britain for weapons training. She stressed that London's initiative to train up to 10,000 Ukrainian troops in the coming months is part of the West's "hybrid war" against Moscow.
Both Russia and Ukraine have denied targeting attacks on civilians and civilians in the nearly five-month-long conflict. While the US HIMARS missile system operating in Ukraine will increase to eight by mid-July, military analysts believe that such advanced weapons could greatly help Ukraine change the state of war.
