BEIJING, July 13 (Xinhua) - China's General Administration of Customs released a score of 19.8 trillion yuan on China's foreign trade and imports in the morning on July 13. 9.4 percent compared to the same period of 2021.
Exports rose 13.2 percent and imports rose 4.8 percent. In particular, in US dollars, the growth rate of China's exports in June reached 17.9 percent, exceeding the estimates of most domestic and foreign market institutions.
In the first three months of this year, China achieved a steady start, up 10.7 percent, followed by the Yangtze and Zhujiang Delta, which are represented by Shanghai and a major foreign trade area. China's main outbreak of 19 epidemics of Kovid, with moderate strikes on exports and imports in April.
Considering the impact of the 19 cases of Kuwait as a test of China's foreign trade in coping with the pressure, the strong recovery in May and June was good in this exam. It is also a strong rejection of the words of the outside world, which often propagates that the Chinese economy is in decline.
The port is also very busy. According to the report, from June to today, on average, every day, the Shanghai Customs Administration can report at the customs office for about 60,000 exports and imports, an increase of 3.44 times compared to Mid-April.
This shows that the world needs China. Developments over the past several decades have made China the only country in the world to have more than 500 industries in all sectors of the UN. In the world, more than 220 Chinese industrial products rank first in the world.
