In the closing ceremony of the convention! Ministry of Tourism launches 11-point work plan to restore national tourism
(Phnom Penh): Closing Ceremony of the Tourism Review Meeting, Review of the Plan for the Rehabilitation and Promotion of Cambodia's Tourism Sector in and After the Kovid-19 Crisis, Phase 1 (2020-2021) and the First Semester of 2022 The second phase of tourism (second half of 2022-2023) was presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the morning of July 14, 2022 at Sokha Residence Hotel, Phnom Penh.
In his remarks, Minister of Tourism Thong Khon said that the meeting was jointly committed to increase cooperation in the responsible implementation of policies, strategic plans and priority measures of the Royal Government to promote The recovery of Cambodia's tourism sector, in which the meeting decided to put out:
First. Committed to continuing to promote domestic tourism to new destinations across the country by offering attractive tour packages.
Second. Continue to promote the development of tourism products and services for the domestic and international tourism markets in the major tourism poles, focusing on innovation, diversity, quality, price, safety and good hospitality.
Third. Continue to promote investment in better support infrastructure and support activities to strengthen and expand the attractiveness and make Cambodia's tourism destinations more vibrant.
Fourth. Continue to promote air, water and land connectivity, as well as open more international gates to attract international tourists.
Fifth. Continue to participate in the implementation of minimum standard operating procedures (SOP) along the new normal path to ensure safety and provide reliable services to national and international tourists, in addition to continuing to promote the implementation of 3 Do 3 protection, we will monitor and promote Vaccination also encourages workers in the tourism industry.
Sixth. Continue to support various campaigns, such as the competition movement, clean city, clean resort, good service and good hospitality, clean tourist village, clean public toilet, campaign without plastic bags at major tourist sites and the standard of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Award for green business in tourism. Hosting the 2023 SEA Games-ASEAN Para Games.
7th. Continue to promote the use of digital technology in the tourism industry to strengthen management efficiency, expand the scope of promotion and increase the productivity of service delivery and design technology ecosystems for the development of smart tourism in key tourist destinations.
8th. Continuing training programs and capacity building for civil servants, employees and entrepreneurs in the tourism sector to strengthen existing skills and train new skills.
10th. Continue to monitor and learn about the latest developments and trends in the tourism market.
