BEIJING: China will step up policy support for a weakening economy, a central bank official said on Wednesday. According to Reuters.
Zou Lan, head of the Monetary Policy Department of the People's Bank of China, said the central bank would maintain sufficient cash flow and urge financial institutions to reduce financing costs for companies.
"In the second half of this year, economic operations continue to face uncertainty and instability," he said. "We must work to maintain economic stability and pay attention to changes in inflation."
Analysts surveyed by Reuters estimated that China's economic growth is likely to slow to 1 percent in the second quarter from 4.8 percent in January. March suggests that policymakers may need to do more to boost growth.
The central bank has been working with local authorities to maintain financial stability and monitor liquidity risk after detecting problems at several banks in Henan province, said Sun Tianqi, head of the Bureau of Financial Stability of the People's Bank of China.
The IMF also cut its GDP growth forecast for 2023 to 1 percent from 1.7 percent on June 24, when it met with US officials for its annual assessment. On US economic policy.
The latest report, released Friday, was revised to reflect lower US first-quarter GDP volatility and weaker consumer spending data in May.
But the fund has continued to highlight the challenge of high inflation and the US Federal Reserve raising interest rates to control inflation.
The rise in inflation "poses systemic risks for both the United States and the global economy," the IMF executive said in a statement. According to Reuters.
Kampong Speu residents rush to pay taxes on right-hand drive and left-hand drive vehicles after the General Department of Customs and the Governor of Cambodia issued a notice to pay taxes
(Kampong Speu): In 2-3 days until July 14, 2022, many people rushed to bring cars to pay taxes with high awareness in accordance with the notification on permission. Paying taxes and duties on duty-free vehicles already exists in the remaining countries in accordance with the words and high decisions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
In fact, Kampong Speu Provincial Customs Branch also advertised to business owners, machinery, construction sites, pits, garages, car repairs, etc. To come and pay taxes as well. It has been observed that customs officials are busy preparing tax returns and inspecting all types of vehicles that have come to pay taxes to the state in recent days.
Please be reminded that after Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia also informed the existing tax-free car owners in the remaining countries to fulfill their tax and duty obligations. Countries know the following:
* First: Owners of right-hand drive vehicles who have already paid taxes and duties but have not yet changed their steering wheel can come and get a vehicle tax receipt with the option to change or not to change the steering wheel to register the license plate.
* Second: Owners of right-hand drive tax-free remaining (not yet tax and tax have to pay taxes and duties or apply for registration as a tax-free right-hand drive existing in the country to pay taxes and duties later No need to adjust the steering wheel at the nearest Customs and Excise on the following dates:
The application for registration of existing tax-free right-hand drive vehicles in the country will start from now until July 31, 2022. After this period, the vehicle that fails to register will be considered as a non-existent vehicle in the country (newly smuggled in) and a subject of crackdown and confiscation in accordance with the provisions in force, taxes and duties will be valid for 90 years. Days from now until October 08, 2022.
* Third: Owners of left-hand drive vehicles without existing taxes in the country can also come to pay taxes and duties from now until October 08, 2022 without penalty.
