He added that the prosecution has made criminal charges and concluded that the court should enforce the law, and in carrying out its duties, prosecutors have the right to mobilize public forces directly to assist and monitor and supervise the judicial police.
Investigative Jurisdiction and Trial Jurisdiction: The Investigative Jurisdiction has the duty to investigate both charges and dismissals in court proceedings. The investigating judge may issue an order appointing an investigator instead. When executing an order ordering an investigation on behalf of a judicial police officer, it shall be under the authority of the investigating judge. The trial phase is the stage carried out by the trial judge to convict the perpetrators.
