(Phnom Penh): Four Cambodian celebrities will debate in a roundtable discussion on "ASEAN between China and the US in a new context" organized by the Royal Academy of Cambodia on the morning of July 14, 2022 tomorrow.
Speakers of this forum are: Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Dr. Meas Ny, Social Development Analyst and Monitor, Mr. Puy Kea, Cambodian Journalist Under the coordination of Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
"Currently, the world situation is changing rapidly, complicated, unpredictable and dangerous," Dr. Kin Phea told Fresh News. "The world has entered an era of new political geography, which is in a difficult transition towards a polar system where new / old actors are competing for roles in world and regional affairs."
The panelist stated that Southeast Asia is one of the fastest growing and most dynamic regions in the world. But concerns are growing over the ongoing geopolitical rivalry between the United States and China. ASEAN has become the center of this fierce competition.
In addition, Dr. Kin Phea said that in the face of growing influence and power struggles between China and the United States, Cambodia has often been accused of being at the center of the Cold War between the two powers. .
The President of the Institute of International Relations emphasized that in this regard, in order to keep up with the development of the global and regional political situation and to keep pace with the great powers, we have organized this roundtable discussion. The Cambodian people, especially our youth, should not be illiterate in the geography, politics and strategy of the superpowers, and our country should not die with just one superpower.
Dr. said that all of us Cambodians must be vigilant not to dance in the wrong rhythm, jump in the wrong cells along the chords of the great power. Our country has been a victim and has suffered countless tragedies due to the ideological race of the great powers and because of the wrong dances, the wrong jumps of politicians in the past. We should not trample on history anymore.
He stressed that looking at US foreign policy shows the contradiction between Washington's actions and words, adding that the presence of US troops in countries in the region, including Iraq, Afghanistan and Syria, is wrong. The law will cause a lot of losses to their people.
