(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, July 14, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the Tourism Summit organized by the Ministry of Tourism and Tourism Operators. The ceremony took place at Sokha Hotel.
On this occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen delivered a speech for more than 30 minutes, the following is the full text:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised and appreciated the achievements made by the leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Tourism, as well as the working group of the Royal Government and the private sector in the restoration and promotion of tourism in Cambodia during and after the Kovid Crisis. -19.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the last decade, Cambodia's tourism sector has grown proudly. Unfortunately, the growth of this sector has been almost completely disrupted during the last two years by the Kovid-19 crisis, which has had a negative impact and severely affected global development.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the tourism sector was the worst affected by Kovid-19 disease, which suspended travel both inside and outside the country, forcing the tourism business and related businesses to close down and losing tens of thousands of jobs. .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has introduced 10 rounds of intervention measures, including measures in 2022 to reduce the negative impact of the Kovid-19 crisis on socio-economic development to ensure a stable daily life. Of people and the balance of economic activity, business and investment.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has also decided to implement the "Strategies for Living in a New Ordinary Path in the Environment of Kovid-19" and the "Strategic Framework and Programs and Programs for the Rehabilitation and Promotion of Cambodia's Economic Growth in Living with Kovid-19 follows the new normal trajectory for 2021-2023 "to ensure the effectiveness of the country's reopening.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Russia-Ukraine war and sanctions made the world economy uncertain.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if fuel prices remain high, the global economic crisis will occur and will also affect tourism.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that raising the price of electricity will affect all hotels in the context of the Kovid 19 crisis.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the promotion of domestic tourism is a major contribution to the tourism sector in the Kovid 19 crisis.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the internal tourism movement will provide opportunities for people to get to know the country and participate in the conservation of natural resources.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the information technology system in Cambodia has contributed to solving the Kovid 19 crisis.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed mobile phone companies and internet service providers to strengthen internet services.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the recovery of international tourism depends on many factors. But internal tourism also depends on the status of Kovid 19.
* In order to further strengthen the development of tourism, especially to revitalize the sector, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has issued the following seven recommendations:
First. To ensure sustainable development, resilience and environment, in which the Royal Government and the private sector, the Ministry of Tourism and relevant ministries and institutions must continue to promote the implementation of tourism development frameworks and strategies and strategies set out in Boost the momentum of tourism. The Ministry of Tourism must continue to monitor and analyze the situation of tourism in Cambodia, the region and the world on a regular basis.
Fifth. Continue to promote the internal tourism movement throughout the country in the spirit of the campaign "Visit our country: tourism, connect the land or patriotism, know the land" and cooperation to promote the implementation of the policy measures to promote the internal tourism movement in 2021 -2023 ”to be highly effective.
Sixth. Strengthen and increase access to Cambodia by air, land and sea to promote the connection of major tourism market sources to Cambodia. The Ministry of Tourism and relevant ministries and institutions must continue to cooperate well in a proactive and interactive spirit and adhere to the "one-player system" approach to facilitate access to Cambodia from market sources. Major regional and global tourism.
