This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Closes a Meeting to Summarize Tourism
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, July 14, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the closing ceremony of the Tourism Summit organized by the Ministry of Tourism and Tourism Operators. The ceremony took place at Sokha Hotel.
Tourism in Cambodia, as well as around the world, has been hit hard over the past two years by the crisis caused by the Kovid 19 outbreak. After the Royal Government of Cambodia overcame the epidemic in late 2022, the Ministry of Tourism, the Royal Government's staff and operators in the tourism sector, have made great efforts to revitalize the sector that Cambodia considers green gold.
The Ministry of Tourism and Tourism Operators in Cambodia held a joint meeting to review tourism activities, plan to rehabilitate and promote Cambodia's tourism sector in and after the Kovid 19 crisis, the first phase (2020-2021) and the first half of 2022 and The direction of the plan to rehabilitate the tourism sector in the second phase (second half of 2022-2023).
The conference, held on July 12 and 13, 2022, officials and experts in the field of tourism discussed and discussed many topics related to tourism. In particular, the crisis and problems that have occurred to the tourism sector that occurred in the Kovid crisis 19. The conference also discussed the introduction of various mechanisms as opportunities for tourism in the face of the uncertainty of Kovid 19.
According to the report presented at the conference, in the first six months of 2022, Cambodia received more than 500,000 international tourists, an increase of 394% compared to the same period in 2021. However, it decreased by -84.8% compared to the same period in 2019 (before the crisis), mainly from Vietnam, Thailand, China, USA, Indonesia, France, Korea, Malaysia, UK, Australia, Singapore and India.
During the same period, Cambodia received more than 7 million domestic tourists, including 6.33 million domestic tourists, an increase of 219% and 680,000 domestic foreign tourists, an increase of 380% over the same period. Together in 2021.
Cambodia is expected to receive around 1 million international tourists in 2022 and about 2 million in 2023, the year that Cambodia will host the 32nd SEA Games-ASEAN Para Games.
