(Kampong Thom): "Training on Guidelines on Standard Procedures and Procedures for Investigating and Preparing Criminal Cases and Money Laundering Offenses from Natural Resources Offenses to Parks Officers as Police Officers "Justice and law enforcement officials are strengthening their capacity and building permanent mechanisms and systems to combat money laundering and terrorist financing for the Ministry of Environment."
This was stated by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Permanent Deputy Chairman of the Anti-Money Laundering Task Force of the Ministry of Environment on the afternoon of July 13, 2022, on the occasion of presiding over the opening of the training course on standard operating procedures for anti-money laundering. Clearing money for judicial police officers of Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Environment.
Kampong Thom Provincial Department of Environment is the ninth province where anti-money laundering teams came to train directly after Kampong Speu, Kep, Kampot, Kratie, Stung Treng, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Preah Vihear provinces in order to strengthen the mechanism and system. Increase the capacity of law enforcement officers against crimes against natural resources and crimes related to money laundering.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment emphasized that the Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing is a valuable legal tool used to contribute to the protection and conservation of Cambodia's natural resources, forests, wildlife and biodiversity, in addition to the law. On protected areas.
The Secretary of State stressed that large-scale natural resource crimes no longer exist, and that there are still small-scale crimes that we need to continue to prevent and crack down on. The crime of domestic wildlife trafficking is a traditional crime to support daily life that professional officials continue to prevent.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that along with the strengthening of legal measures, economic measures also play an important role, and the Ministry of Environment has been putting in place various plans such as animal husbandry, family and community supply, business creation to create local economy. Reduce pressure on natural resources and increase conservation efficiency.
It should be noted that during this training, the Anti-Money Laundering Task Force of the Ministry of Environment gave a presentation on the Law on Protected Areas, the Law on Anti-Money Laundering and Terrorist Financing, and the standard operating procedures to be implemented in anti-money laundering. Money.
Mr. Pheaktra said that judicial police officers would be prosecuted for money laundering and terrorist financing if it was found that the original crimes of forestry and illegal wildlife had clues related to money laundering.
He urged judicial police and law enforcement officers to pay more attention and continue to apply the law strictly and responsibly and professionally to increase efficiency in the protection and conservation of natural resources, and especially Prevent and crack down on crimes related to money laundering and terrorist financing related to natural resource crimes.
