Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister: Good cooperation with stakeholders has become an important input in the implementation of the Sendai Framework 2015-2030
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Lam Heng Huot, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Deputy Chairman of the NEC The Secretary-General assessed that the 29th National Forum on Disaster Risk Reduction was resumed with the good cooperation of all stakeholders, gathering a large number of inputs for the mid-term assessment of the disaster. Implement the Sendai Framework 2015-2030.
Such assessment by Mr. Lam Heng Huot was made at the closing ceremony of the 29th National Disaster Risk Reduction Forum under the theme "Progress of the implementation of the Kingdom of Cambodia" on the afternoon of the 13th. This July 2022.
At the same time, Mr. Lam Heng Huot would like to highly appreciate the technical team of the NCCC. Collaborate with relevant ministries, institutions and partner organizations to organize the "29th National Disaster Risk Reduction Forum" successfully and achieve the expected results.
Mr. Lam Heng Huot stated that in accordance with the words of General Kun Kim, Senior Minister, First Deputy Chairman of the NCAC. As mentioned in the opening ceremony, as of 2015, the National Forum on Disaster Risk Reduction was held for the 28th time and was suspended due to a number of necessary factors. Under the auspices of General Kun Kim, the National Forum on Disaster Risk Reduction has resumed from 2022 onwards.
The senior official of the NCDD confirmed that the 29th National Disaster Risk Reduction Forum, which was held today, coincided with Cambodia's implementation of disaster risk reduction activities under the framework of Sendai Labor Framework 2015-2030, which is now being implemented in the middle of the term, only the NEC. Decided to determine the theme "Progress of the implementation of the framework by the Kingdom of Cambodia."
Throughout the day, there were various presentations, including: Presentations on the main achievements of the National Committee for Disaster Management, Presentations of the Search and Rescue Corps, Presentations of the best female representatives on disaster risk reduction. Disaster, a presentation by a representative of a partner organization, which is to share and update the results of our work.
At the same time, Mr. Lam Heng Huot also supported the summary report of the discussion on 5 topics, which found that in the last 5 years, the National Committee for Disaster Management, Ministries, Government Institutions, Sub-National Government, Cambodian Red Cross All partner organizations and the private sector have implemented and achieved many achievements in the field of disaster risk reduction in response to the Sendai Framework on Disaster Risk Reduction 2015-2030.
Mr. Lam Heng Huot emphasized that the National Committee for Disaster Management still has a lot of work to do after receiving these inputs, and we must continue to work with stakeholders to verify and prepare these inputs in accordance with the guidelines. UN agency in charge of disaster risk reduction President Xi Jinping wishes Chinese people "a lot of fish collection every year"
Taliban to allow Afghan girls to return to high school from Thursday
Kabul: A senior Taliban government official has confirmed that all girls across Afghanistan will be allowed to return to high school from Thursday this week. This is according to a quote from Sky News on Wednesday, July 13, 2022.
According to Sky News, the report was confirmed by senior Taliban officials to the media, with an official announcement by the Taliban Ministry of Education on Thursday.
In mid-September 2021, the Taliban banned girls from attending high schools by ordering the reopening of schools for boys after they came to power in the country. Afghanistan in mid-August the same year.
