Japanese express their admiration and gratitude for the great generosity of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia to Abe (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Japanese express their admiration for the deep respect of The Royal Government and the people of Cambodia to Mr. Abe Shinzo, the former Prime Minister of Japan, who died in a shooting on July 8, 2022.
Abe's death has caused the King, the leaders of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia to express their heartfelt condolences and heartfelt condolences. Condolences of condolences have fallen repeatedly, especially the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has decided to hold a day of mourning on July 10.
At the Japanese Embassy in Phnom Penh and the Japanese Consulate in Siem Reap, the leaders of the Senate, the National Assembly and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, as well as leaders from various ministries and institutions, paid their respects and expressed their condolences. Next.
These gestures are an expression of the deepest respect and love of the Cambodian leadership and people for Abe.
Mr. Thai Susumu, a Japanese man who is the Honorary Consul of Cambodia in Sendai, Japan, expressed his surprise and admiration for the enthusiasm of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia who have expressed their deep respect.
Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra has said that Abe, during his tenure as prime minister, has taken great care to boost relations with Cambodia.
Mr. Thai Susumu reminded that in 2018, when he was appointed by the Royal Government as the Honorary Consul of Cambodia, he had the opportunity to pay a courtesy call on Mr. Abe and Mr. Kono, former Japanese Foreign Minister. During the meeting, in addition to congratulating Abe, he urged him to work hard to improve Cambodian-Japanese relations, especially to promote trade and investment between the two countries.
"Prime Minister Abe has instructed me to work hard for better relations between Cambodia and Japan, especially in the areas of investment, trade, industry, etc., so that the two countries can be linked through my consulate. "I will never forget the warm palms of Abe, who took me by the hand and rebuked me." This is a reminder of Thai Susumu Abe's words when he was the Prime Minister of Japan.
Thai Satsumu has expressed his determination that despite Abe's death, he will continue his mission as instructed by Abe. "I will always remember his words and I will continue this mission until I succeed in achieving your goal," he said.
Former Japanese Prime Minister Abe has died in hospital after being shot during a senate election campaign in western Nara, Japan, on Friday morning.
Despite his resignation, Abe continued to exert a strong influence on Japanese politics due to the success of his "Abenomics" economic policies. He was one of the leaders in the campaign to amend Japan's pacifist constitution, which allowed Japan to conduct military action to help the Allies as part of strengthening Japan's defense.
In terms of relations with Cambodia, Abe went beyond country-to-country relations, reaching out to his individual relationship with Cambodian leader Samdech Techo Hun Sen. It is remembered that in August 2017, during his visit to Japan, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was surprised by a birthday cake prepared by Mr. Abe. That gesture shows a deep and close relationship between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Abe.
Through his personal emotional connection, Abe became one of Japan's leaders who set out a number of diplomatic policies to boost relations with Cambodia, contributing to the building and development of a better Cambodian economy. The legacy of the two countries' relationship from the past.
As Prime Minister of Japan, Abe paid an official visit to Cambodia in November 2013. Through his visit at the time, he decided to provide assistance to help reform the electoral system in Cambodia and some other development assistance.
During his tenure as Prime Minister of Japan, especially from 2012 to 2020, Abe made significant contributions to the development of Cambodia-Japan relations. In that, he made the Cambodian relationship from a normal relationship to a strategic partnership in 2013. In addition, economic and trade relations between Cambodia and Japan have been growing steadily.
