Ministry of Economy Organizes Information Technology Awareness Program for Public Financial Management (FMIS)
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance on July 13, 2022 organized the program "Mainstreaming Awareness on Information Technology for Public Financial Management (FMIS)" to the new entity budget entity. 10 of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Interior.
The program was conducted under the leadership of Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State and Chairman of the FMIS Project Management Team, with the participation of leaders and officials of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Ministry of Interior, who are the key players in using the system. Upcoming FMIS.
The Secretary of State stressed the importance of devolving as much of the budget authority to the budget entities as possible, in line with the Royal Government's reform goals of decentralization. Ability and full ownership to manage and implement the budget on their own.
The Secretary of State added that in 2022, information extracted from FMIS will be recognized as the only official source for budgeting and financial operations, and that FMIS will be the source of budget and financial information. Can be downloaded for review and analysis as needed.
Recently, the working group has officially launched the first generation digital file system (FMIS Portal) for 75 district administrations and 185 commune administrations as a pilot in order to facilitate the implementation of district budget officers and Commune to request payment or payment by scanning the application documents attached to the system sent to the provincial treasury without having to travel directly.
