Please be informed that the initiative to ban cooperation with the tobacco industry of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports is a contribution to the implementation of the Convention on Tobacco Control, of which Cambodia is also a State Party. It should be noted that 15,000 Cambodians die every year from tobacco use, and Cambodia loses about 649 million US dollars (according to a United Nations report).
Students and youth alike claim that tobacco companies intend to attract tobacco use through tobacco advertising, the creation of new generation products that appeal to young people, and sponsorship activities, including the establishment of public relations in the United States. Educational institutions and other institutions to cover up the harmful effects of tobacco use as well.
