(Phnom Penh): General Kun Kim, Senior Minister in Charge of the First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, outlined and updated the progress of its disaster risk reduction activities in line with the 2015-2030 work framework. Focusing on five points.
Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized that disaster risk reduction has the benefit of preventing future losses, so the effectiveness of disaster risk management has contributed significantly to sustainable development. With the efforts of ministries, institutions, government, development partners, national and international organizations and the private sector in the past on disaster risk management.
In the opening ceremony of the 29th National Forum for Disaster Risk Reduction under the theme "Progress of the implementation of the Kingdom of Cambodia's Sendai Framework" on July 13, 2022, Senior Minister Kun Kim said:
First, comprehensive understanding of disaster risk for disaster preparedness and mitigation, development and implementation of appropriate disaster response preparedness.
Second, strengthening disaster risk governance to effectively manage disaster risk and coordinate in the field of cellular communication with disaster risk management on disaster preparedness, mitigation, and response response. And reconstruction.
Third, investment in disaster risk reduction, both public and private, in disaster preparedness and mitigation through structural and non-structural measures that are beneficial and life-saving tools, prevention and Reduce losses.
Fourth: Disaster preparedness, reconstruction and improvement by presenting lessons and experiences learned from the past and key solutions to make the nation and community more resilient.
And fifth, partnerships and partnerships that are central to supporting our efforts to increase resources and technical capacity and technology transfer to reduce disaster risk.
