Cambodia reports on recent developments and achievements in the field of human rights to the UN Forum in Geneva (Video inside) (Geneva): The UN Human Rights Council concluded its 50th session on 8 July. 2022 After organizing interactive dialogues with a total of 23 Special Rapporteurs and 8 discussion forums, and adopted a total of 23 resolutions related to specific topics and countries.
* Cambodia's "blossoming strategy" to provide free and non-discriminatory Kovid-19 vaccination, including prisoners and foreigners, has achieved a vaccination rate of more than 94% of the total population. Several rounds of social protection interventions have also been provided to disadvantaged citizens, vulnerable groups and businesses affected by the Kovid-19 outbreak. Cambodia has been preparing a draft law on social protection.
The United Nations commends Cambodia for its remarkable progress in expanding social protection coverage. Since the introduction of the "National Social Protection Policy Framework" in 2016, social assistance and the social security system have been widely expanded to ensure that not only the most vulnerable groups but also the Cambodian people are at risk. And the risk of falling into poverty is also better protected.
* Nearly 80% of the total Cambodian population are active social media users who freely express their views on public affairs. Their expressions, including those of dissent, are further echoed through the nearly 2,000 traditional and digital media outlets operating without prior inspection and without restriction, and are also guaranteed by Another law on the press.
On the occasion of attending the Universal Periodic Review (UPR), Cambodia accepted a number of recommendations regarding LGBTI rights. To eradicate bullying and discrimination in society and in the workplace, sex education, including gender equality and homosexuality, has been incorporated into school curricula and public awareness campaigns. Through the media as well as through education, both inside and outside the system.
* Cambodia is committed to integrating mental health services into different levels of care across the health system, with a focus on strengthening primary health care in line with WHO recommendations and the Global Action Plan for Mental Health.
* Cambodia is one of the prominent states that has ratified the International Labor Organization's basic conventions, including the Convention on the Minimum Age and the Convention on the Prohibition of the Worst Forms of Child Labor. By 2021, a total of more than 100 campaigns on child labor will be conducted in different types of workplaces, with the participation of nearly 3,000 employees, employers and parents.
* The exercise of freedom of expression, association and peaceful assembly shall adhere to the duties, responsibilities and special restrictions set by law as stated in Article 19 (3), Article 21 and Article 22 (2). ) Of the International Covenant on Civil and Political Rights. Everyone, including those who claim to be human rights defenders, has the obligation to exercise their rights responsibly within the bounds of the law.
* Cambodia, along with many other delegations, reiterates its call for the Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights to be fair and non-politicized, based on the principles of universalism, impartiality, fairness and non-partisanship. In a constructive dialogue based on authentic sources of information and real cooperation.
