Speaking to Fresh News on July 12, Mr. Kim Huot, Director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Commerce, said that the red corn trade in Battambang is still normal, with about 2,500 tons exported per day. 3,000 tons, while the Thai side began to transport the weight of the stock according to the standards set by the Ministry of Public Works after strict legal measures.
He said that before the mobile scales came down to grab the overweight truck, the red corn cost 6.3 baht or more than 700 riel, after a surprise caused Thai traders to temporarily suspend orders, the price of corn dropped to 5. 3 baht or about 600 riel per kilogram, but now the price of corn starts to increase slightly to 5.5 baht to 5.6 baht or 660 to 670 riel.
He said the drop was due to Thai traders taking the opportunity to lower prices, which would hurt farmers due to higher prices of fertilizers, pesticides and oil.
He expects that after CP collects corn from farmers for animal feed production, the price of corn will be even better, as CP generally buys at a better price than selling it to traders to export to Thailand. Typically, CP, based in Pailin province, collects about 120,000 tons of corn per year, which contributes 15%.
Recently, the mobile weighing team of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport conducted an operation to catch overweight trucks on the national road in Phnom Proek district, Battambang province, which was overweight to 80 tons.
Chhim Vachira, director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Agriculture, said that despite cases of overweight trucks being seized, traders continued to buy corn for export to Thailand as usual.
Mr. Tim Lang, a farmer who grows corn on an area of 10 hectares in Sampov Loun district, Battambang province, said that for his plantation, he has already harvested, selling at 6.15 baht per kilogram, which may have some profit. Despite the rise in fertilizer prices.
According to the director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Agriculture, Mr. Chhim Vachira, the current harvest of red corn in Battambang province is about 30% of the more than 53,000 hectares.
3.2 million tons of cassava products exported include:
Mr. Chhim Vachira, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Battambang Province, said, "As for the cassava harvest in the middle of this year, a lot has already been harvested. Other provinces. The price this year is better than previous years, with prices up to 30-50 riel, both dried potatoes and fresh potatoes.
He said that previously, 100,000 hectares of cassava had been planted, but now the planting has increased to 12-130,000 hectares, while the cassava harvest season runs from December to March every year, and in Battambang this year, the production is about More than 3.2 million tons, of which 65% to 70% were exported to Thailand.
