In its letter, the Ministry of Mines stated, "After inspecting the location of Ms. Ros Ratha's station, the Ministry of Mines and Energy has found that this station is under construction in accordance with the technical safety plan of the station. Circular of the Ministry of Mines and Energy.
At the same time, the Ministry of Mines and Energy also issued a letter instructing the station owners to construct the station in accordance with the station safety technical plan approved by the Ministry and to correct the technical specifications of the completed construction as follows:
* First, the location of the fuel storage bag must be at a minimum distance of 6 meters from the house * Second: Build a fence, a wall made of non-combustible material and a minimum height of 3 meters at the border fence of the station adjacent to the carpet Residential land (south).
In case the station owner makes technical adjustments as mentioned above, the preparation of technical safety features of this station will be in accordance with the circular of the Ministry of Mines and Energy.
