(Phnom Penh): On July 9, 2022, the Press and Quick Reaction Unit of the Office of the Council of Ministers released a new video lasting more than 13 minutes under the title "People and the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen" Let's face the global crisis.
This video highlights the recovery of the Kovid-19 epidemic in Cambodia, and in particular the "Challenges of the Fuel Crisis" as the world is now going through a dangerous hurricane that has created a huge global crisis without any country. One can not escape. Big countries, small countries, poor countries or rich countries are all affected to varying degrees and magnitude from the global crisis.
The first problem is Kovid-19, which so far the world has not been able to overcome. This deadly epidemic has left the global economy in a state of shock.
The successful experience of combating Kovid-19 clearly shows that there are two key factors combined to achieve such a good result: the first is the Royal Government making the right political decision and the second is the belief. Trust and support from the people.
Due to good resistance to Kovid-19, the Cambodian economy began to gradually recover. But at the same time, Cambodia is facing an oil crisis as a result of the protracted war in Ukraine. The crisis is also affecting the whole world, making it very difficult for countries as oil and gas prices, which are the basic needs of humanity in the world, continue to rise.
Therefore, to solve the fuel crisis in this situation, the participation of people from all walks of life is necessary and indispensable. The Royal Government is now exploring all means to resolve the fuel crisis by increasing oil stocks and ensuring sufficient oil to supply the market, as well as maintaining economic stability and people's livelihoods.
The Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen is confident and optimistic that with the strong support and active participation of people from all walks of life, we will be able to successfully resist and overcome this global crisis. Certainly, to continue the process of building and developing the motherland of Cambodia and our family in the shadow of peace.
