Thai Ministry of Finance optimistic that the baht will appreciate this year
BANGKOK: The Thai Ministry of Finance, which asked not to be named, told the Bangkok Post that the ministry expects the baht to appreciate in the second half of this year, in line with the expected decline. Current accountability.
The Bank of Thailand said last weekend that it would allow the baht to fluctuate in line with market prices, but would control the value of the currency if it fluctuated too much.
The current account deficit is expected to widen in the third and fourth quarters as more foreign tourists return to Thailand, a ministry source said.
The number of foreign tourist arrivals in the first six months of this year was 1.98 million, while the Thai Ministry of Tourism and Sports estimates 9 million this year. A strong export-backed economic recovery should also support the baht. In addition, according to some analysts, the Bank of Thailand is likely to raise policy rates in August.
The same source said that all these factors show that the average value of the baht throughout the year will not fall sharply.
As of May, Thailand had a current account deficit of $ 3.71 billion, up from $ 3.05 billion in April, as the two-month period was dominated by foreign-based companies. Thailand sends profits and dividends back to their country.
According to the Bangkok Post, the average baht this year is 33.1 baht to the dollar, which is between 32.1 and 34.1 baht. On Thursday last week, the baht fell to 36.35 baht per dollar, the lowest level in nearly seven years.
