The World Bank Representative highlighted that the second phase of the Health Quality Improvement and Equity Project is five years old and will be valid from July 7, 2022. Non-communicable disease screening and treatment services will be expanded nationwide, and cervical cancer screening and treatment services will be expanded to 500 health centers and 60 referral hospitals.
