Customs has set July 31 for duty-free right-hand drive car owners to apply for registration as existing vehicles in the country, while tax entry is valid until October 8, 2022.
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia on July 11, 2022 issued a follow-up notification on the permission to pay taxes and duties on existing duty-free vehicles in the remaining countries.
According to the statement and the high decision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the concession to the owners of existing duty-free right-hand drive vehicles in the remaining countries to fulfill their tax and duty obligations, the General Department of Customs And the Cambodian Excise of the Ministry of Economy and Finance would like to inform the existing duty-free car owners in the following countries:
1: Owners of right-hand drive vehicles who have already paid taxes and duties but have not yet changed their steering wheel can come and get a vehicle tax receipt with the option to change or not to change the steering wheel to register the license plate.
2. The owner of the remaining duty-free right-hand drive vehicle (not yet taxed and taxed) must come to pay taxes and duties or apply for registration as a tax-free right-hand drive vehicle existing in the country to pay taxes and duties. Steering is not required at the nearest customs and excise office on the following dates:
Application for registration of existing tax-free right-hand drive vehicles in the country will start from now until July 31, 2022. After this period, the vehicle that fails to register will be considered as a non-existent vehicle in the country (newly smuggled in) and a sign of crackdown and confiscation in accordance with the regulations in force.
3: Meanwhile, owners of left-hand drive vehicles without taxes in the country can also come to pay taxes and duties from now until October 8, 2022 without penalty.
The General Department of Customs states that the implementation of the above preferential principle does not apply to vehicles with model year from 2021 onwards, which are subject to tax payment and fines in accordance with the provisions in force.
At the same time, the General Department of Customs appealed to all tax-free car owners to register and fulfill their tax and duty obligations by the above deadlines.
According to the Director General of Customs, on July 11, 2022, the remaining owners of right-hand drive vehicles came to pay taxes without correcting the steering wheel and registered (occupying and applying for tax at a later time) a total of 52 vehicles. . Daughter of Norodom Ranariddh Appointed Vice President of FUNCINPEC
