(Kratie): The assailant used an ax to cut his sister-in-law to death and tried to swim in the river to escape being intercepted by the police immediately after the incident. This incident happened at 8:20 AM on July 11, 2022 at Koh Dambang village, Boeung Char commune, Sambo district, Kratie province.
According to the report of the Sambo District Police Inspectorate, the victim was 27-year-old Ty Srey Mao. As for the suspect, his name is Lin Nan, 34 years old. Both of them live in the same commune.
Prior to the incident, the victim was sitting and talking with his sister, Tha Linet, on a bed in the basement. Severe injuries (for no reason), then the family sent the victim to the hospital, but unfortunately when he arrived at the Sambo District Referral Hospital, the victim died.
As for the suspect, after the action, he escaped. At 10 am on the same day, the Sambo District Special Forces, in cooperation with the Boeung Char Police Force and the People's Defense Force, arrested him in the middle of the Mekong River while The man was swimming in the reserve to escape.
Through interrogation, the perpetrator confessed that as soon as he saw the victim, he was angry and hated, so he used an ax. Currently, the suspects are being interrogated at the Sambo District Police Inspectorate to build a case to be sent to the provincial specialized office to proceed with the procedure.
Authorities call on people to travel up and down the An Se border checkpoint, beware of natural disasters, rocks falling from the top of the mountain
(Preah Vihear): The authority of Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, on July 11, 2022, issued a notice to the people who wish to travel to An Se, Thai border, please be very careful. A natural disaster occurred on a stretch of road at the foot of a mountain with rocks falling from the top of the mountain.
According to Colonel Say Det, Police Inspector of Choam Ksan District, on the afternoon of July 11, 2022, the case of a stone falling from a mountain across the road to An Ses Pass did not cause any danger to the villagers. No, this case is suspected to be caused by a natural disaster, heavy rain caused the rain to erode the soil on the top of the mountain, causing the rocks to fall like this.
The district inspector said that as of this afternoon, the road up to An Se, near the Thai border, could be used normally due to the fact that from the place where the stone fell to the sidewalk on the right side, there was still 5 meters left. It fell 1.60 meters by 2.00 meters and was 1.20 meters high, and the team planned to use machinery to push the stone off the road.
Please note that An Ses border checkpoint in Kampong village, An Ses village, Choam Ksan commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province is scheduled to officially open on July 21, 2022, after being temporarily closed for more than 2 years due to the disease crisis. Kovid 19.
