Sports have the same standards in every country, while politics and democracy in the world do not have the same standards. This is an important statement that Samdech always mentioned when meeting with the Cambodian team.
Samdech considered that this point makes us respect the role of sports is the international standard in this field. But standards on politics, governance, democracy and human rights are not international.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has repeatedly stated in the United States that only 40 percent or less than 40 percent of the population can run for president because only 60 percent or 70 percent of voters go to the polls. In France, no more than 50 percent of the vote is possible.
He added that democracy works differently from country to country, but is called the same type of democracy. Some countries have a presidential system, some countries have a parliamentary system, and even the presidential or parliamentary system is called democracy, but the standards are not the same.
