Ministry of Tourism announces the termination of the requirements for tourists who have not been vaccinated or the local dose has not been completed.
(Phnom Penh): Following the decision of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Ministry of Tourism has issued a notification to the Association of Private Sector Tourism, relevant institutions, national and international tourism journalists and the public on the adjustment of the requirements for national and international tourists who have not been vaccinated.
The amendment of this condition shall be implemented from July 11, 2022 onwards by following the following procedures:
1. Required a quick test for Kovid 19 antigen by health officials at international ports, waterways, land and airways When international tourists arrive in Cambodia, a test fee of US $ 5 per person is required.
* In case of negative negative test results: National and international tourists can travel to tourist destinations throughout Cambodia without being required to do so.
* In case of a positive test result, it is a serious illness: National and international tourists must be treated at the Kovid-19 treatment unit in a hospital that is integrated into the same health system, and have to pay for medical treatment and accommodation for international tourists. .
Second, national and international tourists who failed to be vaccinated due to various factors, please hurry to get vaccinated at the vaccination sites in the capital-province throughout Cambodia, free of charge.
