Cambodian-Chinese Students Association Visits Keo Phos Development Zone, Preah Sihanouk Province
(Preah Sihanouk): Leaders of 500 members and members of the Cambodian Students Association in the People's Republic of China visited the Keo Phos Development Zone in Preah Sihanouk Province with the support of Dr. Mong Reththy, Chairman of the Third Committee of the Senate and Chairman of the Cambodia-China Senate Friendship Group on July 10, 2022.
The above members and members of the Association of Cambodian Students are led by Mr. Ou Vuthy, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Association, Ms. Hor Raksmey, President of the Association of the 5th Mandate, Mr. Nhel Soviet, Vice Chairman of the Board of Directors, Mr. Hong Heng Try, Vice Chairman of the Board of the Association.
Ms. Hor Reaksmey said that this study tour to Keo Phos Development Zone is the first study visit for students studying in China.
She continued that the study visit to Keo Phos Development Zone encourages all students to study and learn more about the development of agriculture and industry in Cambodia, and also a rare opportunity for our students to meet and study. New knowledge together. On the other hand, this study tour shows the friendship and solidarity between the students.
Mr. Nhel Soviet said that after Cambodian students studying in China visited all development areas in Sihanoukville by Dr. Mong Reththy, all our students gained a lot of knowledge related. And developments in the agro-industrial sector in Cambodia, such as:
Mr. Ou Vuthy said that the visit reflected Dr. Mong Reththy's concern for the younger generation. In particular, encouraging students to study agriculture to contribute to the development of the agricultural sector in Cambodia to be more modern and prosperous, because our economy depends on agriculture as the core.
He said that this is also an encouragement to Cambodian students who are studying online from Cambodia, waiting for the opportunity to return to study in China in the near future.
Dr. Mong Reththy expressed his appreciation to the Cambodian students studying in China who have always maintained the unity and solidarity in the past leadership of the student association, especially the gathering of students to visit this study, which provided wisdom. Agro-industry to students who are the successors of bamboo for the next shift.
Dr. welcomes students who have graduated from China in all fields, especially in agriculture, who wish to work or intern at the Mong Reththy Group.
He also encouraged students to study hard, even if they are studying online, and wished them to return to China to study directly in the near future.
Minister of Labor: The Implementation of the Social Security Pension System as a Development of a Complete Social Security System in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The implementation of the social security system for pensions for individuals under the provisions of the Labor Law is another step towards the development of a complete social security system in Cambodia. This is according to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training and Chairman of the Board of the National Social Security Fund.
He said that this law defines the management of the social security system of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which includes occupational risk, health care, pension and unemployment. So far, Cambodia has implemented three social security regimes, including: 1. Occupational risk, implemented in 2008, 2. Health care, implemented in 2016, and 3. Pension, implemented from the first day. This July 2022.
(Battambang): Mobile scales officials and the deputy governor of Battambang province also said that the group of traders collecting corn and other agricultural products along the corrupt border is behind and encouraging Thai traders to come and transport. Overweight in Cambodia.
Seeing the risk of road damage due to overweight transportation, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, made every effort to comply with the law to prevent overweight transportation. On national roads, all scales are placed, and mobile scales operate on roads that do not have static scales.
The operation to prevent overweight shipments has upset transport operators. They give similar reasons that will make them unprofitable from shipping. Officials' operations often erupt into conflicts between officials and traders.
In fact, the operation of the mobile scales of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport on the border in Phnom Proek and Sampov Loun districts of Battambang province on July 9 has caused some protests from the group of traders to buy corn. The reaction of Cambodian traders to buy corn to prevent overweight, they argued that not to overweight Thai cars will not come to buy corn from Cambodia.
The traders even told the corn growers that not allowing Thai traders to be overweight would hamper the corn harvest. The words of the traders made some farmers and some workers organized by the traders to protest against the implementation of the law by the officials. Blocking law enforcement officers is against the law and is punishable under the Cambodian Penal Code.
Meanwhile, farmers in Phnom Proek and Sampov Loun are starting to harvest corn. Cambodian and Thai traders are also busy with their business. O'Rumduol, located in Phnom Proek district, is a regional port between Cambodia and Thailand, has become the largest transit point for agricultural products from Cambodia to Thailand during this harvest season. There are hundreds of cars coming and going every day.
The fact that trucks transporting agricultural products between Cambodia and Thailand in and out of O'Rumduol is more complicated due to the lack of formalities, which leads to more complications and can carry more weight at will. The traders claim that they pay only 13,000 baht for a car, or about $ 400, to the border officials between the two countries.
