(Phnom Penh): The Council of the ASEAN Para Games Federation and the Council of the Southeast Asian Games Federation on Monday morning, July 11, 2022, held a meeting to discuss preparations for the Paralympic Games and the SEA Games, which Cambodia is hosting. House in 2023.
The opening ceremony was held at the Sokha Hotel under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. According to the report, the two federal meetings will be held for three days from July 11 to 13.
Please note that Cambodia will host the first Southeast Asian Games or the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games on May 5, 2023. Cambodia has started a 300-day countdown to the SEA Games on July 8, 2022.
The 11-nation Southeast Asian Games is held every two years. So far, the event of the Southeast Asian Games, or SEA Games, has been going on for 64 years. Due to the political crisis and war as well as the limited economic situation, Cambodia has never hosted this tournament.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has said that he has asked not to host the tournament many times when it is Cambodia's turn to host. Samdech Techo stated that the request not to host is because Cambodia needs funds to develop other areas necessary to promote the growth of the national economy.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia will spend about $ 30 million to host the ASEAN Para Games and the Southeast Asian Games. In that, Cambodia has saved about 40 billion riels or 10 million US dollars to spend on this competition per year.
To move forward with organizing this historic event, Cambodia has paid close attention to a lot of work. Samdech Techo Hun Sen made five recommendations to launch a national campaign to promote the 32nd SEA Games and the 12th ASEAN Para Games 2023. The five recommendations include:
First, ministries, institutions, capitals, provinces, departments, units, and competent forces must effectively participate in the 2023 SEA Games-ASEAN Para Games in all its forms and through its various media outlets.
Second, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, embassies, diplomatic missions abroad and other ministries and institutions must participate in the campaign of diplomacy and foreign affairs, sports, with the agenda of the promotion "The Kingdom of Cambodia to host the SEA Games - ASEAN. Para Games 2023 for the first time ”using all the forums, hearings, bilateral meetings, multilateral meetings as an opportunity to broadcast live to seek international support.
Third, to jointly promote the honor and image of Cambodia through the influence of the 2023 SEA Games-ASEAN Para Games. In the campaign to educate society and promote sports, live in peace, one person plays one sport, Cambodia is clean, Cambodia reduces traffic accidents and reduces the effects of drugs.
Fourth, the National Organizing Committee of the 32nd Southeast Asian Games 2023 must be responsible for organizing the SEA Games - ASEAN Para Games 2023 in accordance with the principles of green sports and clean sports to maintain dignity in the name. Hosted the first SEA Games.
The National Sports Federation, Athletes, Athletes, Disabled Athletes, please make every effort to take the physical, mental, intellectual and spiritual training to develop professional sports and fulfill their respective missions with a high sense of responsibility to host the event Successful SEA Games-ASEAN Para Games 2023.
Fifth, I would like to ask Excellencies, Lok Chumteavs, Neak Oknha, Oknha, Ladies and Gentlemen and all private enterprises to support the 2023 Southeast Asian Games Foundation to contribute to the success of the 2023 SEA Games and ASEAN Para Games. "
