In response to the deep merits and sentiments that Abe has for the country and the people of Cambodia, in the early hours of July 9, 2022, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, decided to mourn on Sunday, July 10, all over the country. A day to mourn the people of Japan over Abe's death.
In a voice message on the morning of July 9, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted that Abe Shinzo's death was not only a tragic, tragic and tragic loss for the people of Japan, but for the people of the world. Including Cambodians.
The Prime Minister, who has the deepest feelings and closeness with Abe, stated that in his two terms as Prime Minister of Japan, Abe Shinzo has made great efforts to promote Japan-Cambodia relations to become a strategic partner. In 2013. In addition, Abe has stepped up support for development in all areas of Cambodia, including infrastructure.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded that Mr. Abe is also the Prime Minister who has promoted ASEAN-Japan relations and Mekong-Japan relations.
