Through Facebook, Mr. Hun Many described that "July 10, 2022 is an official day of mourning for the body of His Excellency Shinzo Abe, former Prime Minister of Japan, who passed away on July 8. Taking the opportunity of the opening ceremony of the seminar of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia this morning, we held a one-minute meditation to honor the soul of His Excellency, a good friend of Cambodia.
We will remember His Excellency's great contribution to strengthening bilateral relations between our two countries. May His Excellency's soul go to a place of peace, do not mourn. "
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to mourn on Sunday, July 10, 2022, for a day to mourn with the people of Japan over the death of Shinzo Abe.
Anti-government protests have been going on for months in Sri Lanka due to the worst economic crisis that has seen the island nation of 22 million people suffer from high inflation. Ability to import basic commodities such as food, fuel and medicine. July 10, National Day of Remembrance of Preah Vihear and Sambor Prei Kuk in the World Heritage List
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, in 2018, declared July 10 as the National Day of Remembrance of the inclusion of the Temple of Preah Vihear and Sambor Prei Kuk in the World Heritage List.
Despite being inscribed on the World Heritage List for many years before and after, the Temple of Preah Vihear and Sambor Prei Kuk were decided to be inscribed on the World Heritage List in July. Namely, the temple of Preah Vihear was inaugurated on July 7, 2008 and the temple of Sambor Prei Kuk was inaugurated on July 8, 2017.
Because of this, in 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to make July 10 as the National Day of Remembrance for this event full of joy and happiness of the Khmer nation. At that time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen introduced various programs to celebrate the inclusion of both temples in the World Heritage List on July 10 every year.
But for 2021, there is no big meeting program due to the problem of Kovid 19.
Until the inclusion of these two temples in the World Heritage List, the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has made efforts to prepare joint documents and other procedures in accordance with UNESCO requirements. In particular, special envoys such as Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An and Mrs. Phoeung Sakna, Minister of Culture and Fine Arts, presented and affirmed in front of the World Heritage Committee.
* History and struggle to put Preah Vihear temple on the World Heritage List
Please note that the temple of Preah Vihear is a sacred temple of Cambodia, located on Phnom Dangrek, 625 meters above sea level in Sraem commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, about 100 km north of Preah Vihear city and about 230 km northeast of Siem Reap city and about 414 km north of Phnom Penh.
The temple was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage Committee's list of World Heritage Sites on July 7, 2008 at the 32nd Meeting in Quebec City, Canada.
In the cause of upholding national cultural heritage and defending national sovereignty, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, sent a letter to UNESCO in 2001 requesting the registration of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site. The Prime Minister said that the inscription of the Temple of Preah Vihear on the World Heritage List is in line with the planned plan, which is a priority of Cambodia's foreign policy.
The decision by UNESCO to designate the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site is a great success for Cambodia under the leadership of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen in claiming ownership of the Temple of Preah Vihear after re-administration. From Thailand on June 15, 1962 under the great crusade of King Norodom Sihanouk.
Until the inclusion of the Temple of Preah Vihear in the World Heritage List, the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has made great efforts to advocate for the proposed inclusion of the Temple of Preah Vihear in the World Heritage List. Thailand has ambitions to take over the Temple of Preah Vihear, which it has ruled for many years.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo, with special envoys such as Samdech Vibol Panha Sok An, has worked hard to prepare joint documents and other procedures in accordance with UNESCO requirements.
Cambodia's success has brought a lot of pain to the Thai people. Just days after the temple was inscribed on the World Heritage List, Thailand raised troops to invade Cambodian territory in the area of the Preah Vihear temple.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government and a Khmer Rouge son who was determined to defend the nation and the territory, fought hard by all means, including the armed forces and the means of international law, to protect this valuable property of Cambodia from being lost. .
Prasat Sambo Prey Kuk Resort is located in Sambo Village, Sambo Commune, Prasat Sambo District, Kampong Thom Province, about 30 km north of Stung Sen City. The area of Sambor Prei Kuk temple is large and there are 7 villages in that area. Sambor Prei Kuk resort is divided into large areas: the former capital area on the west side and the temple area on the eastern side, separated by a stream called Kru Ke.
Despite the relocation of the capital to Angkor in the 9th century, the Sambor Prei Kuk area remained an important religious center during the Angkorian period, with additional religious structures and the restoration of existing structures for subsequent worship. The Sambor Prei Kuk temple resort has been built for many generations, highlighting many of the temples, statues, and other works of art and has become one of Cambodia's most famous historical sites today.
Currently, the Sambor Prei Kuk temple resort is open to national and international tourists and specialists to visit and study archeology, history, culture and religion.
As a result, the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site was decided by the World Heritage Committee to be included in the World Heritage List at the request of Cambodia on July 08, 2017 during the 41st Summit, which took place from 2 to 12 May. July 2017 in Krakow, Poland, which has 193 member countries and 21 permanent standing evaluation committees.
Achieving the inclusion of this ancient temple in the World Heritage List is not a simple and easy task. Under the high decision and guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts has started to prepare documents to request the designation of Sambor Prei Kuk Temple as a World Heritage Site in 2012.
Hasane International and the Muslim Development Foundation of Cambodia are committed to strengthening cooperation to contribute to the development of the Cambodian community.
