The Royal Government allows, in principle, Muslim women to wear their heads, make passports, ID cards, or take photographs for administrative documents. Muslim students can wear traditional clothing and wear a krama while studying at both public and private educational institutions. In addition, the Royal Government has included about 1,500 Khmer Muslim teachers in the framework of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and 180 contract officials.
Finally, he strongly hopes that Hasane International and the Cambodian Muslim Development Foundation will continue to strengthen ties and cooperation to further develop the Cambodian community.
