In the first six months of this year, Cambodia approved 1,984 construction projects with an investment of more than 1 billion dollars
(Phnom Penh): In the first six months of 2022, Cambodia has approved 1,984 construction projects with an investment of more than 1 billion dollars. This was confirmed by Mr. Charles Van, representative of Duke Dr. Pung Kheav Se, President of the Cambodian Builders Association.
During the 12th Meeting on Business Construction and Communication on July 8, 2022, Mr. Charles Van stated that "Looking at the construction data of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction found that in the middle of 2022 Ministry Has issued construction permits for 1,984 projects and investment capital of 1.041 million US dollars.
He also said that according to the forecast of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the construction and real estate sector will increase after the Kovid-19 crisis is alleviated in 2022. Construction will grow by 5.4%, while the real estate sector will grow by 4.1% and both sectors will continue to grow.
He thinks investment in construction and real estate will rebound and will also provide employment for tens of thousands of people. These are contributions to the Royal Government in reviving the national economy after the Kovid-19 crisis.
According to the circular on the preparation of the draft law on finance for the management of 2023 by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the construction sector is projected to continue to recover at a rate of 7.2% in 2023 due to expectations. Save the flow of foreign investment for construction for tourism and trade.
At the same time, low- and medium-cost housing construction is expected to continue to maintain good growth due to the increase in the actual demand of the people to organize families in line with the trend of increasing domestic investment.
The real estate sector, on the other hand, is projected to continue to grow at a rate of 5.2 percent in 2023 due to expectations of a recovery in high-end real estate transactions, condominiums and apartments, in line with investment and demand. Domestically, low- and medium-cost residential real estate is expected to maintain strong growth.
