TKY Farm CEO, Mr. Yi Sinath, said that TKW Farm is a large company established by Cambodian children and has been successful in investing in durian crops on more than 200 hectares in the area of O village. Po commune, Romney district, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province, with 3 varieties of durian crops, including: durian manthong, dried milk, durian oak, and durian musan king on more than 16,000 plants, and more than 4,000 durians are harvesting.
"The durian that our company is planting can be said to be the durian brand of Preah Vihear, the taste of Preah Vihear, marking our province, because we think that the history of Preah Vihear province, which is a kind of chalk, has never had a large farm," he said. "Hundreds of hectares that grow durian successfully like this."
The CEO of TK Y Farm said that for this year's output, the company got a lot of profit compared to last year is up to twice.
"The durians we are harvesting are 7 to 8 years old and the yield per tree is between 40 and 60 fruits, and the harvest per day is between 6 tons and 6 tons," he said. 10 tons. In terms of output, this year we have doubled compared to last year's output, last year we only got more than 100 tons, while this year we estimate that we will get more than 300 tons. "
At present, TKY Farm has been exporting durian meat to the Chinese market for the first time in the amount of 120 tons of durian varieties, so far the company has been supplying to partners in China already has more than 50 tons. Next year, Chinese investors will give the green light to the company to expand its export volume to another 500 tons.
