The working group of the Royal Government and the private sector met to review the work in accordance with the roadmap for the first half of 2022
(Phnom Penh): The Secretariat of the Royal Government-Private Working Group for the Restoration and Promotion of Tourism in and After the Kovid-19 Crisis On the morning of July 8, 2022, held a meeting to review the work results in accordance with the roadmap for the semester. First, 2022 at the Ministry of Tourism.
Mr. Thong Rathsak, Director General of Tourism Development and International Cooperation and Acting Director of the Secretariat of the Government-Private Working Group for the Rehabilitation and Promotion of Tourism in and After the Kovid-19 Crisis, chaired the meeting with the participation of the heads of relevant departments. Responsible and director of the capital-provincial tourism department through a video zoom system, a total of about 70 people.
Speaking at the meeting, Mr. Thong Rathsak confirmed that the overall situation of international tourists is gradually increasing, including that in the first six months of 2022, the situation of tourism in Europe and the United States has increased from 20 -25% and for the Asia-Pacific region increased by 1% due to the lack of Chinese tourism. Also, in July 2022, Cambodia received a significant increase in incoming flights.
He added that Cambodia now receives an overall increase in international tourists of nearly 150% compared to the same period in 2021.
Currently, all ASEAN member countries are prioritizing the implementation of the 2022-2023 Action Plan on the tourism situation, focusing on further boosting economic recovery, along with environmental and climate change considerations, and digitalization. And considering the design of an ecotourism community as a tourist attraction product.
In addition, Mr. Thong Rathsak reviewed the results achieved in the past and assessed that all relevant units have completed the work in accordance with the roadmap, achieving 80% by the first half of 2022. However, the Secretariat awaits additional reports from the private sector in the tourism sector to be included and supplemented in the team's achievements report.
The Director General requested the Secretariat of the three sub-working groups to play an additional role in coordinating with all relevant departments and units for their respective sub-working groups to explain and encourage those relevant departments and units to complete their activities in a timely manner. Time.
He also requested the Secretariat of the three sub-working groups to prepare a report and regular meeting for their respective sub-groups to collect the results from the relevant departments and units on a monthly or at least quarterly basis and to summarize and evaluate. Before submitting to the Secretariat of the working group of the Royal Government and the private sector for summary.
Heads of relevant units and departments must monitor their daily activities with high responsibility and request for clarification from the Secretariat immediately in case of any questions or perceived duties in any point of action to move forward.
These achievements will be jointly disseminated for the achievements of the Ministry of Tourism in the conference to be held on July 12-14, 2022.
