ACU Confirmation of Declaration of Assets and Liabilities for Commune / Sangkat Councilors of the 5th Mandate Confirmation of Declaration of Assets and Liabilities for Commune / Sangkat Councilors of the 5th Mandate
According to the Anti-Corruption Unit's answer:
(Article 18) The regime of declaration of assets and liabilities of the Anti-Corruption Law) The maximum period of 30 days after taking office is from the date of the Commune / Sangkat Council validation ceremony. Of no later than 30 days after taking office.
Second, new members of the Commune / Sangkat Council who have not previously received this position and have never had any other function required to declare assets and liabilities must implement the declaration of assets and liabilities within 30 days at the latest. From entering the position.
Third, the old members who are re-elected in this mandate do not need to declare their assets and liabilities within 30 days after taking office, and must declare their assets and liabilities under the 2-year regime. January 2023 for those who declared assets and liabilities in 2021 and in January 2024 for those who declared assets and liabilities in 2022.
Fourth, the Commune / Sangkat Councilors of the old mandate (4th) who did not stand for re-election, who did not resign and who did not have any remaining functions and liabilities, had to declare their assets and liabilities for the last time during the 30-year period. The day after the Commune / Sangkat Council validation ceremony.
