International Analysis: Fear of facing Putin is like Russia winning the war in Ukraine
WASHINGTON: The great struggle of the Ukrainian people against the Russian war, which the West calls an invasion, has been widely praised around the world. But it is not enough, and it should not be used to cover up the fact that the United States, NATO and the European Union are still afraid to confront Putin and do not have a "clear political objective". Ukraine will not be able to win.
In contrast to the West, Putin has always been clear about his political ambitions and objectives. For example, in a speech at a security conference in Munich, Germany, in 2007, the strongman showed the West his ambition to restore "Russia's great strength" and later took action in Georgia. In 2008, Crimea and Donbass in 2014, in Syria and now in the war in Ukraine.
But if Russia can recover its military economy and overcome Western sanctions in the Ukraine war, Moscow will not be afraid to go to war, and more importantly, the Ukrainian war will teach Putin a lesson. Keep in mind that NATO and the European Union will avoid confrontation with him. This is the real danger.
