KOICA and Sun Joon Yang University Medical Center provide training program for nurses in Korea to Preah Ang Duong Hospital
(Phnom Penh): The Korea International Cooperation Agency (KOICA) and Sun Joon-yang Medical University Center of the Republic of Korea have invited one more doctor and seven nurses from Ang Duong Hospital to continue their studies. In the Republic of Korea in the program "Invitation training program for nurses / nurses".
The training program is part of the "Capacity Building Project for the Ear, Nose and Throat (ENT) Center at Ang Duong Hospital." They will go for 14 days of training from July 10 to July 23, 2022, planning to leave Cambodia for the Republic of Korea on July 10, 2022.
The objectives of this training program are: First: Awareness of infection prevention and control, Second: Capacity building of the Department of Hospital Services Management / Outpatient Services and Nursing Care Management and Techniques / And 3: Improving specialized knowledge (operating room, supply room, etc.), management and nursing techniques / staff.
To facilitate this training program, KOICA Office in Cambodia provided a pre-departure orientation program for doctors and nurses on July 7, 2022.
The pre-departure orientation program is to facilitate the participation of Cambodian trainees, to introduce them to Korean culture and to make the most of their lives in the Republic of Korea. During the pre-departure orientation program, KOICA provided key topics on 1: Korea Information, 2: Course Information, and 3: Ethics on Integrity and Avoidance of Road Harassment. Gender for trainees and so on.
All participants who participated in the pre-departure orientation program expressed their gratitude to KOICA and Sunjunyang Medical University Center for their support and commitment. High will strive to study to enhance capacity building for a comprehensive understanding of training programs for nurses.
