(Battambang): A report from the Cambodian-Thai border in Battambang province confirmed that despite the recent crackdown on overweight trucks up to 80 tons driving on the national road by the mobile weighing team. According to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, on July 7, 2022, the Thai heavy vehicles will continue to enter Cambodia through the overweight corridor.
According to the report, the vehicles entered and exited through Lem or O'Rumduol ports in Phnom Preuk district, Battambang province, weighing 75 to 80 tons, and the vehicles refused to be transported through the international international border where the legal tonnage was set. No, they sneaked into the corridor without any inspection from the competent authorities.
He said that the operation to seize the overweight truck did not affect the purchase and sale of agricultural products of the people. The seizure of overweight trucks is limited to heavy overweight vehicles, and vehicles not overweight by law are not caught.
He said that there are groups of traders who do not exceed the weight limit by law, they can still do business normally without any hindrance. In particular, this is a group of traders collecting a small amount of corn, who refuse to change their behavior, respect the law and still want to continue to be overweight. Preventing overweight trucks is a necessity that can not be reversed, otherwise the road is still vulnerable.
