(Sihanoukville): In order to keep the city beautiful and hygienic as a tourist city, the Sihanoukville City Authority has issued guidelines for environmental sanitation, coastal hygiene, and told mobile vendors along the coast and streets to stop Set tables, chairs and cookers on the beach by July 7, 2022.
In Sihanoukville on July 6, Mr. I Sok Leng, Governor of Sihanoukville, said that "the promotion of mobile vendors along the coast has been long enough, starting from June 22 until "July 7, 2022 is observed that the people who are mobile vendors on the beach are involved in the cooperation of about 90 percent, but at night there is a significant increase."
However, according to Mr. Sok Leng, the administration of Sihanoukville will take administrative action on July 8, 2022, without allowing them to set up tents, tables, chairs and stoves, pots and pans for cooking. The beach is detrimental to the environment, the beauty of the city, the order of the beach, because the beach is a public beach for the public, tourists to visit freely.
