Foreign Minister Lan Chang-Mekong Continues to Strengthen Solidarity and Cooperation
(Phnom Penh): The 7th Ministerial Meeting of the Mekong-Lanchang Cooperation (MLC) expressed its continued commitment to strengthening solidarity and cooperation to better respond to common challenges. This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on July 7, 2022.
The 7th MLC Foreign Ministers' Meeting was held under the theme "Solidarity for Peace and Prosperity" and chaired by Wang Yi, State Councilor and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the People's Republic of China, and Wunna Minglwin, Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Republic of the Union of China. Myanmar, with the participation of the Foreign Ministers of Cambodia, Laos, Thailand and Vietnam.
The Ministers praised the MLC, which since its inception has supported more than 600 projects in areas such as water resources, agriculture, tourism, education, poverty reduction, health and women's empowerment, and praised The six countries that have worked hard to implement the project.
Finally, strengthen efforts to build the Mekong-Lanchang Economic Development Belt by cooperating with the new international land-sea trade corridor to reap the benefits of emerging trade and investment opportunities. From the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP).
