(Kampong Thom): The Royal Government's working group in Kampong Thom province has decided to set 15 key work directions for the second half of 2022 in order to successfully support the Royal Government in supporting, monitoring and monitoring the implementation of political programs and strategies. The fourth phase of the Royal Government in Kampong Thom province.
After the meeting reported and discussed and exchanged views, Mr. Thong Khon set out the main implementation direction in the second half of 2022 as follows:
First, continue to work to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid-19, especially to promote the third, fourth and fifth doses of the vaccine to all people.
Second, strictly implement the order of Samdech Techo Prime Minister to suppress and prevent encroachment on state land in the flooded forest area of Tonle Sap area in Kampong Thom province.
Fourth: Effective implementation of Sub-Decree No. 105 Dated 31 May 2022 on the revision of 6,385 hectares of land from 3 areas to 2 areas of Tonle Sap Lake area in Kampong Thom province and handed over to the people for possession and enjoyment.
Fifth: Effective implementation of Notification No. 437 Bottle dated June 10, 2022 on the definition of management areas and for practical use in protected areas and biodiversity corridors located in Kampong Thom province.
Sixth: Continue to inspect, measure, extract data and identify clearly and practically the land in area 3 in some target cities and districts to request to cut into two areas.
Seventh, continue to organize public forums at the municipal / district level to review and address the requests, challenges, concerns and suggestions of the people effectively and transparently. He advised the working group to conduct public forums to select the necessary topics in front to effectively organize and raise public awareness.
Eighth: Review and adjust the leadership structure of the Royal Government working group to visit some cities / districts. The chairman encouraged the members of the working group to work with the commune chief and village chief to help solve the work and accomplish the work at the village level.
Ninth: Continue to strengthen security, public order and social security through the implementation of safe village-commune policy. This is an important factor in maintaining security at the local level, which the Royal Government pays close attention to.
Eleventh, continue to strive to promote the provision of public services with a sense of responsibility, transparency and accountability to the people. He advised commune chiefs and commune clerks to work together to serve the people well.
Twelfth: Continue to examine and resolve the challenges, concerns and requests of the remaining number of people, including attention to resolving disputes and disputes outside the judiciary. He said that if the commune / village authorities or local authorities help solve a lot of problems for the people outside the court system, it will really help a lot of work for the people and the Royal Government.
13th: Continue to promote the issuance of a new model of Khmer nationality identity card to all people so that people have enough documents to participate in the upcoming 6th National Assembly election in 2023.
14th: Prepare to host the 7th River Festival in March 2023. In this ceremony, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Samdech Kattipritthbandit will be honored to preside.
Fifth, strive to eliminate inaction / shortcomings and do good deeds to increase the trust, confidence and warmth of the people on the Royal Government.
Nationwide blood demand in 2021 is almost 100,000 blocks, today Vital and students of the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia organize a new large-scale blood donation event after the failure of Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): OneFreternity (Vital) Co., Ltd. has re-organized a large-scale blood donation event after the reduction of Kovid 19 disease in collaboration with the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia and the National Blood Transfusion Center under the theme "Solidarity of "Heroes donate blood."
This program was held on the morning of July 7, 2022 in the conference hall of the NPIC Institute in order to inspire the volunteer movement to donate blood to contribute to the needs of blood storage for patients in need of blood in hospitals and As the number of blood donors decreases, so does the demand for blood.
The event was held in the presence of Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, General Director of OneFrighting (Vital), Mr. Muong Phasy, Deputy Director of the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia and represented by Dr. Bun Phearin, Director of NPIC, Dr. Sok Po, President of the National Blood Transfusion Center Leading civil servants-staff and students by receiving nearly 350 blood donation volunteers.
On behalf of the National Blood Transfusion Center, we would like to express our sincere gratitude for all the support for the humanitarian cause and call for continued support in all its forms in future campaigns.
Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy expressed her gratitude to the leaders and students of the National Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia for co-organizing this year's event and supporting Vital's activities.
She added that the program comes at a time when the local situation, the local community as well as the world is experiencing a recurrence of 19 cases of Kovid, and Vital and the NPIC have made informed decisions. Highly responsible for re-establishing the voluntary blood donation of leaders, civil servants, staff and philanthropists in the new normal trajectory.
It should be noted that Vital, which has a fund of 25R, has continued to maintain the basis of support in all activities and campaigns of voluntary blood donation from all institutions.
