Minister of Health shows positive in eliminating all kinds of malaria before the 2025 deadline
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, presided over a meeting to promote and prioritize Cambodia's sustainability in response to malaria at the Phnom Penh Hotel on July 7, 2022. Has shown positive in eliminating all types of malaria before the 2025 deadline.
Minister Mam Bunheng said, "We are committed to eradicating all forms of malaria before the 2025 deadline because we already know which areas are most at risk." So we will rush to that area to get rid of the pain faster. Currently, only 21 provinces face high risk of malaria: Kampong Speu and Stung Treng.
The Minister stated that Cambodia plans to eradicate all forms of malaria by 2025 under the direct initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
"We are now close to eradication, but the path for Cambodia to eradicate is not easy," he said. The challenge of resistance to antiretroviral drugs and the provision of services to communities and hard-to-reach communities remains.
In the face of these challenges, the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Bacteriology remains committed to doing its utmost to continue to work with our government partners, international community partners and civil society to build a successful eradication program. .
Today, under the guidance of Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, the National Center for Malaria Eradication (MEAF) has a detailed framework for malaria eradication and is supported by many partners throughout the network. The Royal Government, civil society and international organizations, most of which are present here.
He strongly hopes that continuing the efforts of high responsibility and full support, we will achieve the goal of eliminating malaria transmission by falciparum by 2023 and free of all malaria transmission in 2025. Svay Rieng authorities burn more than 21 kilograms of drugs on the occasion of the International Day Against Drug Abuse
(Svay Rieng): Six types of drugs weighing 21.32 kg were burned during the celebration of the International Day Against Drugs in Svay Rieng this morning, July 7, 2022 under the theme "Solve the drug problem. In the health and humanitarian crisis.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Chum Hat, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province and Chairman of the Provincial Drug Control Committee, and Lt. Gen. Thong Sokunthea, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs.
Mr. Men Vibol set some goals to improve the effectiveness of drug prevention and control in Svay Rieng, including:
* First, we must continue to pay more attention to the implementation of the Royal Government's order on the strengthening of anti-drug measures, safe village, commune policy, "S" village policy, drug-free commune. In particular, the implementation of the five measures of the campaign to fight illegal drugs very strictly.
* Second: To continue to promote education better, more active and active by continuing to strengthen and expand cooperation and movement for participation and support from all components of society to ensure that all target groups. Educate and better understand the law and its effects on drugs
* Fourth: All competent authorities must inspire the people as well as the owners of guesthouses, rental houses, hotels, karaoke, nightclubs and casinos, etc. When you know or have suspicions about drug trafficking, distribution or use, please be more active. More to provide information from criminals who intend to secretly try to produce, process and trade drugs in the province
* Fifth: The commanders of all types of armed forces must strictly enforce the law and pay attention to educating, guiding and managing the forces under their command as strictly as possible, absolutely avoiding "Do 4". Do not be involved, do not be behind the scenes, do not relax and do not intervene in drug cases.
