(Phnom Penh): On the morning of July 7, 2022, at the Office of Non-Banking Financial Services Authority, a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was signed between the Real Estate and Mortgage Regulators and the University of Economics and Finance for the purpose of establishing long-term relations and cooperation. In the long run, based on the common ground is to participate in the development of human resources in the real estate sector in Cambodia.
The MoU signing ceremony was chaired by Mr. Chou Vannak, Director General of Real Estate and Mortgage Business Regulator and Dr. Chuon Rattanak, Rector of the University of Economics and Finance, accompanied by management and colleagues, professors, students and representatives of real estate service providers. .
Dr. Rector said that the Memorandum of Understanding, the University has more opportunities to contribute to the strengthening and expansion of the real estate sector to contribute to the socio-economic development of Cambodia through the creation of more professional human resources in the real estate sector. Respond to current and future real work needs.
During the ceremony, the Director General of the Real Estate and Mortgage Business Regulator said that the benefits of the current MoU will provide an opportunity for both parties to work more closely together to enhance knowledge and organize training programs. Build and develop human resource capacity in the real estate sector to improve.
Through this Memorandum, the Real Estate and Mortgage Business Regulator has a role to play in strengthening the quality of training of the University of Economics and Finance on real estate-related skills through the function of supervising and recognizing the training program, professional certificates and study certificates issued by the University. Economics and Finance.
At the same time, the University must develop and update the training program as needed in accordance with the needs and changes of the labor market related to real estate in Cambodia.
