The training will provide official certification by the real estate regulator and mortgage to the trainees who have successfully completed the training. Comment: China is a leader in the fight against climate change
(Phnom Penh): Climate change is one of the world's major challenges threatening the health and well-being of humankind on the planet. Fighting climate change requires the joint efforts of all countries and regions.
As the largest developing country with a population of over 1.4 billion, China has a key role to play in the fight against global climate change. Many experts agree that if China does not succeed in reducing its carbon footprint, the world will not be able to win the war on climate change.
With a high degree of responsibility, China has adopted and implemented a number of policies, measures and actions to combat climate change and has been actively involved in global climate governance. The Chinese government considers environmental protection a top priority, with environmental protection integrated into all of the country's economic and social development plans.
So far, China's efforts to combat pollution have achieved remarkable success. At present, China has achieved remarkably better environmental conditions, especially air quality.
Overall, with strong economic power and strong and responsible technological capabilities, China has played a leading role in combating global climate change. China's success in combating climate change is a global success.
