(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on July 7, 2022, posted a message to celebrate the 14th anniversary of the inclusion of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site.
Samdech stated that today is the 14th anniversary of the registration of "Temple of Preah Vihear" as a World Heritage Site (July 7, 2008-July 7, 2022). The event, which took place on July 7, 2008, is considered a new historical event since Cambodia received this sacred temple after winning a case against Thailand at the International Court of Justice in The Hague on June 15, 2008. 1962
He added that the Temple of Preah Vihear, Cambodia's sacred temple on the Dangrek Mountains, was inscribed on the World Heritage List at the 32nd meeting of the UNESCO World Heritage Committee on July 7. July 2008 in Quebec City, Canada.
At the same time, Samdech appealed to the people to take care to protect all ancient temples throughout the country for the survival of all generations of Cambodians. This morning, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia held a press conference to present the results of the collection of tax on duty-free vehicles in the country under various license plates.
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia held a press conference on the morning of July 7, 2022 to present the results of tax collection work on existing tax-free vehicles in the country under various license plates.
The press conference was held at the headquarters of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia under the chairmanship of Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia.
Please be informed that the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to collect tax on existing duty-free cars in the country of refuge under various license plates from September 2021 and ending on June 30, 2022.
Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, told Fresh News on July 1, 2022 that by the deadline of June 30, 2022 Taxes on duty-free vehicles under various license plates, both steering and left-hand drive, earned more than $ 76 million from a total of 9,707 vehicles.
Of the total 4,490 right-hand drive vehicles that came to deposit, the right-hand steering wheel was changed from right to left and the deposit was converted into tax payment to the national budget, and another 2,09 right-hand drive vehicles were in the process. Adjust the steering wheel in various garages.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on July 6, 2022, agreed with the request of the people to allow the existing duty-free right-hand drive vehicles in the country to pay tax without having to change the steering wheel from right to left. The left.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the right to allow right-hand drive vehicles to pay without modifying the steering wheel is only for cars that are present in Cambodia until July 6, 2022, but new imported cars are not allowed to pay tax. Capture at once.
Of the above cases, 464 were imported and the rest were domestic cases.
