With the support of the Ministry of Interior, the program "Cambodia, my second home" will facilitate and attract foreign investors
(Phnom Penh): With the full support of the General Department of Immigration of the Ministry of Interior will make a good program "Cambodia, my second home" to facilitate and attract more foreign investors to invest in Cambodia. The program attracts foreign investors by helping them escape some of the rogue networks that run the immigration business, leading them to be deceived and distrustful of wanting to invest in Cambodia.
He said that with the trust and support of the members of the Khmer Family Foundation Association, the program "Cambodia, my second home" program, which is supported by the Ministry of Interior in accordance with the immigration law and policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Please be informed that in the 1990s, the Royal Government of Cambodia enacted immigration laws to attract foreign investment to Cambodia.
At that time, the plan was very successful and became a driving force for local economic development and increased Cambodia's GDP during 1994-2018 with surprising results. However, because the management system at that time was not yet detailed, many unscrupulous companies took the opportunity to cheat on immigration, causing many cases of immigration fraud at that time.
After much discussion and scrutiny, the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Interior, sees this as the most appropriate time to implement the first steps of the new immigration law. Therefore, the Ministry of Interior, through the General Department of Immigration, has decided to officially support the "Cambodia, My Second Home" program.
