Minister Thong Khon: In the first half of 2022, more than half a million international visitors came to Cambodia, and air transport also increased
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Tourism, Mr. Thong Khon, confirmed the situation of international tourists entering Cambodia in the first half of 2022 (January-June), in which more than half a million international tourists came to Cambodia or more than 500,000 Air and land transportation are also on the rise.
The minister said that about 5,000 to 5,600 international tourists come in a day. The main market sources of international tourists coming to Cambodia are from Thailand, Vietnam, China, USA, Indonesia, France, Korea, Malaysia, UK, Australia and so on.
At present, there are a total of 3,317 incoming flights, with 27 airlines, of which 10 are flying daily. Phnom Penh International Airport (PNH) has 2,864 flights, Siem Reap International Airport (REP) has 265 flights and Sihanoukville International Airport (KOS) has 198 flights.
It should be noted that after the Royal Government launched Visa on Arrivals and reduced the requirements on health, international tourists increased significantly compared to the same period in 2021, but still lower than the same period. Together in 2019 a lot. According to the Minister of Tourism, in the first 12 months of 2022, Cambodia may receive about 1 million international tourists or more.
