(Phnom Penh): On Wednesday morning, July 6, 2022, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, met with the ASEAN Para Games delegates and gave some advice before they left for the ASEAN Para Games or the ASEAN Para Games. The 11th in Solo, Indonesia.
The ASEAN Paralympic Games or ASEAN Para Games, a competition between disabled athletes among ASEAN member countries, is held regularly every two years. The competition has been held 10 times already. But in 2019, a match scheduled for the Philippines was missed due to the Kovid 19 crisis.
The 11th match was actually held in Vietnam, but Vietnam asked for a postponement due to the 19-year-old Kovid crisis to be held in Indonesia instead.
Yi Veasna, Secretary General of the National Paralympic Committee of Cambodia, said that in the 11th ASEAN Para Games, Cambodia sent a total of 166 sports delegates. There were 115 athletes and sports delegates, 39 coaches, assistant coaches, 7 technical officers and 5 national delegates.
Mr. Yi Veasna said that Cambodia sends athletes to compete in 11 sports, including table tennis, weightlifting, athletics, swimming, volleyball, men and women, basketball, the blind, 7-sided football, basketball, wheelchair men and women. Badminton and chess.
According to Mr. Yi Veasna, the delegation of the Cambodian Para Games will leave on July 24, 2022. In that, Samdech Techo Hun Sen assigned Mr. HUN Many as the leader of the delegation to participate in the competition in Indonesia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, pays great attention to sports and always gives the honor of meeting with the Cambodian sports delegation before going out to participate in various events. Through these meetings, the head of the Royal Government always provides guidance and advice to maintain the honor and dignity of Cambodia as well as sports delegates.
It should be noted that the National Paralympic Committee of Cambodia was established on October 25, 1997 with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as its chairman. The Paralympic Committee of Cambodia is a full member of the International Paralympic Committee (IPC), a full member of the Asian Paralympic Committee and a founding and full member of the ASEAN Paralympic Federation.
The National Paralympic Committee of Cambodia always participates in this Paralympic Games. In the 9th ASEAN Para Games in Malaysia, Cambodia won a total of 10 medals, 5 silver and 5 bronze.
